 a different amount <> +350 AOTEAROA f aS STOP FOSSIL FUELS = \u2014i \u2018BUILD 1OO%RE RENEWABLES >> ABLES.\u00bb 2,997 actions 20 far ANZ- DROP 3 needed to get to 2,000 DENNISTON oe monsterous mine proposal EMAIL ADDRESS\" -ontinuing to offer banking \u2018Services to Bathurst. With enough pressure, we can push ANZ to phase out banking Services With not only Bathurst, but all fossil fuel expansion companies. rv New Zealand : Others banks, such as BNZ, have committed to shutting down banking services to fossil fuel expansionists ~ lke Bathurst - by 2030.In2026,it's time fOr ANZ to dothe \u2014curwumstomes stnnverrns vou same. can unsubscribe at any time View the fullptition text. ABOUT359 \u00a9 We believe in a safe climate and a better future \u2014 a just, prosperous, and equitable world built with the power of engaged advocates. 360 is building a global grassroots climate movement that can hold our leaders accountable to the realities of science and the principles of justice. That movement is rising from the bottom up all over the world, and is uniting to create the solutions that will ensure a better future for all. Our online campaigns, grassroots organizing, and mass public actions bring together a global network active in over 188 countries. Here's how we get there: 1 Keep carbon in the ground. 2 Help build a new, more equitable low-carbon economy. 3 Pressure governments into limiting emissions. MORE + UBLIC HOUSIN 350 Aotearoa is building a grassroots movement to solve the climate crisis. Our online campaigns, grassroots organising, and public actions are led from the bottom up by ordinary people. \u2018Sign up to receive 350 Aotearoa updates! Millions of people are taking quick, simple actions for climate justice -be one of them. Would youlke to receive you about important campaign, stories, nd actions? BUILD A POWERFUL CLIMATE MOVEMENT IN AOTEAROA Contribute directly to cutting-edge campaigns to address the climate crisis. ON SOCIAL MEDIA media to stay up-to-date withthe lt (350 AOTEAROA ON INSTAGRAM f 350 AOTEAROA ON FACEBOOK \u20ac 350 Aotearoa is the New Zealand arm of the international climate a @\u00ae movement 350.0rg, which aims to unite the world around climate AOTEAROA change solutions. Our mission is to strengthen and grow climate NZ Charity Commission #0041367 action in communities across New Zealand. Privacy Policy | Terms of Service", "ocr_text_len": 2567}
{"_key": "350asia", "source_key": "350asia", "filename": "350_Asia.png", "image_file": "350_Asia.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.2398, "s008_neutral_headlines": 1.5527, "s010_scare_quotes": 1.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 0.0, "s085_standard_sections": 1.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 27.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00279, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.9192, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.0, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00078, "small_face_count": 2.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0501, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.1117, "content_column_count": "1", "side_margin_frac": 0.0, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0778, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "purple", "accent_color_count": 2.4829, "background_brightness": "offwhite", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0257, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 22.0, "footer_link_count": 117.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 1.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 5.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 4.333, "headline_size_variance": 0.2661, "page_text_density": "medium", "timestamp_count": 1.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0966, "number_token_frac": 0.0338, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.0, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.2398, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.1583, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.0, "lx_local_civic_per100": 1.9185}, "ocr_text": "4350 9 ssour RESOURCES GET INVOLVED yv # @ ( Donate RE-IMAGINE ASIA What if the world's biggest continent was powered by the sun, the wind, and the people? Draw the Line \u2018September we will come together to draw the line against injustice, pollution, and violence - and for a future built on peace, clean energy, and fairness. FOR LIFE, PLANET FOR PEOPLE, FOR THE From September 19 to 21, thousands of people across Asia rose up in streets and communities, by rivers and seas, and outside halls of power to deliver a message: We Draw the Line for Life, for People, for Planet. 350.0rg Asia and its partners held over 50 actions in 12 countries\u2014 from street marches to standing protests, art festivals to interfaith gatherings, fluvial parade to human chains. SEE THE ACTIONS ACROSS ASIA > People powering their lives with community- led renewables and other climate solutions \u2018Check out more inspiring global stories at \u2018our Hope Hub Reimagining Asia's Energy Future \u2018Speakers: \u2018+ Omkar Subedi | Research Fellow Digo Bikas Institute (Nepal) Erina Imai | Sun Sun Suita Community Power (Japan) \u2018Arbaatun | Women Leader of Gunung Sawur Microhydro Community (Indonesia) Sisilia Nurmala Dewi | Asia Director (Interim) - '350.0rg Asia (based in Indonesia) (Chuck Baclagon | Asia Finance Campaigner ~ 350.079 INDONESIA IRRIGATING LIVES. The community-run Kulon Progo Micro- Hydro Dam in Yogyakarta won over the hearts of farmers for providing affordable electricity while ensuring healthy water flows. More SWEET AND SUSTAINABLE. Powering sustainable agro- forestry, the Bunikasih Micro-Hydro Project boosts incomes and inspires the youth to remain as the forest's guardians. More PHILIPPINES RECHARGE TO STUDY. Engineering students from an energy- strapped university in the Philippines created a solar charging station as their contribution to the planet-and their right to education. More MOTHERS POWERING HOPE. A group of mothers in Quezon City pioneered a solar charging station, serving as a lifeline to an urban poor community when disasters hit. More NEPAL 1 WOMEN POWER. In an upland village, the Dhapsung Women\u2019s Group runs a solar micro-grid that generates clean energy used by homes, schools, mills, and irrigation systems. More FRIDAY, 17 JULY 2025, 4 PM PHT CE IMAGINE ASIA Asia stands at the crossroads of increasing climate vulnerability and an unprecedented opportunity to transition to renewable energy. At the heart of this shift are communities, where climate solutions are born, shaped by local wisdom and powered by collective action. Watch the webinar below and learn more about how we are reimagining Asia's energy future with concrete actions while the", "ocr_text_len": 2669}
{"_key": "350australia", "source_key": "350australia", "filename": "350_Australia.png", "image_file": "350_Australia.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 1.2821, "s008_neutral_headlines": -0.941, "s010_scare_quotes": 0.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 1.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 1.0, "s085_standard_sections": 6.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 16.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.04245, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.9118, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.0, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.0, "small_face_count": 0.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.063, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.1288, "content_column_count": "1", "side_margin_frac": 0.0, "header_band_height_frac": 0.1753, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 2.8125, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0561, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 47.0, "footer_link_count": 37.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 2.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 6.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 2.0, "headline_size_variance": 0.2433, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 0.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0314, "number_token_frac": 0.0277, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.5495, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.0, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 5.3114, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.0, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.3663}, "ocr_text": "35D eusrara asour- cawpaions aevenrs- QGBERED OUR WORK FOR CLIMATE JUSTICE We believe a better future is possible \u2014 one where Country, climate and communities flourish. Across this continent, communities are already living with the impacts of the climate crisis. But alongside the harm, there is strength, knowledge, power and determination to protect what we love and build a fairer future for everyone. We are growing a grassroots movement for climate justice led by those with the most at stake: First Nations communities, young people, and people on the frontline of fires, floods and rising seas. By organising together, we are transforming grief into healing and demanding urgent action that puts care and community at the heart of our political and economic systems. Join our movement To address the climate crisis, we need a movement more powerful than those who pollute our planet. Sign up here to learn more about the ways you can take action. Join a community of people across the continent imagining and organising together to create a better, world by keeping fossil fuels in the ground, securing a just transition and acting in solidarity for the protection and return of First Nations lands and island homes. Gas corporations are planning a huge expansion in Australia in the coming years, and to stop them we need a historic shift in the politics of fossil fuels. We have an opportunity to shift the politics of fossil fuel exports and achieve meaningful legislative change to keep fossil fuels in the ground. Read More + OUR ISLANDS OUR HOME Zenadth Kes (the Torres Strait Islands & surrounding seas) is home to Traditional Owners who have lived with a deep connection to land, sea, sky and culture for over 60,000 years. Right now, Torres Strait Islanders are onthe frontlines of the climate crisis and urgent action is needed to ensure they can remain on their homelands. Advancing seas are already threatening homes, as well as Our Islands Our Home is a campaign led by Torres Strait Islanders to protect their island homes. OUR MISSION Our vision is of a world where communities can thrive and we are all safe from the impacts of climate change. We are growing a grassroots movement to end fossil fuels and create community-led solutions to the climate crisis. Through education and action, a global grassroots \u2018movement can hold our leaders accountable to the realities of science and the principles of justice. The \u2018movement is rising from the ground up all over the world and is uniting to create the solutions that will create a better future for all. 350.0rg Australia is a not-for-profit project helping build this movement from our corner of the globe. Read More Together we can build our collective power to win campaigns Contribute directly to cutting-edge campaigns to address the climate crisis. On Social Media Follow 350 Australia on social media withthe latest new f 350 ON FACEBOOK (350 ON INSTAGRAM Join 350 Australia Keep up to date with the latest news & ways you can get involved. \u2018350.0rg Ltd (Australia) s a registered charity and registered as a company limited by guarantee. Authorised by Te Raukura O'Connell Rapira, 552 Victoria St North Melbourne, VIC, 3051, ABN: 46 138 156 192 Privacy Policy | Terms of Service |", "ocr_text_len": 3261}
