{"_key": "agriculturedive", "source_key": "agriculturedive", "filename": "AgricultureDive.png", "image_file": "AgricultureDive.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.1994, "s008_neutral_headlines": 1.6881, "s010_scare_quotes": 4.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 2.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 0.0, "s085_standard_sections": 5.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 17.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00513, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.4793, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.5114, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00067, "small_face_count": 2.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0506, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.3556, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.198, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0123, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "orange", "accent_color_count": 2.1387, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0136, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 81.0, "footer_link_count": 138.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 2.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 20.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 4.818, "headline_size_variance": 0.1724, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 5.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0371, "number_token_frac": 0.0431, "city_or_county_in_name": 1.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.1994, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.2393, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.4985, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0997, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0997, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.991, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.5982, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.8973, "lx_local_civic_per100": 1.6949}, "ocr_text": "Deep Dive G acricuttureoive : = Crops Meat Dairy Technology Sustainability Regulations Farming & Climate Supply Chain Operations Agriculture Dive will stop publishing on Feb. 1, 2025. We appreciate your readership and hope to provide you with valuable coverage from one of our other XX publications, Read more from our team, TOP STORIES Farmland loans for regenerative agriculture: FBN and Walton family launch \u2018first-of-its-kind\u2019 lending program \u2018cowMN 2. Agtech Seedlings: Bonsai Robotics secures $15M to advance automated fruit harvesters 3. Cargill, Foster Farms to close turkey plants as demand wanes 4, S questions about Trump's tariff plans Agriculture Dive to stop publishing On Feb. 1, 025, Agriculture Dive will stop publishing. We hope our 5. Meat giant JBS breaks into the egg business daily coverage of the agriculture space was helpful to you. Read more > THE LATEST Trump freeze on federal grants and loans sparks confusion in agriculture \u2018The Office of Management and Budget said aid to farmers won't be affected, but listed dozens of USDA programs to be reviewed for \u2018Marxist equity, transgenderism, and green new deal social engineering policies: Crops Zeldin is confirmed as the new EPA administrator. What's next? Agriculture groups welcomed the former New York representatives approach to deregulation and his support for extending year-round access to EIS @ Crops US detects rare bird flu strain HSN9 in poultry for first time The finding at a California duck farm is raising alarms among public health experts that bird flu could further mutate into \u201cunpredictable @ Meat Smithfield falls short of expectations in muted IPO \u2018The public offering came in at $522 million, altho producer had anticipated more than $900 million. the pork @ Moat Deere loses appeal against Agco in patent dispute over precision planting technology A federal court upheld a ruling that Agco's SpeedTube seed delivery system did not infringe upon Deere\u2019 intellectual property @ Technology Egg prices could break more records in 2025 \u2018The USDA is expecting consumer costs to rise another 20% this year as bird flu devastates commercial flocks. @ Meat Lend an ear: Corn-based material introduced for biodegradable packaging Corn Next believes it has cracked the corn code for more sustainable packaging and is eyeing a move to Ilinois to be closer to supplier ADM. Crops Investment in agtech startups plummeted in 2024 Deal activity fell during the year with a string of companies declaring bankruptcy, but Pitchbook analysts say a rebound could stil happen. Crops USDA slow to update food safety standards for meat and poultry, watchdog finds \u2018The US. Government Accountability Office recommended action on dormant pathogen standards and better collaboration within the USDAS outbreak investigation activities, @ Moat How new food traceability requirements will impact the grocery industry Retailers have less than a year to get their supply chains ready, yet challenges and confusion remain, Crops Trump's agriculture secretary nominee lays out \u2018day one\u2019 priorities for USDA Brooke Rollins presented her vision to \u201cmodernize\u201d the department and sided with the president on controversial issues like immigration and tariffs, @ Crops Agtech Seedlings: CH4 Global to expand methane-reducing cattle feed with Mitsubishi Also in this week's farm technology news: Deere & Co. will partner with six agtech startups in 2025, and Google makes two biochar carbon credit deals @ Technology Covenant pays poultry carrier another multimillion-dollar performance award \u2018The $100 million acquisition of Lew Thompson & Sons Trucking in 2023 included up to $30 million in earnouts. 6 Meat How a rare southern snowstorm could bring risks to farms Experts warn citrus and livestock farmers in states like Texas, Georgia and Alabama will need to take precautions to protect their operations. 4 Crops Why an independent grocer is holding the line on egg prices Connecticut supermarket chain LaBonne\u2019s Markets sees the ongoing egg shortage as an opportunity to demonstrate to shoppers that itis, focused on helping them afford groceries, CEO Bob LaBonne Jr. said. @ Meat Perdue Farms to shutter Tennessee chicken plant The company is set to close the Monterey facility at the end of March, climinating 433 jobs. 6 Meat Trump threatens 10% tariff on China \u2018The president said duties could go into effect Feb. 1, the same day as potential 259% tariffs on Mexico and Canada, Regulation USDA releases guidance on climate-smart crops in biofuels The interim rule gives insight into how farmers can access renewable fuel tax credits, though a Trump administration freeze on recent federal regulations is creating more uncertainty. Crops Smithfield Foods eyes $10.7B valuation in IPO \u2018The company said it plans to raise up to $939.6 million through its shareholder offering. @ Moat Cargill reaches $32M settlement in turkey price-fixing lawsuit \u2018Tyson Foods previously agreed to pay $4.62 million in the case, which accuses meatpackers of colluding to drive up consumer prices, @ Moat Trump says 25% tariffs on Mexico and Canada to take effect Feb. 1 \u2018The president on his first day of office also directed federal agencies to review trade pacts with China, Crops Foreign ownership of US farmland continues to rise, but Chinese holdings dip As renewable energy projects drive foreign land investments, acreage owned by China has declined 27% between 2022 and 2023, according to the USDAS latest report # Farming & Cimate Deere sued by FTC over farmers\u2019 right to repair equipment The tractor giant is accused of holding a monopoly over its repair services, forcing customers to pay more at dealerships to fix equipment. @ Technology coun Agtech seedlings: Amazon-backed Windfall Bio hits commercial milestone Get the free newsletter Subscribe to Agriculture Dive for top news, trends & analysis LIBRARY RESOURCES E]_ How To Adopt a Proactive Approach to Risk During Expansion \u00a9_ Boost Crop Yields and Cut Crop Losses with Visual AI for Precision Agriculture fp Tee Agriculture Dive Outlook on 2024 View all WHAT WE'RE READING \u00a9 v.00 \u2018Trump's California Water Order Does More for Farms Than Fires Black farmers\u2019 heirs challenge USDA payments at federal appeals court in Cincinnati (3 (2 THE ASSOCIATED PRE: A food bank netted a huge haul of 13,000 fresh salmon, The catch? The fish were still alive (% View all EVENTS: View all", "ocr_text_len": 6395}
