DONATE 7 \\ AMERICANS UNITED FOR SEPARATION OF CHURCH AND STATE Freedom Without Favor, Equality Without Exception The separation of church and state protects everyone's right to live as themselves and believe as they choose, as long as they don\u2019t harm others. For nearly 80 years, Americans United has defended church- state separation - a pillar of our democracy and the best way to ensure freedom without favor and equality without exception for all. Join the Movement SSS People across America are uniting to protect everyone's right to live as themselves and believe as they choose! FEDERAL WORKERS SUE TRUMP BECOME A YOUTH ORGANIZING FIGHT CHRISTIAN NATIONALISM ADMINISTRATION FELLOW WITH JONATHAN VAN NESS We protect religious freedom for Everyone For nearly 80 years Americans United has defended the separation of church and state against waves of white Christian Nationalism. We're organizing in every city, county and state because we know church-state separation is the cure for white Christian Nationalism and the foundation of \u2018our democracy. Fighting Christian Nationalism and Project 2025 Christian Nationalist billionaires and politicians are trying to destroy our democracy by|undermining}tti\u00e9 Separation of church and state. Not ort our Watch. ( LEARN MORE AND FIGHT BACK) iN ) Our Work on the most critical issues affecting your freedom and equality Defending Religious Minorities Protecting Public Schools Fighting Discrimination < Top 10 church-state separation questions answered Looking for real answers to your questions about the separation of church and state? Americans United has got you covered! Is America a Christian Nation? > Is the separation of church and state in the Constitution? > What did the Founding Fathers really say about church-state separation? & Is church-state separation anti-religion? Is America's government based on the Bible? Haven't we always had prayer in school? Why do we have \"In God We Trust\" on our money? Why is \"under God\" in the Pledge of Allegiance? Was George Washington an Evangelical Christian? What are famous quotes about church-state separation? Read the latest blogs from Americans United Stay current on the movement for religious freedom. Read updates on legal cases, advocacy efforts, and the people making a difference. ae Foundation to Freedom: Announcing the 2026 David Reflections from SRF 2026 Norr Youth Activist Award winner Why church-state separation still matters today Growing up between belief and belonging", "ocr_text_len": 2567}
