egister for Email Updates \u2018Search BOB \u2018SUPPORT US Login STAY INFORMED | PRESS | 2026 NPT Review Conference Sty: BY Libby Fiatoff and Daryl G. Kimball in Arms Control Today Arms Control TODAY Volume 56: June 2026 Arms Control =\"TODA' \u2018The Puzzle of Multi By Alexey Arbatov \u2018Saudi Arabia's Gilded Nuclear Swoethes By Sharon Squassoni 1 Arms Control Exports Assess NPT Review Conference News \u2018Trump Says US, Iran Close to Deal 2026 NPT Review Conference Stymied by Disputes \u2018Trump Claims to Discuss Arms Control in China Read more. Download the PDF Latest Analysis The U.S. War on Iran: New and Lingering Nuclear Risks USS. President Donald Trump continues to allege, without evidence, that Iran's nuclear program posed an imminent threat to the United States. The following are answers to frequently asked questions about Iran's proliferation risk and nuclear security issues, March 10, 2026 Did Iran's Nuclear and Missile Programs Pose an Imminent Threat? No. U.S. President Donald Trump and senior administration officials have offered conflicting justifications for the renewed U.S. strikes on Iran, including the claim that nt threat to the United Stat \u2018Therw is no evidence, however, to support those claims. Read ths issue brief for Is Trump Jeopardizing Nonproliferation Efforts to Get A Nuclear Cooperation Deal with Saudi Arabia? A Report To Congress Suggests He Is. When the Trump administration announced a joint declaration on U.S. nuclear jon with Saudi Arabia in Novernbor 2026, the White House claimed the F nuclear oF key questions about the nonpro has openly threatened to develop nut under the proposed agreement. February 19, 2026 \u2018weapons if Iran does\u2014will be subject to Resources Donate About Contact Us Email Updates fSnG The Puzzle of Multilateral Arms Control ACAis a small organization with a big impact. The financial support of individuals like you is key to sustaining its vital work. \"Today, we both need to work to prevent the breakdown moment when guardrails against nuclear catastrophe evaporate, and be prepared to seize the breakthrough moment, when we can advance again in the direction of the security of a world free of nuclear weapons.\" ACA Board Chair, Tom Countryman, June 2024 Be a part of the solution. Join today! Arms Control NOW Into the Final Week: Can the NPT States Come Together on a Final Document? \u2018Amb. Do Hung Viet, President of the 11th NPT Review Conference, circulated an updated Draft Outcome Document to states parties on the evening of May 13. Upon circulating the latest draft text, Viet told the assembled delegates that \u201cit represents our best chance for consensus,\u201d and he urged states to demonstrate flexibility, calling upon all delegations \u201cto bring forward concrete proposals on how to bridge remaining differences.\u201d \u2018May 16, 2026 Events & Remarks 12026 Arms Control Associ June 02, 2028 jon Annual Meeting Virtual Briefing: Multilateral Arms Control after New START: Involving China and Other Nucloar-Armed States March 26, 2028 ACA Joins 36 Organizations To Urge US to Stop Purchase of Cluster Munitions February 18, 2026, Join the Arms Control Association \u2018The Arms Control Association depends on the \u2018generous contributions of individuals who share \u2018Our goal of promoting public understanding of and support for effective arms control policies. ACA is \u2018a nonpartisan, nonprofit membership organization, \u2018and your financial support makes a difference. \u2018Your membership comes with a 12-month subscription to Arms Control Today. 1100 H Street NW, #520, Washington, DC 20005 Tel: (202) 463.8270 EIN: 23-7124588 PRIVACY | RESOURCES | ARMS CONTROL TODAY | BLOG | ABOUT | JOIN | DONATE", "ocr_text_len": 3822}
