{"_key": "automotivedive", "source_key": "automotivedive", "filename": "AutomotiveDive.png", "image_file": "AutomotiveDive.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.2008, "s008_neutral_headlines": 0.5719, "s010_scare_quotes": 1.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 0.0, "s085_standard_sections": 5.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 4.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00363, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.3068, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.0, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.0, "small_face_count": 0.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0507, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.4335, "content_column_count": "2", "side_margin_frac": 0.148, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0162, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 1.2427, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0019, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 44.0, "footer_link_count": 107.0, "cta_button_count": 3.0, "newsletter_box_count": 7.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 1.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 6.429, "headline_size_variance": 0.1207, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 3.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0488, "number_token_frac": 0.0173, "city_or_county_in_name": 1.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.3012, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.3012, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.3012, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.4096, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.1004, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.4016}, "ocr_text": "From Shopper Insight to Inventory Action \"=\" New Car Buyer Journey Insights Wh wannss70. veep dive opinion Library Pres Releases 10 Best Awards \u2018Automakers Dealers Operations Regulations Technology Vehicles Welcome to the new WardsAuto We have a new website as a result of our combination with Automotive Dive. Here's a reminder of our mission. \u2018Automotive Dive and WardsAuto's logos. The two publications combined in October. Courtesy of Aufomative D Editor's note: You may be reaching this page because you tried to reach a URL on Automotive Dive or WardsAuto that is no longer supported. WardsAuto and Automotive Dive combined in October 2025, resulting in a new website design. Unfortunately, that meant some legacy webpages had to be retired. Fear not: Our commitment to bringing you quality journalism remains unchanged. You can access our latest news coverage in our new home page at WardsAuto.com, sign up for our newsletters, and read up on why we merged publications here. Also, take a look at WardsAuto\u2019s mission statement below, which explains our approach to covering the automotive industry. Looking for a specific resource? Email a member of our team at wardsauto.editors@informatechtarget.com, and we'll get back to you as soon as possible. Welcome to the new WardsAuto. Our mission is to serve you. WardsAuto\u2019s core mission is to deliver incisive, timely and comprehensive coverage of the automotive industry. Today, we do so by providing an assortment of digital products that help automakers and dealers stay ahead of the curve, as well as awards programs that unpack the latest vehicle technology trends. For over a century, WardsAuto has been at the forefront of reporting on, analyzing, and interpreting the key trends in the automotive world, thereby illuminating paths for industry professionals. New Car Buyer Journey insights Founded on a commitment to deliver incisive, timely, and comprehensive coverage, WardsAuto has grown to become an indispensable resource for insights into new automotive technologies and emerging business strategies. From the rise of the internal- combustion engine to the advent of electric vehicles and autonomous driving, we've not just witnessed history; we've helped shape the narrative. \u2018The WardsAuto legacy is built on a bedrock of trust and expertise. Our team comprises seasoned journalists who live and breathe automotive. This passion is reflected in our coverage, which encompasses a broad spectrum of topics, including vehicle reviews, industry news, analysis and much more. At WardsAuto, we pride ourselves on being more than just a media site; we are a hub for the automotive community. Whether it's providing in- depth evaluations of the latest models, analyzing industry trends, or offering a platform for dialogue and discussion, our mission is to keep our readers informed, engaged and ahead of the curve. As we move into our second century, WardsAuto.com continues to evolve. Our commitment to excellence and innovation drives us to embrace new technologies and platforms, ensuring we remain the definitive voice in automotive journalism. Get in touch today! Email wards.auto.editors@informatechtarget.com and a member of our team will be in touch. RECOMMENDED READING WardsAuto and Automotive Dive Combine: New Site and Newsletter Coming Soon Bi Adduson Google Shore @ PURCHASE LICENSING RIGHTS Filed Under: Automakers. Dealers. Operations. Regulations. Suppliers. Technology. Vehicles WardsAuto news delivered to your inbox Get the free daily newsletter read by industry experts COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS View all | Post a press release From \u2018Shopper sao Insight to hetion New Car Buyer Ea Journey Insights Get the free newsletter Subscribe to WardsAuto for top news, trends & analysis MOST POPULAR Range Rover SV Ultra promises stellar sound and elevated luxury Scaling up: What dealers should know about Stellantis\u2019 big product revamp Sedan finds your electric comfort zone UAW strike at Michigan supplier to GM seeks amends for 2008 ENN) 2026 Lexus ES review: ow LIBRARY RESOURCES Puava0oK [E]_ Advance your supply chain durability with regionalization WEBINAR - ON DEMAND \u00a9) How virtual twins drive