 new rules for a Community Justice Worker Program that would allow certified lay advocates limited practice in some courts. Details about how to participate are available online. The Montana Bar Association provides context about professional standards within Montana's legal community. Business GOVERNMENT GOVERNMENT Fourteen Montana softbal sianforte and DEQ seek to Bozeman releases weekly players carn All-America intervene in large new load tariff community development Scholar-Athlete honors case notice and project update More News wie: ay Fad fcormerot I { Governor Gianforte honors veterans in Billings and Miles City Governor Greg Gianforte honored local veterans during stops on his statewide tour this week. The governor presented \u2018commendations to two decorated servicemembers at ceremonies in Billings before addressing attendees at an annual VW. convention in Miles City. NON-PROFIT Montana State doctoral student receives NIH grant for gut robiome and arsenic research \u201cTrenton Wolfe at Montana State University has been awarded an NIM fellowship supporting his study on antibiotics\u2019 impact on gut bacteria involved in detoxifying arsenic. His work connects. June 19,2026 Montana State filmmaker Trent Pietsch receives regional w award for experimental film \u2018Trent Pietsch earned regional recognition for his experimental film while studying filmmaking at \u2018Montana State University His award-winning project explores creative struggles through. ing June 18,2026 Great Falls siblings sentenced to prison for stealing and cashing neighbor's checks \u201cTwo siblings from Great Falls have been sentenced to consecutive prison terms after pleading aulty to stealing their neighbor's checks following a medical emergency absence from home. The. June 18, 2026 \u2018GOVERNMENT Billings man sentenced to 10 years for firing handgun after attempted robbery Billings man received a ten-year prison sentence for firing shots after an attempted robbery at alocal conven