 from the past two decades of struggle? Harsha Walia ARTS IN SOCIETY The Reality Drive Ashort story. Emmett Rensin ARTS IN SOCIETY Art Thieves Watching Kelly Reichardt\u2019s films in the age of Anthropic. Jacob Rubin poLitics Sovereignty\u2019s End and Beginning In Somaliland, the pursuit of statehood has come with a bitter irony. Farah Bakaari POLITICS, SCIENCE Artificial Reason conversation on Al, rationality, and violence. Kevin T. Baker, Sophia Goodfriend, Benjamin Recht, Lily Hu BOSTON REVIEW FOREVER | WARS ARTS IN SOCIETY The Machines Get in the Way The work of art\u2014and the work of making art \u2014in an age increasingly hostile to it. Luke Dunne Pouitics Dispatches from the Forever \u2018Wars A special section in our Spring 2026 issue, with writing from Iran, Lebanon, Iraq, and. the West Bank Pouitics How Not to Defeat Authoritarianism Moderation used to help Demoorats win, but its advantages now have been greatly exaggerated, \u2018Adam Bonica, Jake Grumbach with responses from Cori Bush, Amanda Litman, Matthew Yolesias, G. Elliott Mortis, Julia Serano, Eric Rauchway, Suzanne Mettler & Trevor E. Brown, \u2018Thomas Ferguson, Timothy Shenk, Jared Abbott & Milan Loewer, Jenifer Fernandez Ancona, Lily Geismer, Danielle Wiggins, William A. Galston, Henry Burke BOSTON REVIEW The olite delusions fueling the violonce of the present. Featuring 2 roundtable on Iran & dispatches from Beirut, Baghdad, and Ramallah Plus Olif$mi 0. Tatwd on ipunity, David \u2018Waldstreleher on America at 250, Harsha \u2018Walia on how not to abolish ICE, and FOREVER | WARS ending CURRENT ISSUE From the Editors: Forever Wars Introducing our Spring 2026 issue. Boston Review ine Pouitics The Real Border Crisis The problem isn\u2019t immigration. It\u2019s the failure of liberal democracy itself. Lea Ypi with responses from Paulina Ochoa Espejo, T. Alexander Aleinikoff, Dara Lind, Daniel Denvir, Chandran Kukathas, Ayelet \u2018Shachar pouitics \u2018The War on Gaza Has Not Ended A hundred days after Trump's Board of Peace was ratified, nothing has improved hore. Asem Alnabih , at N Signup forour WY carr AA A :. *ALIFOR} iT NIA au AION YONAL GUARD PoLitics The Responsibility of Intellectuals in the Age of Fascism and Genocide Speaking the truth and exposing lies is not enough, Robin D. G. Kelley with responses from David Waldstreicher, Jennifer Zacharia, Martin O'Neill The War on Iran: A Conversation A roundtable on the consequences of U.S. and Israeli aggression, reactions from Iran and the Iranian diaspora, and the future of Iranian struggles for freedom and democracy. Peyman Jafari, Ali Kadivar, Manijeh Moradian, Naghmeh Sohrabi, Alex Shams Iran After Khamenei An interview with sociologist Asef Bayat on the U.S.-Israeli war, democratic opposition to the Islamic Republic, and the country\u2019s uncertain future. Asef Bayat, Alex Shams War on Iran and the Folly of Regime Change Essential reading from the BR archive. Boston Review \u201cTo live forever, to be truly good, and to know\u2014to really know-\u2014the truth. Whole lives\u2014whole generations! \u2014have been wasted in the pursuit of these impossibilities.\u201d \u2014\"The Reality Drive,\" a short story by Emmett Rensin r ~~ os FROM THE ARCHIVE ARTS IN SOCIETY \u201cRe al", "ocr_text_len": 3376}
