{"_key": "cstoredive", "source_key": "cstoredive", "filename": "C-StoreDive.png", "image_file": "C-StoreDive.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.1003, "s008_neutral_headlines": 1.441, "s010_scare_quotes": 3.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 1.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 0.0, "s085_standard_sections": 6.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 13.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.0014, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.3805, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.7742, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00051, "small_face_count": 1.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0536, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.3608, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.162, "header_band_height_frac": 0.012, "logo_centered": 0.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 2.2192, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0079, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 45.0, "footer_link_count": 119.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 2.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 13.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 4.867, "headline_size_variance": 0.1767, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 1.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0373, "number_token_frac": 0.0333, "city_or_county_in_name": 1.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.1003, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.1805, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.1003, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 3.1093, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.5015, "lx_local_civic_per100": 1.3039}, "ocr_text": "@ cstorepive How 5 super regional c-store chains 5. Deep Dive Opinion Library Events Press Releases Foodservico M&A Fuels Operations Category Trends TOP STORIES energy drinks are reshaping the competitive landscape Companies like Wawa, QuikTrip and Sheetz are pushing aggressively into new states and challenging incumbent players both small and large. Read more > THE LATEST [oF Stinker Stores overhauls C-suite following CEO\u2019s departure Chair and owner Nancy Jones is now CEO, and the retailer has also appointed a new chief operating officer, chief technology officer and chief experience officer. Operations 7-Eleven fully integrates 204 Stripes stores \u2018The locations, which the retailer bought in 2024 for $1 billion, now have 7-Eleven\u2019s loyalty and technology platforms, and received renovations and upgraded foodservice and fuel offerings. Operations coun 3 Big Numbers: Cumberland Farms spotlights progress on major initiatives \u2018The recently renamed retailer shared updates on its financial situation, its revamped loyalty program and three pending M&A @ Operations Cumberland Farms taps Murphy USA tech chief as new CIO Michael Verdesca has held technology-focused leadership positions across convenience retail and restaurants for the past two decades. Operations How smarter data and free ice cream supercharged Coen Markets\u2019 loyalty program After getting more insight into customer behaviors and habits, the company has seen penetration rates at some sites that are well above the industry average. @ Technology Buc-ee\u2019s allegedly treated worker with a disability with \u2018reckless indifference\u2019 \u201cInflexible thinking\u201d can cause employers to run afoul of reasonable accommodation requirements, an acting regional attorney for the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission said. @ Labor Prepared food surge in c-stores brings packaging innovations As convenience stores offer more fresh food, their packaging needs shift. Packaging companies are exploring forms that maintain food quality, offer versatility and minimize storage space. Operations What 6 fuel and convenience leaders are saying about the Iran war Executives from BP, Sunoco, Murphy USA and more shared their \u2018thoughts on the impact of oil supply disruption and how it will affect the rest ofthe year. Fuels Stinker Stores CEO is stepping down Nate Brazier, who assumed leadership of the retailer in 2024, said he is taking time to focus on his family \u201cand reflect on whats next. Operations Stewart's allocates $55M for c-store growth through 2026 \u2018The retailer is building new stores in several areas of New York and remodeling at least 15 older and smaller sites to feature enhanced food and beverage offerings. Operations Former Seven & i CEO dies at 93 \u2018Toshifumi Suzuki, who had been serving as an honorary advisor of the company, passed away on May 18 from heart failure, the company announced, Operations BP ousts board chair, citing misconduct Albert Manifold has been removed following \u201cserious concerns raised to the Board related to important governance standards, oversight and conduct,\u201d BP said Operations Mirabito acquires 9 Quicklee\u2019s c-stores All ofthe locations are in Western New York, with four in Rochester and one each in Fairport, Hamlin, Batavia, Lyons and Dalton. o Maa CrossAmerica sells 16 c-stores for nearly $13M With its latest sale, the retailer is continuing the real estate rationalization efforts that it launched over a year ago. oman Campbell Oil makes 2nd fuels acquisition this year \u2018The parent company of Minuteman Food Mart acquired the assets of John's Fuel Service, expanding its dealer division, tank wagon fuel operations and jobber network. o Maa 3 Big Numbers: The c-store payments problem A surprising number of estore operators have multiple payment systems across their stores. A recent survey from Vontier delved deeper into the pros and cons of that approach. @ Technology 7-Eleven\u2019s turbulent 2026: IPO delays, layoffs and a bigger food push After its parent company fended off a takeover bid and saw its CEO depart last year, the North American chain has made a series of moves to-cut costs and rebound the business. Operations Global Partners taps Starbucks vet to lead retail operations Operations Kwik Trip doubles down on gamification @ Technology 7-Eleven hit by data breach The retailer confirmed that an unauthorized third party gained access to certain systems used to store franchisee documents earlier this spring. Atleast 50 people have been impacted @ Technology Couche-Tard\u2019s head of data and AI resigns Iris Singhania leaves the key tech role shetd held since January 2028. Its not clear who will be taking over her duties. @ Technology Private-equity-backed firm makes fuels- focused M&A push Continental Fuel Group aims to acquire fuel distributors in the bulk, on-site, mobile and wholesale delivery sectors, which are seeing consolidation, Maa Fueling Up: Breaking down 7-Eleven\u2019s competing growth strategies retailer is ramping up franchising and wholesale conversions while still focusing on foodservice goals. Technology Labor 1. Yesway moving into Arizona 2. Sunoco acquires wholesale assets in Texas 3. SNAP waivers could lead to $830M sales loss for soda, candy, 4, CEO departures lead May exec changes Dolly Parton's travel center to open in late June Get the free newsletter Subscribe to C-Store Dive for top news, trends & analysis MOST POPULAR How 5 super regional c~ store chains are reshaping the competitive landscape Gan. \u2014 Dolly Parton's travel center to open in late June = Sunoco acquires wholesale assets in Texas Yesway moving into Arizona LIBRARY RESOURCES \u00a9) Winning in a Confusing Economy: Getting Faster, Better Retail Insights with Consumer Transaction Data InFocRapHic \u00a9] How To Build a Connected, Compliant Retail Network WEBINAR - ON DEMAND \u00a9 _ Bridging the Execution Gap from HQ to Store Floor COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS ZeroToOne.Al Deploys its Large Behavioral Model at Advertising Scale \u2018Through GroundTruth, Laun. Kwik Trip Selects Eagle Eye to Deliver Al-Powered Personalized Loyalty Across U.S. Convenience... all | Post a press release WHAT WE'RE READING \u00a9 Nacs Circle K Rolls Out Butterfinger Exclusives Ct A Korean-style convenience store is opening in downtown Durham (% Gy ResTAURANT OVE The restaurant industry's real crisis isn\u2019t food costs \u2014 it\u2019s access to financing (1 VIRTUAL EVENT | NOON ET How the payments landscape is evolving in retail View all | Promote an event", "ocr_text_len": 6452}
