{"_key": "cxdive", "source_key": "cxdive", "filename": "CX_Dive.png", "image_file": "CX_Dive.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.1038, "s008_neutral_headlines": 1.5503, "s010_scare_quotes": 5.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 1.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 0.0, "s085_standard_sections": 4.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 15.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00278, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.4486, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.7522, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.0009, "small_face_count": 2.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0561, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.3383, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.148, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0048, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 2.0825, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0164, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 56.0, "footer_link_count": 119.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 2.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 19.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 4.933, "headline_size_variance": 0.7438, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 1.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0597, "number_token_frac": 0.0199, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.0, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.2285, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.1038, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 3.946, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.2077, "lx_local_civic_per100": 1.2461}, "ocr_text": "Bridge the gap between strategy and execution { necssow J & cxoive Q A ATLASSIAN Deep Dive Library Events Press Releases Strategy Al& Automation Technology Loyalty Data & Analytics Customer Service Personalization TOP STORIES 1. McDonald's to invest in CX tools, worker support for growth plan 2. Victoria's Secret rides cohesive brand experiences to strong sales growth 3. Regulars keep restaurants afloat as overall experience keeps diners coming back 4. Dick's launches AI adviser to go beyond shopping advice Half of current customer service jobs will be lost to AI by 2030, Forrester predicts \u201cThere are humans today doing jobs that don't require the level of Costco\u2019s digital personalization effort drives $500M in digital sales intelligence that a human has,\u201d going to go away.\u201d Read more > THE LATEST Forrester\u2019s Max Ball said. \u201cThat work is The FCC wants to onshore contact centers: How 7 organizations respond # Customer Service Kohl's CX changes score minor wins, but the business remains challenged Improvements to digital friction and in-store consistency helped the retailer narrow its comparable sales loss, but sales growth is elusive, @ Strategy Consumers feel the economic squeeze, pull back on spending Write-in survey responses from consumers this month leaned toward pessimism, with two-thirds of consumers cutting back on spending, the Conference Board said @ Strategy How Target is putting CX front and center \u2018The retailer wants to revive its store experience by focusing on the store basics, from employee engagement to carts and bathrooms. @ Strategy Bridge the gap between strategy and execution AATLASSIAN Chipotle supercharges its rewards relaunch with \u2018Summer of Extras\u2019 Curt Garner, chief strategy and technology officer at the chain, explains how a \u201cSummer of Extras\u201d effort builds on and gamifies its rewards program, @ Loyalty Best Buy's incoming CEO sees customer experience as core to its evolution # Strategy Target's latest CX strategy: evaluating employees on customer engagement \u2018Target provided guest experience training to more than 300,000 associates focused on four performance factors: interaction, execution, teamwork and reliability 1 Customer Service Dick\u2019s continues to reap the gains from its experiential stores Customers continue to spend more time and money at House of Sport locations, and stores are still driving comparable sales growth years after opening, CEO Lauren Hobart said @ Strategy Bridge the gap between strategy and execution A ATLASSIAN Wingstop launches loyalty program Club Wingstop's exclusive perks and experiences could help improve guest frequency and same-store sales growth, @ Loyalty How major retailers are investing in their associates to better serve customers Lowe's is reporting success putting AI companions in the hands of employees, while Walmart and Home Depot are betting specialized positions will better meet customers needs. @ Strategy Why three-quarters of enterprises have rolled back Al agents Organizations with mature governance frameworks are even more likely to roll back customer-facing Al agents, a Sinch survey found, @ AL& Automation Kwik Trip doubles down on gamification \u2018The Midwestern re ris partnering with Eagle Eye to add AF powered individualized \u201cchallenges,\u201d which are more targeted than typical discounts. @ Loyalty What CX leaders need to know about customer journey mapping @ Strategy Nearly all hoteliers use AI, but some experiences should be human-led: Mews As more hoteliers embrace artificial intelligence, re as their next priority, ahead of efficiency or cost reduction, per a new survey is emerging @ AL& Automation Inside Starbucks\u2019 atmospheric and experiential renovations Ata remodeled Chicago cafe, the proportion of on-premise trafic has doubled as consumers enjoy couches, comfy seating, outlets and warm lighting, @ Strategy Intuit customers spending more as it improves experiences across brands \u2018The company is tapping into a \u201cflywheel effect\u201d with its customers and has seen higher revenue per users with customers using multiple products, CEO Sasan Goodarzi said @ AL& Automation Walmart paid loyalty shines as membership revenue grows double-digits \u2018The growing subscription-based recurring revenue stream insulates the retailer from \u201csome of the winds in the economy,\u201d CFO John David Rainey said. @ Loyalty Lowe's courts DIY shoppers as AI tools boost online conversions \u2018The retailer is aiming to build relationships with its DIY customers through Al-enhanced omnichannel shopping, associate-led services and loyalty program options. @ AL& Automation What customers consider when using AI to shop \u2018The vast majority of consumers say it's important to recognize the seller or merchant and check customer reviews before purchasing, a PSE Consulting survey found. @ 18 Automation Target\u2019s CX investments lead to 3-year highs in store metrics \u2018The retailer's first quarter results beat expectations, but there is more to be done before Target has \u201cthe most delightful shopping experience in retail,\u201d CEO Michael Fiddelke said, @ Strategy Applebee's offers free delivery to Wyndham Rewards members @ Loyalty Bridge the gap between strategy and execution AATLASSIAN Get the free newsletter Subscribe to CX Dive for top news, trends & analysis MOST POPULAR Costco\u2019s digital personalization effort drives $500M in digital sales Why three-quarters of enterprises have rolled back AI agents The FCC wants to onshore contact centers: How 7 organizations respond Dick\u2019s launches AI adviser to go beyond shopping advice Fea wi LIBRARY RESOURCES e How AI Is Reshaping the Enterprise EE] How cx Leaders Rebuild Customer Confidence \u00a9) _ How Utilities are Modernizing the Last Mile of CX View all COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS Stackable Labs Launches First AI Experience Layer for Customer Service Messaging View all | Post a press release WHAT WE'RE READING Onourrer How Small Language Models could have big CX impact (3 Amazon offers Al agent tech to other retailers (2 ETPLACE 10 banking customer experience strategies for 2026 % EVENTS 04 atin rentaon? viding Common Pain Points Global Brands Face While Scaling at Speed 09 CX Insights > Action Webinar Series: How CX teams can close the customer expectation gap. View all | Promote an event INDUSTRY INTEL Redesigning the Service Role for the AI Agent Era featuring ASAPP and Forrester Bridge the gap between strategy and execution A ATLASSIAN", "ocr_text_len": 6410}
