save money. It will leave billions behind \u2018Building Canada Strong\u2019 needs sectoral bargaining and standards Who will defend the public university? Media academics to blame in part for our news mess It is becoming clear where workers are placed in the Team Canada Strong framework. Labour is treated as \u201chuman capital\u201d: workers are inputs to production, future workers are \u201cinvestments,\u201d and their value is, \u2018measured by the economic returns they generate and the labour market demand for their work. Worker rights are largely absent from the narrative. INTRODUCING THE CD ARCHIVE Canadian Dimension teamed up with the University of Manitoba Archives and Special Collections department to create this digital register of CD's past issues, going all the way back to our 1963 inaugural edition. LEARN MOR SUPPORT CD TODAY More than 75% of our operating budget comes to us in the form of donations from our readers. These donations help to pay our bills, and honorariums for some of our writers, photographers and graphic artists. Our supporters are part of everything we do. NEVER MISS A STORY Sign up for our email newsletter and get our news and analysis delivered on the regular. DONATE NOW OUR COLUMNISTS LAURENCE BRAUN- MARC EDGE JOHN CLARKE KEN THEOBALD NOLS Media academics to Where the truth lies Inside Toronto's growing What Canadian cities can _ blame in part for our news \\ c tenant revolt lear from Zohran mess Mamdani\u2019s housing plan BROWSE ALL COLUMNISTS UNIFOR Aunion for ever RECENT STORIES LATEST CARTOON The \u2018we\u2019 of anti-Zionism Where the truth lies Inside Toronto's growing tenant revolt To GAME A NATION \u201cTo Game a Nation\u2019, by Evin Coll. True lies across the water Hiner Me 4 POPULAR STORIES Who will defend the public university? Cutting CRA experts won't save money, It will Alberta separatists think their referendum pitch is about democracy. It\u2019s leave billions behind Media academics to blame in part for our news