are, financial instability and mental health are being replaced with uniformed service members. bby Marcus Bram Join Our Community of Fact-Based News Readers \u2018Sign up for our newsletter for exclusive investigative series, live events, and special stores. Feds to Open Tens of Thousands of Acres of Colorado Wilderness to Oil Drilling Top Democratic Candidates Agree on Housing Urgency, Not the Fix California Moves to Ban Quartz Countertop Fabrication to Combat Silicosis Epidemic Inthe governor's race, Steyer backs enforcement. Wildlife habitat, endangered animals and recreation could all be at risk in state's biggest public land sale in modern history. \u2018The incurable lung disease has killed 51 countertop workers and sickened 560, numbers that are expected to keep climbing while regulators draft emergency rules. Contitions at California ICE Detention Centers Are Getting Worse, Inspections Find A state Department of Justice inspection of seven California facilities found overcrowding, poor medical care, inadequate food and excessive force from guards. Where California's Gubernatorial In California Governor's Race, Xavier Candidates Stand on Climate and Becerra Walks Away From Single- Taking Big Oil Money Payer While fr ers Steyer and Becerra dvocate for a universal slug it out, they're clashing over their \u2018now focuses on incremental commitment to clean energy and shielding Californians from Capital With Promises of Money, Controversial Ga Navajo Nation Passes First Hurdle Pipeline would cross 234 miles of tribal land in New Mexico and / hearing schedule catches community group off gu The Arc The Arc examines the persistent barriers to racial justice and opportunities for progress in an era of receding black presence in Los Angeles and California \u2018Nike Isn't Playing Trump's Anti-DEI Game. What Will That Cost? 1s There Stil Hope fr Racial Justice When Authoritarians Rule by Conspiracy Theory? DONATE More From Capital & Main SUPPORT REAL JOURNALISM DONAT