Stay up to date. \u201ci A DIFFERENT APPROACH Where traditional intemational security institutions just see a collection of states, we see an interconnected set of systems. We focus on the underlying threats to global security: the illicit networks that operate across borders to destabilize communities, prevent development, and devastate the environment. DATA & TECH INNOVATION We conduct data-driven, tech-powered investigations into the networks harming our world. Our cutting-edge data and technology capabilities allow us to harness the power of Publicly Available Information to map out entire transnational illicit systems \u2014 and identify precisely how to target them. GLOBAL IMPACT NETWORK Innovation only goes so far without collaboration. Our global network of action-focused partners takes us from analysis to systemic impact. By building trusted partnerships with public, private, and civil society stakeholders, we work to cteate unified responses to illicit networks and ultimately undermine the motivating forces behind them. Featured News BIC Investigation Reveals $1.2 Billion Belarusian Weapons Supply Network C4ADS pariner the Belarusian Investigative Center (BIC) finds 58 Belarusian enterprises supplied Russian arms REPORT manufacturers with over $1.2 billon In goods since. Hardwired Repression expanave mats survellance syslem Inthe Uyghur regon, AWuietly processing blomettc and behavioral data. News Sudan's Armed Conflict Enters Its Fourth Year \u2018As armed conflict in Sudan enters its fourth year, C4ADS remains commited to supporting our Sudanese partners \u2018across elvl society working towards. event China\u2019s Greyzone Fleet: Detecting and Disrupting Beijing's Strategy in the Indo-Pacific On March 26, 2026, the Australian Strategic Policy * = Inatue (ASP) and C4ADS convened a puble pane! discussion on how China s deploying submisions @ colologued in = Pe) UN \u2014 AP Gateway higgers \u2018@ Lambda Function News C4ADS Releases 2025 Annual Report TECH BULLETIN (On March 17, 2026, C4ADS published is 2025 annual WhatsApp Bots impact report. \u2018Our second Data in Motion article details how C4ADS bulla WhatsApp-based evidence submission tool for NGO partners in Sudan to document. COMMENTARY Anchors Away In this commentary, we examine how beneficial owners across the fishing, cargo, and tanker Industries exploit shell companies and open flag registies. Cyber Chase event Following the release of ou Deceptive by Design sve 1SSUE BRIEF bret CAADS hosted a webinar on March 10,202, to Deceptive by Design dramatically scale thelr operations. An opaque View ALL Our Tools A Horizons Sanctions Explorer Triton Wildlife Seizure Dashboard At C4ADS, we strive fo create measurable impacts on the world around us We are hiring! Join OUr tEGIM. \u2014 irourmisionto detect tict networks in that work, out team s constonty Pushing the boundaries of what has been done before and what is possible. RcoanecscereertPs News vewan 5/97/2026 NEWS 4/15/2626 NEWS 3/17/2026 NEWS BIC Investigation Reveals $1.2 Billion Sudan's Armed Conflict Enters Its C4ADS Releases 2025 Annual Report Belarusian Weapons Supply Network Fourth Year", "ocr_text_len": 3270}
