nd pseudoscience. Founded and inspired by great minds, such as Carl Sagan, Isaac Asimov, James Randi, Paul Kurtz, and Richard Dawkins, CFI advocates for science, secularism, and critical thinking worldwide. Center for Inquiry Headquarters | \u2018About CFI Take Action Donate Stay Updated Learn More About CFI Make a difference Today ~~ Sign up for important email updates How We Make Our Impact The Center for Inquiry's core mission is defending reason, science, and secular values. Here is how we carry out our vision. ns 2 ah) SECULAR A Ld RESCUE ScjenceSaves CRARLTUSE \u00ae TRUTH eMHOPE P's0/ _ Secular Rescue Secular Rescue provides emergency assistance to writers, bloggers, publishers, and activists who face threats due to their beliefs or expressions regarding religion. ScienceSaves ScienceSaves promotes science appreciation by highlighting the many ways science has greatly Teacher Institute for Evolutionary Science \u2018TIES glves middle school teachers the tools they need to effectively teach evolution and answer its critics based on new Next Generation Science improved the lives of everyone. Standards. \u2018Teachers, spread the word! Right now you can earn graduate credit or certificate for each January online course through Adams State University, featuring expert content and classroom-ready resources. Latest In Skepticism The Chroniclers of Curiosity Feature Article Organizing Doubt: Before CSICOP Had a Name Massimo Polidoro Editor's note: This isthe second in a series of columns from Massimo Polidoro as he recounts stories from the history of the modern skeptical movement and the Committee for the Scientific Investigation of Claims of the Paranormal (CSICOP). Before CSICOP had a name, a mission, or a public face, it already had a problem... Continue Reading in Skeptical Inquirer Latest In Secularism Determinism, Free Will, and Moral Responsibility Feature Article The Modular-with-Feedback Theory of Free Will: Challenging Determinism, Compatibilism, and Sundry Libertarians Peter Lugten Free will isa genuine, real property of the human condition, a stance that \u2018overthrows conventional arguments. Suppose that a man pulls the trigger of a gun. Mechanistically, the muscles in his index finger contracted because they were \u2018stimulated by a neuron having an action potential (ie. being in a particularly excited state). That neuron. Conti }eading in Free Inquiry Get Involved Urge Your Representative Louisiana: Help Defeat These Two Theocratic Bills May 19, Azhar Majeed The Center for Inquiry (CFi) is calling on our supporters in Louisiana to help defeat two bills that promote religion in public schools. Both bills ha passed in the Louisiana Senate and are currently before the House of already is scheduled to end on June 1, making this an urgent TAKE ACTION CFI Freethinking Blogs wy ltl \u201cABig Challenge to Any Religious fing Worldview\u2019 - Aliens and Theology, Nones, and the Partisan Healthcare Gap ing June 1, 2026 The Morning F Jeff Dellinger \u2018Welcome to the Morning Heresy, CFI\u2019 thrice-weekly roundup of news and headlines for the reality-based community. Southwest Florida's WGCU spoke with Elyssa Vazquez of Cape Coral, Florida, the first-prize inner in the 2026 ScienceSaves Video Scholarship Contest. One of the prompts was to create a 20- to 30- second video answering the question, \u201cWhat has science This Pale Blue Backwater\u201d - More from Free Inquiry, Powdered Greens, and Retread Conspiracy Theories May 29,2026 The Morning F Jeff Dellinge he Morning Heres: \u2018Welcome to the Morning Heresy, CFI's roundup of news and headlines for the reality-based community. The June/July 2026 issue of Free Inquiry focuses on \"The US: Where It's Been, Where It Is, Where It Shoul But that's not all the new issue has to offer. You'l also find anew commentary from Richard Dawkins \u201cA Product of the Enlightenment\u201d - New Free Inquiry, Video Scholarship Winners, and Poisonous Frog Skin May 27,2024 The Morning F Jeff Dellinger \u2018And we're back! Welcome to the Morning Heres regular roundup of news and headlines for the reality based community. The June/July 2026 issue of Free Inquiry is now available to read online. The focus of this latest issue is on \u201cThe U.S.: Where It's Been, Where Its, \u2018Where It Should Go\" As the United About Us Our Work Get Involved Join a Comnmnity Find a group near you. Connect with student groups, humanists, and critical thinking groups nationwide! Stay Up To Date Sign up today for our important email newsletter and stay updated on news and information. News & Press ScienceSaves Announces Winners of Its 2026 Video Scholarship Contest May 27,2026 Press Releas Jeff Dellinger \u2018The Center for Inquiry's (CFI) ScienceSaves programis pleased to announce the winners of its 2026 ScienceSaves Video Scholars \u2018hundreds of submissions from college-bound high school seniors across the country, with each video detailing the impact science has had on their lives or the life of someone they know personally. Contest. This year, ScienceSaves received Center for Inquiry Slams \u2018Rededicate 250\u2019 Event, Calls for Renewed \u2018Commitment to Jefferson's \u201cWall of Separation Between Church and State May 18, News Jeff Delling: \u2018On Sunday, the National Mall played host to \"Rededicate 250: A National Jubilee of Prayer, Praise & Thanksgiving. an event \u2018partly funded by millions in public dollars\" which organizers designed to \u201cprepare for the nation\u2019s 250th birthday with Scripture, testimony, prayer, and rededication of our country as One Nation to God\" The Center for Inquiry Mary Roach and Bill Nye to Receive Special Awards at CSICon 2026 April 30, 2026 Press Releases Jeff Dellinger Friday, May 1, marks the official fiftieth anniversary of the founding of the Committee for \u2018Skeptical Inquiry (CSI), a program of the Center for Inquiry (CFI). In celebration of this landmark anniversary, the Committee for S