inue Manage before he died after being fatally stabbed by Vickrum Digwa. \u00a2 WRDAM, DE Henry Nowak: PM and leader of \u201cIk opposition warn against whipping up i emotions amid two-tier policing $i \u201cANAY \u2018OMmy OF clewne \"A MASSACRE We're in Westminster to find out what MPs have been saying about the Henry Novak case. Over 50 MPs turn on Starmer, so who leads i Labe ct? \u2018Anti-white racism is structurally abour nex 1 embedded\u2019 in police - Reform UK on Henry Nowak case We spoke to Reform UK's Home Affairs Spokesperson, Zia Yusuf, and asked him what he thought Nigel Farage meant when he said people should respond with \u201cpure cold rage\" to the treatment of Henry Nowak Why Americans fell out of love with Israel - explained Henry Nowak case: Allegations of Caught by Snapchat: two-tier policing \u2018needs to be ry: How police tracked the evidenced-based\u2019 - National Black bike shockers Police Association We spoke to Andy George, president of the National Black Police Association and asked whether he - agrees with those who've claimed that the Henry Will jet fuel shortages Novak case is an example of two-tier policing force Brits to cancel summer holiday plans? Inside Lebanon: New ceasefire fails to stop Israel from bombing south Israel has continued its airstrikes on southern FactCheck: Double- Lebanon despite the partial ceasefire agreement decker buses and with Hezbollah, hearses among vehicles targeted by thieves US Sec of State grilled by Congress in first testimony since start of Iran Anthropic co-founder: war Al impact \u201c10x larger The US Secretary of State Marco Rubio has been and 10x faster than grilled by Congressmen in his first public testimony industrial revolution\u2019 since the start of the Iran war. MTENEY Trump \u2018very frustrated\u2019 with and feels MMMWET deceived by Netanyahu over length CURLM of war says US professor fig] Shibloy Tothami from the University of Maryland joins Russia launches one of its biggest attacks ever on Ukraine killing at least 22 At least 22 people are known to have been killed and more than 100 others injured after Russia launched start ofthe full-scale war in February 2022. Court hears details of Peter Murrell\u2019s \u00a3400,000 SNP embezzlement Details have been revealed showing how former { scottish National party chief Peter Murrell embezzled \u00a3400,000 from party funds. NR South West Water fined \u00a31.8m after parasitic contamination of supply South West Water has been fined \u00a31.85m ~ a record fine for a drinking water offence - after it admitted to supplying contaminated water, which was unfit for human consumption, to thousands of residents in south Devon Should the UK offer more Gaza children life-saving NHS treatment? The government had suggested up to 300 seriously ill or injured children from Gaza would be brought to the UK for treatment - but have told this programme just 50 children have actually arrived. UN warns of El Nifio extreme weather risk The world has been warned to prepare for the imminent return of El Nifo ~ along with extreme weather conditions. Why Fifa World Cup 2026 could be doomed from the start In our latest episode of the breakdown, Channel 4 News looks at the controversy around prices and politics dominating the buildup to one of the world\u2019s biggest sporting events. 1 Jun 2026 Taking a stand against taunts to \u2018go back where you came from\u2019 When 24-year-old Jaiyana is faced with the taunt \u201cgo back where you come from\u2019, she has an answer: \"Go back to where?\u201d Colombia election: Pro-Trump candidate heads to run-off with leftist opponent The polls didn\u2019t predict it but Colombia's right-wing presidential challenger has come out infront after the first round of the country\u2019s elections, prompting the left-wing president to question the results Chinook crash: Former minister = claims information \u2018withheld\u2019 after tragedy The former Defence Secretary Sir Liam Fox has told this programme he may have been misled by the Ministry of Defence over the 1994 Chinook crash on the Mull of Kintyre Ebola: $62 million pledge to speed up vaccine development A global body set up to accelerate the development of vaccines has pledged $62 million to speed up progress on experimental jabs aimed at tackling the virus behind the Ebola outbreak. Nottingham university staff strike over plans to cut jobs and programmes Staff at the University of Nottingham have begun a \u2018two month strike, along with a marking boycott, over plans to cut more than 700 jobs and shut down dozens of degree programmes altogether. Man jailed for 21 years after stabbing 18-year-old Henry Nowak to death \u2018Aman who stabbed a student to death has been jailed for at least 21 years. \u2018Strikes on Lebanon have nothing to do with security of Israel\u2019 - Gideon Levy We were joined by Gideon Levy, a columnist for the Haaretz newspaper. Israel orders strikes on south Beirut as forces push deeper into Lebanon People are fleeing the Lebanese capital after Israel warned of new air strikes but Donald Trump has claimed Hezbollah and Israel have agreed not to attack each other. \u2018How did Mandelson get the job?\u201d asks Foreign Affairs Committee chair We were joined by Labour MP Dame Emily Thornberry, who is Chair of the Foreign Affairs Committee. New batch of Mandelson files published - how embarrassing is it 4 for the government? In three volumes, with hundreds of emails, WhatsApps and memos, the Mandelson files handed government publications 4 Mariana Mazzucato: Why is there always money for war but never for public investment? Economic growth is at the centre of British politics once again. Nicola Sturgeon defends record following estranged husband's conviction Scotland's former first minister Nicola Sturgeon has defended her record ~ after her estranged husband was convicted for embezzling more than \u00a3400,000 from the Scottish National Party. (IM \u2018Middle East war has devastating", "ocr_text_len": 6042}
