{"_key": "codastory", "source_key": "codastory", "filename": "Coda_Story.png", "image_file": "Coda_Story.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 1.5103, "s008_neutral_headlines": -1.5248, "s010_scare_quotes": 3.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 2.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.318, "s078_absolutist_framing": 4.0, "s085_standard_sections": 5.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 9.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00263, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.6863, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.6748, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.0, "small_face_count": 0.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0337, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.5251, "content_column_count": "2", "side_margin_frac": 0.043, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0055, "logo_centered": 0.0, "accent_hue": "red", "accent_color_count": 1.5918, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0083, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 29.0, "footer_link_count": 100.0, "cta_button_count": 0.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 2.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 2.375, "headline_size_variance": 0.1629, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 0.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0127, "number_token_frac": 0.0016, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.4769, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.159, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.0, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.318, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 7.4722, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.318, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.159}, "ocr_text": "= Q .coda Journalism that unpacks the global authoritarian toolkit Rewriting History In this current, stories on how those in The new samizdat For years at Coda, we have tried to understand not just what is happening in the world, but how seemingly separate crises, technologies and political movements connect power shape our future by weaponized the past and manipulating our \u2018The Belongers: What the Chagos Islands tells us about the new world order A strategically important base is the setting for a new version of an old story about colonialism, exile, sovereignty, and the projection of power SPECIAL PROJECT The Alibi Machine In Russia's information war, the cover story is written before the bomb drops. Is that a crime? id our Authoritarian Tech In this current, stories on how technology has captured every aspect, \u201cAll my fundees have blue eyes.\u201d Epstein and the tech . * world\u2019s dark ideology How Brazil is starting to rein in Big Tech The Age of Exile \u2018What does displacement look lke in the era of digital connection? Our series explores how exile has evolved from historical punishment into a defining condition of our time. Polarization Peter Thiel is building a parallel justice system \u2014 Powered by AI His investment in Objection.ai points to a new model: private investigations, Al verdicts, and accountability mechanisms that operate outside democratic institutions. Who you are and what you believe have been weaponized in new ways in the power struggles of the 2Ist century. We track what price individuals and societies pay for these identity battles. Always on the outside: Exile isn\u2019t about the country you leave When a lie about Haitians in Ohio spread nationwide, a pioneering Haitian-American journalist was forced to ask if belonging will always be conditional. Exile, he realized, is not geography, i's the distance between who you are and who the nation insists you must be \u201cThe Politics of Dysfunction\u201d THE THINKERS from Coda Media: bold ideas, urgent questions, and the people behind them. Recorded at ZEG Storytelling Festival. \u2018Author and researcher Peter Pomerantsev has spent years dissecting how modern authoritarianism works \u2014 and why democracies keep losing ground. In this, conversation, he explains how strongmen are learning to network across borders, why \u201cgetting-shit-done\u201d politics is winning people over, and what treating information like a weapon does to our public life. He also reveals the one group he thinks will shape our future \u2014 and why, despite everything, he stil finds a sliver of hope. Armed Conflict In this current, we take a deep dive into how digital technology is re defining armed conflicts, Why an insurgency in Mali matters in Moscow For years, Russia has been interfering in the Sahel, using misinformation and mercenaries in what now looks like a botched bid to secure influence and control OA STOR Teens making drones: Russia\u2019s demographic collapse Despite the Kremlin's focus on raising birth rates, a combination of war and failed policy means the country\u2019s steep Population decline now seems terminal. Captured Newsletters The afterlife of empire My mother tongues \u2018The Al therapist epidemic: When bots replace humans The Werewolf game: an interview with Google\u2019s former news chief Richard Gingras cova story \u2018The Identitarians are back: How a discredited worldview dominates the global agenda Europe vs Big Tech: A battle for democracy? Silicon Valley and the U.S. government are positioning ther frustration over detense of reedom over government contol An endless purgatory: How an exiled Iranian waits and watches The Al-powered \u2018forever wars\u2019 start now The Secret Behind Silicon Valley's Al Takeover isa thrilling journey into the hidden worlds of the tech elite, and a whistleblower's look into the scii future they're building for all of us. You can listen to the podcast here, or dig deeper into our stories here:", "ocr_text_len": 3895}
