ionship between Darwinism and real science is parasitic. The theory's main use is. for Darwinists to claim credit for whatever biology discovers. If research shows that humans are selfish, Darwinism can explain that. If science shows we are unselfish, why, it can explain that too. If we are a combination of both \u2014 no problem. If cells are simple or complex, if sexual reproduction is common or rare, if embryos are similar or different, Darwinism will explain ital for you. The elasticity of the theory would make Sigmund Freud blush. \u2014 Michael Behe, First Things (Nov 2000) Latest Headlines VIEW HEADLINES ONLY June 3, 2026 \u201cBrain as a Computer\" Metaphor Rebooted While the brain is certainly more and other than a compute, itis also not less than one. \u2018CONTINUE READING \u2014 (READ MOREIN MIND AND BRAIN) June 2, 2028 Cells Have a \u201cHail Mary\u201d Strategy to Minimize Damage Living colls are equipped with extraordinarily sophisticated, energy-intensive systems. designed primarily to suppress mutations \u2018CONTINUE READING - . (READ WORE! CELL BIOLOGY) June 1 2026 Debunked Vestigial Organs Argument Rises Again \\Why have these same vestigial-organ claims been repeated over and over again for many decades?\u201d \u2018CONTINUE READING a (EAD MORE IN DARWIN AND EVOLUTION May 31,2026 Whales Break Record for Migration Distance \u2018Scientists observe humpback whales migrating 15,000 km between Australia and Braz We reflect on the purpose and implications of these observations from a creation perspective. \u2018CONTINUE READING May 30,2026 temporary habits picked up in a lawless flux \u2018CONTINUE READING May 28,2026 When Laws Evolve, Part 1: The Emerging Crisis of Modern Science In order to maintain the commitments of \u2018methodological naturalism, the definition of CONTINUE READING May 27,2026 Climate Change Alarmism Pushed in Schools \u2018A proposed act rises ongoing questions about how controversial scientific topics should be CLIMATE CHANGE!