g but to. actively suppressing any attempt to take the United Kingdom's problems seriously. [EVENT | June 29] America at 250: A Conversation with Adom Getachew, Aziz Rana, and Davi Waldstreicher Editors * June 1, 2026 An online event in partnership with Boston Review. [ R Lal sill Know Your Enemy: Mi American Manhood Matthew Sitman and Sam Adler-Bell \u00bb May 27, 2026 ry Educa nand i] u Matt and Sam talk to Jasper Craven about his new book, God Forgives, Brothers Don't: The Long March of Military Education and the Making of American Manhood. ee pe Resurrecting the Bund Mark Erlich * Summer 2026 In Here Where We Live Is Our Country, Molly Crabapple elevates an important part of the democratic socialist tradition at a time when many are looking for just such a usable past. Sign up for the Dissent newsletter: Which Way, Western Marxism? Who Paid the Pipers of Western Marxism?is an inversion of a right-wing conspiracy, in which the prominence of the Frankfurt \u2018School is explained as the result of a plot to destroy truly GLOBAL, revolutionary Marsism. PORES BARCELONA Callitthe End \u2018APRIL 20: Patrick Iber = Summer 2026 RODE STO OMEN, Introducing our Summer 2026 issue on America at 250. Capital of the American Century Mason B. Williams = Winter 2026 Mike Wallace's Gotham at War offers a guidebook to a half- vanished city, and brings to life the immense human drama that unfolded in New York during the Second World War. Know Your Enemy: The Seven Year Anniversary Mailbag Episode Matthew Sitman and Sam Adler-Bell * May 12, 2026 Matt and Sam answer listener questions about post-Trump, politics, the meaning of Zohran Mamdani, the fate of liberalism, Doubling Down Michael Knapp * May 11, 2026 Online sports gambling has been normalized at a breakneck pace. Is there any way to push back against a predatory culture of promo codes and prop bets? The Many Sides of Shame Rhoda Feng = May 6, 2026 While the case that resulted in the conviction of fifty-one men for the rape of Gis\u00e9le Pelicot last year was extraordinary, itis continuous with other forms of sexual violence. How Mamdani Can Build Mass Engagement Mark Engler and Matthew Miles Goodrich * May 4, 2026 The success of Organize NYC, a new initiative designed to bring a grassroots base into the guts of the governing process, will have implications for the left outside the five boroughs. Constitutional Moment in Hungary? Gabor Halmai \u00ab April 30, 2026 The defeat of Viktor Orb\u00e9n wasn't primarily driven by anger over the dismantling of liberal democracy. But the new government could serve as a positive example for others working to reverse democratic backsliding. Know Your Enemy: Peter Thiel and the Antichrist Matthew Sitman and Sam Adler-Bell * April 28, 2026 Matt and Sam discuss Peter Thies lectures on the Antichrist and what they reveal about his politics and this political moment. The Bronx Still Burns David Helps * Winter 2026 The borough's arson wave in the 1970s was caused by financial forces and political priorities that continue to hold power in New York City. Power and Abuse in the United Farm Workers Nahomi Linda Esquivel * April 16, 2026 The alleged sexual violence committed by Cesar Chavez cannot be understood as the failing of a single charismatic leader. It unfolded within a patterned system of organizational control over Building a Post-Trump Foreign Policy Andre Paglisrini * April 15, 2026 Progressives need to ground international commitments to democratic accountability at home and engage with social movements abroad. Few political figures have articulated this as clearly as Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez. About Sontact \u2018Advertise Donate Facebook Subscribe Tuatter Newsletter \u2018This website ante content \u00a9 Dissent Magazine 2026. Allrghts reserved,", "ocr_text_len": 3943}
