{"_key": "euvsdisinfo", "source_key": "euvsdisinfo", "filename": "EUvsDisinfo.png", "image_file": "EUvsDisinfo.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 1.6453, "s008_neutral_headlines": 1.2814, "s010_scare_quotes": 2.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.3656, "s078_absolutist_framing": 1.0, "s085_standard_sections": 2.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 11.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00338, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.8462, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.5555, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00219, "small_face_count": 2.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0456, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.248, "content_column_count": "1", "side_margin_frac": 0.0, "header_band_height_frac": 0.1155, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 1.3306, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0153, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 33.0, "footer_link_count": 45.0, "cta_button_count": 2.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 1.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 0.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 6.333, "headline_size_variance": 0.2523, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 5.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0404, "number_token_frac": 0.0386, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.0, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.2559, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.9141, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.3656, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.1938, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.0, "lx_local_civic_per100": 2.3766}, "ocr_text": "Subscribe to the Disinfo Review Your weekly update on pro-Kremlin disinformation Data Protection Information * The Disinformation Review is sent through Mailchimp.com. See Mailchimp\u2019s privacy policy and find out more on how EAS protects your personal data. Ihave read and understood the Privacy Statemen Cookies This site uses cookies to offer you a better browsing experience. Find out more on how we use cookies. [ACCEPT ONLY ESSENTIAL COOKIES disinformation cases collected and debunked Reports 4th EEAS Report on Foreign 3rd EEAS Report on Foreign 2nd EEAS Report on Foreign 1st Information Manipulation and Information Manipulation and Information Manipulation and Inf Interference Threats Interference Threats Interference Threats Int News and Analysis Guest content Victim-blaming Kyiv, pressuring Moldova, and drone disinformation + Russia tries to shift blame for its deadly strikes on Kyiv. + Transnistria is used as a tool to destabilise Moldova. + Ukraine is, being falsely accused of trying to drag the Baltic states into war with Russia News and Analysis Tough love: Spies, dating apps and the dark side of online intimacy Dating apps promise connection, chemistry, and maybe even love. For Ukrainian and Russian intelligence services, they also offer something else: data, emotional vulnerability, and a private channel to manipulate targets. Guest content The Digital Iron Curtain 2.0: how the MAX messenger is reshaping Russia's communication space UpenMinds DYrhws The dog that didn\u2019t bark: What the Danish election reveals about Russian influence operations According to Danish state authorities, there were no major foreign influence campaigns to speak of in the lead-up to Denmark's, March 2026 parliamentary election. Local fact-checkers and journalists tracked pro-Russian narratives and fringe propaganda channels, but nothing resembling a broad, coordinated campaign with significant reach emerged. Monitoring and analysis by Defense Innovation Highway and OpenMinds of part of the Danish online information environment during the campaign reached similar conclusions. Disinformation Review Lies about Russia's military success, Yermak\u2019s arrest and secret biolabs Ukrainian strikes on Russian targets are falsely framed as cover for domestic political scandals. Europe is again portrayed as standing in the way of peace. Old \u201cUkrainian biolabs\u201d conspiracy theories make a comeback. News and Analysis Victory Day propaganda, masking fear with intimidation, and abduction denial The Kremlin recycles \u2018Nazi Ukraine\u2019 myths amid Victory Day celebrations. By 2026, Russia's digital control strategy has evolved from blocking platforms like Telegram to building its own: MAX, a state- backed messenger with over 55 million users. More than an app, MAX integrates messaging, verified digital IDs, and state services \u2014effectively embedding surveillance into daily life. Though not legally mandatory, schools and agencies now rely on it, making alternatives impractical. The Kremlin isn\u2019t just censoring; it's redesigning the digital environment to ensure compliance by default. View all ill h View Infographics Subscribe to the Disinfo Review Your weekly update on pro-Kremiin disinformation yy March 0-Merch 16 Last Week on EUvsDisinfo - February 24 - March 2, 2025 Last Week on EUvsDisinfo - March 3 - 9, 2025 Last Week on EUvsDisinfo - Las March 10 - 16, 2025 Ma Content Categories Articles Ukraine DONT BE DECEIVED, QUESTION EVEN MORE Database Belarus Learn Moldova Contact Us Research Georgia European External Action Service (EEAS) Rdpt Robert Schuman 9, 1046 Brussels, Belgium Videos Eastern Partnership General en EASY Guest content China About Africa cooxtes DATA PROTECTION DISCLAIMER", "ocr_text_len": 3710}
