 Northern Ireland. FactCheckNl is an independent team of fact-checkers committed to examining key public statements related to Northern Ireland. We analyse the best available evidence and publish fact-check articles to enhance the quality of public debate, knowledge and understanding. Search the facts EDUCATION ECONOMY Articles | Economy | Environment | Topics Politics in NI: Was redevelopment of the AS stopped by the Climate Change Act? \u00a9 June 2026 CLAIM: Despite Sinn F\u00e9in Leader Mary Lou McDonald suggesting unionism had a hand in stopping redevelopment of the As Western Transport Corridor, the project was halted by the Climate Change Act~andall unionist parties supportamending the Act. RATING ACCURATE (On 26 April in a post on social media, newspaper columnist Newton Emerson said: This claim that redevelopment of the As was stopped by the $\u00a2 Choose from over 300 fact checks on the topics that matter most to you Europe des Brexit, the Irish border, passports, Good Friday Agreement, Environment Includes agriculture, animals, climate change and recycling Latest fact checks \\ yn Articles | Economy | Peace | Topics WhatsApp Information in NI: Will the Orange Order help you purchase ahome? \u00a9 21 May 2026 CLAIM: People looking to buy homes in the near future could get support to do so from the Grand Orange Lodge of Ireland. RATING INACCURATE Inrecent weeks, messages have been circulating \u2018on social media making claims that the Orange Order, and one lodge in the Castlecaulfield area in particular, VIEW ALL \u00b0 \u00abat Elections Includes party manifestos, hustings, and election processes > > Services Transparency of sources vantour readersto be able rify our findings themselves Newsletter sign up Keep up with the latest from F newslet lonly send Gy FactCheckn uthe share you email address. Fact Check Search Engine \u2018We have published over 300 fact check articles on topics relating to life in Northern Ireland since 2016 Thisis a free resource that anyone can use 24 hours a day, Learn more Fact Check Toolkit We've created a simple guide that's perfect for anyone wanting tolearn how totell the difference between fact, fiction, and \u201cfake news\" We encourage everyone to think critically, and inthis article, we share tips on how you can check the information you come across especially online Learnmore Why trust us? FactCheckNI is Northern Ireland's first and only dedicated fact checking service, operating with the following commitments Transparency of Funding and Organisation Weare transparent about our funding sources. NIwith our email ff, Well never spam Open and Honest Corrections Policy We publish our corrections policy and follow it scrupulously, Topics Economy Education Elections Environment Europe FactCheck NI About Us TheTeam Articles | Economy | Environment | Explainer| Topics Green energy in NI #1: The Renewables boom, and what came after \u00a9 18 May 2026 \\Whatis renewable energy doing for people in Northern Ireland? What more can it do? How do \u2018we make that happen? Recent shocksin the 9 B o) Education Economy Includes child-care, primary. Includes hor secondary and tertiary poverty, and education spent. \u2018Training We design and deliver bespoke training sessions in fact checking and critical thinking skills to groups, organisations and, communities across NI Learn more International Fact- Nonparti Checking Network fairness We area verified signatory toits Weuse thes Code of Principles every subjec Governance Code of Principles Process Funding ContactUs News 26 FactCheckNI All rights reserved \u00a5HEO web design and web development by wile", "ocr_text_len": 3809}
