{"_key": "factcheckorg", "source_key": "factcheckorg", "filename": "FactCheck.org.png", "image_file": "FactCheck.org.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 1.0989, "s008_neutral_headlines": 1.1219, "s010_scare_quotes": 12.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 0.0, "s085_standard_sections": 4.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 18.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.0039, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.7629, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.5201, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00237, "small_face_count": 4.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0625, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.2307, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.207, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0098, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 1.9678, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0202, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 64.0, "footer_link_count": 87.0, "cta_button_count": 2.0, "newsletter_box_count": 1.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 1.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 7.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 5.692, "headline_size_variance": 0.1366, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 11.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0321, "number_token_frac": 0.0398, "city_or_county_in_name": 1.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.0, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0659, "lx_timestamp_per100": 1.2088, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.2198, "lx_health_scare_per100": 1.3187, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.1978, "lx_culture_war_per100": 1.6484, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.6593, "lx_local_civic_per100": 2.1978}, "ocr_text": "\\ATE | FactCheck.org A Project of The Annenberg Public Policy Center fix HOME ARTICLES~ ASK A QUESTION NATE TOPICS~ ABOUTUS~ SEARCH \u2014 MORE 4. Ask FactCheck (Q:Has President Trump asked for a billion dollars for the ballroom? A: Since the White House announced plans in July for a ballroom, the president has promised to fund its construction without using public money. But in May congressional Republicans proposed $1 \u2018Trump Distorts Maryland\u2019s Primary Ballot Mi Dillion in federal funding for \u201csecurity Mail-in Voting adjustments and upgrades\u201d including at the White House and the ballroom site. Read the full question and answer View the Ask FactCheck archives Have a question? Ask us. A Timeline of RFK Jr\u2019s Mixed Messaging on the Measles Vaccine Donate Now May 28, 2026 Because facts matter. In defending his record on measles, Health and Human secause facts matiet Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. twice said during a recent Senate hearing, \u201cWe promote\u201d the measles vaccine. While it\u2019s true that the Centers for SciCheck's COVID- Disease Control and Prevention continues to 19/Vaccination Project recommend the shot, Kennedy has rarely made an Preempting and exposing \u2018unequivocal endorsement of it, even as the nation has vaccination and COVID-19, misinformation. Proyecto de seen an alarming rise in measles cases. as COVID-19 y sus vacunas up to Attack Mail-in Voting May 27,2026 SciCheck Fact-checking science-based \u2018Maryland election officials are mailing replacement claims. ballots to voters after a vendor error led to some voters Vacunaci\u00e9n/COVID-19 Precaviendo y exponiendo la Trump Distorts Maryland\u2019s Primary Ballot Mix- desinformaci\u00e9n sobre el receiving a mail-in ballot for the wrong political party's primary in June. However, in criticizing the mix-up, Viral Spiral President Donald Trump distorted the facts to claim that Neenah 500,000 \u201cfake,\u201d \u201ccorrupt\u201d and \u201cillegal\u201d ballots had been Dont get spun by internet mailed to ensure \u201cDemocrats win.\u201d \u00a9 Newsletter Get our free weekly email REK Jr.\u2019s Muddled Claims on Drug Approval Speed May 22, 2026 Mailbag \u2018The Food and Drug Administration in recent months Letters from our readers. has approved a small number of drugs quite quickly under a new expedited review program. But Health and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. has overstated the impact of the program by making misleading comparisons to the pace of drug approvals in On the Air Our staff on TV and radio. & a the past. NewsFeed Defenders Ad in Texas GOP Runoff Attacks Cornyn on detect misinformation. Immigration, Islam May 21, 2026 ATVad attacking incumbent Texas Sen. John Cornyn for supporting \u201cMuslim mass immigration\u201d misleadingly cites a 2021 quote from Cornyn about certain Afghan refugees and claims that \u201cCornyn has a special place in his heart for radical Islam\u201d GOP SENATOR What Will Happen to Gasoline Prices When the Iran War Ends? \u2018May 1, 2026 President Donald Trump on multiple occasions has assured the public that high gasoline prices will \u201crapidly\u201d or \u201cquickly\u201d decline \u201cas soon as\u201d the war with Iran ends. Energy experts told us that prices will start to fall when the conflict is resolved, but it could take many months before the national average price is back to where it was before the conflict began. Who\u2019s Paying for the White House Ballroom? May 14, 2026 Has President Trump asked for abi ballroom? dollars for the \u2018A: Since the White House announced plans in July fora ballroom, the president has promised to fund its construction without using public money. But in May congressional Republicans proposed $1 billion in federal funding for \u201csecurity adjustments and upgrades\u201d including at the White House and the ballroom site. Republicans Repeat Problematic Estimate of Medication Abortion Harms May 12, 2026 we comonia Mitepristone Tablets 15 the midst ofa court battle over whether to continue to allow access by mail to the medication abortion pill mifepristone, Republican lawmakers have claimed that 10% or more of women who take the drug have serious side effects. A 2025 report from an anti-abortion group that put forward the figure has been criticized by reproductive health researchers for methodological issues and a lack of transparency about its data source. Kennedy Denies the One Big Beautiful Bill Act\u2019s Spending Cuts to Medicaid May 6, 2026 \u2018The nonpartisan Congressional Budget Office estimated that the One Big Beautiful Bill Act will reduce federal \u2018Medicaid spending by more than $900 billion over a decade. But in a series of congressional hearings last month, Health and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. misleadingly claimed that \u201cthere are no cuts to Medicaid\u201d as.a result of that 2025 law. Democratic Ad Attacks Collins on Healthcare, Iran War \u2018May 4, 2026 \u2018Anad attacking Sen. Susan Collins in Maine claimed that she voted \u201cto raise healthcare costs and raise insurance premiums;\u2019 as well as give President Donald \u2018Trump \u201ca blank check for his war in Iran.\u201d But neither claim fully explains Collins\u2019 more nuanced position on. those issues. REK Jr\u2019s Unsupported Claims About Tylenol- Autism Study He Called \u2018Garbage\u2019 April 30, 2026 During an April 17 congressional hearing, Health and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. called for retraction of a new Danish study that didn't find a link between Tylenol and autism, repeatedly calling it \u201cgarbage\u201d and baselessly suggesting that it was industry-generated and \u201cfraudulent\u201d |: Eee ARCHIVES PRIVACY COPYRIGHT POLICY CONTACTUS REPORT ACCESSIBILITY ISSUES AND GET HELP Copyright 2026 FactCheck.org \u00ae [Project of he Annenberg Public Policy Cente of the University of Pennsyvania", "ocr_text_len": 5654}
