{"_key": "factmyth", "source_key": "factmyth", "filename": "Fact_Myth.png", "image_file": "Fact_Myth.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.8661, "s008_neutral_headlines": -0.1377, "s010_scare_quotes": 10.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0787, "s078_absolutist_framing": 5.0, "s085_standard_sections": 6.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 13.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.04115, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.6087, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.0, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00071, "small_face_count": 3.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0859, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.2887, "content_column_count": "1", "side_margin_frac": 0.177, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0122, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 3.5938, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0163, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 50.0, "footer_link_count": 251.0, "cta_button_count": 0.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 1.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 1.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 7.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 3.5, "headline_size_variance": 0.1853, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 0.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0174, "number_token_frac": 0.0087, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.6299, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.1102, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.0, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0787, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.3937, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.9921, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0787, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.7087, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.7874}, "ocr_text": "CT / MYTH FACTS MYTHS BLOG FactMyth.com, where \u201calternative facts\" are laid to rest. Help us fact-check by commenting, Facts and Myths on Everything Coinbase, Binance, Oculus, Namecheap, ExpressVPN, and more! FactMyth.com isa fact checking website that presents a collection of facts and myths. It is an educational resource full of explainer videos, citations, history logic, and science. We FactMyth jelcome to FactMyth aq \\ eS 3: -! EB YouTube: FactMyth.com into video. We fact-check the conclusions of common internet talking points, peer-reviewed journals, the classics, Netflix documentaries, historians\u2019 accounts of history, smart \u2018TV shows, select claims by officials and official reports, YouTube videos, economic theories, scientific theories, popular science, folklore, commonly held beliefs, and other academically minded \u201cfactoids\u201d (unverified claims AKA unverified propositions) passed around the culture and media of any era, After researching a \u201cfactoid,\u201d curating the best citations and videos we can find inthe process (the best evidence of any sort), we rate the overarching statement (proposition) as \u201cfact\u201d or \u201cmyth\u201d (thus assigning a certain truth-value to the proposition based on research). We then explain our position in as simple and clear terms as possible to build a case for our conclusion, using citations and offering insight into counterpoints (we back up our assigned truth-value by presenting an informal argument, generally written in essay form) It isn't that we are always correct, in fact we are only human (as Montaigne said, \u201cwhat do I know?\", as Plato's Socrates had previously answered \u201cL know that I know nothing\u2019, although as Lincoln said, \u201cLam not a Know-Nothing\u2019). In fact, that isan important part ofthe site, we are always digging deeper and seeking alternative viewpoints! \u2018To rephrase the above, digging for the truth is complex, we don\u2019t have all the answers, and that is why we need your help! Users can help us stay relevant and accurate by commenting on our facts and myths to offer rebuttals and insight. We \u201cfollow the truth where it may lead\u201d as they say, 0 feel free to offer citations and challenge our findings! \u2018Simply put, we aren't experts, we are researchers, and the hunt for truth isa collective process of \u201cbeing skeptical\" and \u201cquestioning everything\u201d (feel free to join in cn the fun by commenting and questioning us!) With that al said, one should note that FactMyth.com isnt a place to debate emotionally charged opinions and rhetoric (we cover relevant political science and policy, but try to avoid the political talking points of the day, for example). The focus is instead on high-level academic information (including facts and myths on histon hy, people, the ars, sciences, maths, and philosophies) and practical information (including facts and myths related to self-help, health, skill es, technology, finance, and culture). In this way the site doubles as a free online university for general knowledge (or atleast an encyclopedia or reference guide of interesting and useful truths; ie. i is an encyclopedia of knowledge of all types, presented as a fact-checking sie). We ask abit of the reader intellectually, but we try to keep it simple and \u201cexplain i like you are five (a really smart 5)\" Help us level up the collective intelligence of the internet by commenting and sharing. There is cake! \u2018TIP: If you're not feeling epistemological, you're not paying attention! Learn more about \u201cHow FactMyth.com works. Discover more science scientific Science BROWSE FACTS BROWSE MYTHS 223) Horseshoe Crab Blood is Valuable Qo Horseshoe crab blood is highly valued, especialy in the biomedical field. Its blue blood fs \u201ce\u201d is Just as Important as Pi Gap We all have heard of the famous mathematical constant Pi, but did you know there. Humans Share Over 50% Of Their DNA With Bananas! Gap We assume humans are very different from plants. The surprising truth is that humans share There are more possible iterations ofa game of chess than there are atoms in the known universe Gap \u2018The claim that a game of chess has more possible iterations than atoms in the. Some Jellyfish are Immortal G9 Its true that Turritopsis dohrii, known as the \u201cimmortal jellyfish\u201d can avoid death from. Can Al Write an Article? The Future of Fact- Checking and Al Collaboration collaboration, current Al limitations, and the. This article explores the relationship between AI and human How Isaac Newton Actually Lost His Money in the South Sea Bubble bought early. The Difference Between Truth and Facts same, Price's Law root of all contributors.\u201d Why Oil Prices Went Negative translated to oil producers paying. Isaac Newton didn't just buy the top in the South Sea bubble. He \u2018Truth and facts have a lot in common, but they are not exactly the Price's Law says, \u201chalf ofthe publications come from the square il prices went negative on April 2oth, 2020. This essentially BROWSE ALL ARTICLES Cheese Causes Nightmares (LB \u2018While diet can impact sleep, there is no substantial evidence to support the claim that. Humans Explode or Freeze in Space Without a Spacesuit Gy Contrary to popular belief, humans do not explode or freeze in the vacuum of space. People Swallow Spiders in Their Sleep \u2018The widespread belief that people unknowingly swallow many spiders during sleep each year isa Hair and Nails Continue to Grow After Death GQ \u2018This article dispels the myth that hair and nails continue to grow after death by. Lightning Doesn't Strike the Same Place Twice ip Lightning has been a source of both wonder and fear for centuries. Among the numerous, Subjects Arts and Cutture Geography and Places Health and Fitness History and Events Mathematics and Logic People and Self Philosophy and Thinking Religion and Belief Systems Society and Social Sciences o oe oO o o Natural and Physical Sciences = @ eo oe oO C2) \u00b0o Technology and Applied Sciences \u2018About One Half of... Abraham Lincoln Ada Lovelace Adam Smith Alan Turing Albert Einstein Alexander Hamilton, American Politics Antikythera Nechanism Artificial Intelligence Astrology Atari Attention Augmented Reality Baseball Benjamin Franklin BiaS Blaise Pascal Bob Moog Calorie Cannabis Capitalism Cells Charles Babbage Christmas cruses timate Climate Change Cognitive Computing Collective Intelligence Competition Complexity Science Conspiracy Theories Cooperation cryptocurrency Cryptography Derek de Sola Price DNA Drugs Early Computers Economic Bubble Economic Inequality Electricity Elements Empathy Energy England Environment Epistemology Equality eSports Essentialism and Existentialism Ethics Evolution Eyesightracwis Fathers or Mothers of a Field Feminism France Galileo Galilei Gambling Game Theory George Washington Germany Google Gravity Gun Control and Gun Rights Har Happiness Kip Hop Human Brain Human Rights 16M immanuel Kant Individualism and Collectivism Infinity Internet Isaac Newton James Madison James Monroe Jean-Jacques Rousseau John Locke John Maynard Keynes KariMan. Learning Left-right Politics inisnLiberalism and Conservatism Liberty tite Hacks ight Logic and Reason Ludwig von Mises Malaria Markets Mary Shelley Mass Meat Memory Metaphysics Money Morality mortality Rates Music Theory Napoleon Bonaparte NASA Neurons Neuroplasticity Niccolo Machiaveli Nintendo (Company) Party Switching Penn itette Perception Philosophy of Language Philosophy of Law Plato. Aristotle. and Other Greek Philosophers Politically Correct Probability and Odds Propaganda Quantum Mechanics Randomness Relativity Ren\u00e9 Descartes Rock Music Role Playing Games Rome Russia Self-Help Senses Sex. Gender. and Sexuality Silicon Valley Simultaneous Discovery \u2018Small World Theory Social Contract Theory and the State of Nature Social Engineering Socialism Sound Space Spain Stanley Milgram Star Wars Stock Market synthesizers SySt@MS Thanksgiving The Beates The Dutch The Earth The Law of Attraction Theoretical Physics Theories The Universe Thomas Jefferson Tonas Paine Time Trade Truth Types of Gover