{"_key": "fashiondive", "source_key": "fashiondive", "filename": "FashionDive.png", "image_file": "FashionDive.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.3297, "s008_neutral_headlines": 0.8879, "s010_scare_quotes": 2.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 0.0, "s085_standard_sections": 4.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 17.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00273, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.5823, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.7425, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.0, "small_face_count": 0.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0484, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.355, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.227, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0128, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 2.0142, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0121, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 82.0, "footer_link_count": 119.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 2.0, "social_icon_count": 1.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 7.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 5.714, "headline_size_variance": 0.1504, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 2.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0221, "number_token_frac": 0.0332, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.2198, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.044, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.2198, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 3.6264, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.7692, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.8791}, "ocr_text": "Technology Sustainability Sourcing Coneumer Behavior : = Compliance Marketing Retail Fashion Dive will stop publishing on Aug. 30, 2025. We appreciate your readership and hope to provide you with valuable coverage from one of our other x publications, Read more from our team, Fashion Dive to stop publishing Fi TOP STORIES experience hhion Dive will cease operations. We are grateful to our readers for being with us on this journey. Read more > THE LATEST US-bound shipments restricted by postal carriers in Europe, Asia export services. @ Sourcing Al won't stop the next supply chain disruption, but it can help companies plan With the right data and tools, fashion and apparel brands can successfully mitigate pandemics, tariffs and what comes next, writes Paul F. Magel, president of Computer Generated Solutions, @ Technology Wilson CEO to step down Joe Dudy is exiting the chief executive role after spending three decades at Wilson and parent company Amer Sports. @ Brand Shein, Temu and AliExpress should be labeled \u2018notorious markets, nonprofit says The Information Technology and Innovation Foundation bought more than 50 products from the companies and said nearly half were fakes. @ Brands Adore Me founder out at Victoria's Secret & Co. Now leading the brand is Christine Vellani, who has worked in merchandising and new business atthe lingerie giant for nearly six @ Brands Caleres names new head of HR Kathleen Welter will oversee human resources for the company\u2019s portfolio of brands, including Famous Footwear, Allen Edmonds and the newly acquired Stuart Weitzman. @ Brands Claire's strikes $140M private equity takeover deal, pauses store liquidations The bankrupt tween accessories retailer had plans to shutter at least 700 stores \u2014 possibly twice that \u2014 and now most will remain open, 6 Marketing 9 summer 2025 CEO changes that shook the fashion industry Corporate transformations heated up in June and July at some of the sector\u2019 biggest firms. 4 Brand Levi's hires Victoria\u2019s Secret chief supply chain officer Chris Callieri will start in September, reporting directly to CEO Michelle Gass. porate/Finance Kenneth Cole launches men\u2019s footwear collection The Fall made through a partnership with Mare Fisher Footwear, collection includes Oxfords, boots and sneakers and is @ Brands J.C. Penney debuts Aeropostale, Hurley in fall assortment \u2018The department store will also carry exclusive designs from JS Jessica Simpson as it pushes forward a style and value brand position, @ Brand Shein\u2019s UK revenue up 32% last year The results come as the fast fashion company has been shifting its marketing spending tothe U.K. and EU after steep tariff impacts. @ Brands Asics, Clarks top StockX trend report Pop Marts Labubu collectibles also made an impact in the first half of the year, due in part to the product\u2019 blind box sales model Consumer Behavior How to win back-to-school marketing as American Eagle's big bet blows up \u2018Though spending forecasts are bleak, value-focused messaging and smart social media plays could help brands transcend the turbulence. @ Brands 5 ongoing fashion lawsuits to watch the rest of the year While some lawsuits filed in 2025 have been resolved, others are well underway, and some yearslong legal battles are continuing without resolution. Corporate/Finance EBay\u2019s pre-loved, circular runway initiative to return this September Designers Altuzarra, Erdem and Luar are participating in the Endless Runway event with archival pieces. @ Technology Wholesale, back to school propel Birkenstock in Q3 Executives called tariffs \u201cmanageable\u201d with a mix of price hikes, production efficiency and vendor negotiations, among other moves. @ Brands Coach again drives growth for Tapestry in revenue, new customers value at Kate Spade @ Brands 6 recycled material firms to watch this year So far in 2025, brands such as Lululemon and Tapestry have signed long-term partnerships with alternative material producers, @ Technology Poshmark co-founder steps away from CEO role After 15 years atthe helm, Manish Chandra will make way for an executive from Poshmark\u2019s parent company to step into the position # Corporate Gildan Activewear to buy HanesBrands for $2.2 billion The deal would nearly double Gildan\u2019s revenue, but there could be antitrust hurdles because both companies sell underwear, hosiery and shirts. 6 Brand Lilly Pulitzer announces Vintage Vault collection The limited edition line will feature archival prints and offer multiple drops of women\u2019s and girls\u2019 apparel, with the first capsule launching in August @ Brand On raises full-year outlook, shrugs off tariff impact Currency changes challenged the Swiss brand in Q2, but net sales stil rose with direct to consumer leading the way. @ Brands \u2018Temu sued for allegedly misappropriating likeness of late musician MF Doom \u2018The fast fashion giant is accused of violating trademark rights owned by the rapper's estate @ Brands Florsheim and Horween Leather release shoe collab \u2018The six-piece collection was inspired by Chicago's industrial roots and American Eagle's Travis Kelce collab extends celebrity-led marketing streak 2. Mass beauty outpaces prestige in the first half of 2025 3. Fashion licensing grew 8.1% in 2024: report 4. Urban Outfitters taps Levi's for its next On Rotation 5. Luxury jewelry sales mixed amid consumer pullback Get the free newsletter Subscribe to Fashion Dive for top news. trends & analysis LIBRARY RESOURCES \u00a9) From Automation to Connection: Balancing AI With Human-Centered Journeys why Growth Strategy Beats Product in Economic Downturns LAyB00K E]_ How to reduce fit friction and build customer lifetime value View all WHAT WE'RE READING PVH Corp. Talks Tariff Mitigation Efforts & Why Brands Started Taking TikTok Shop Seriously (% V voaue susin Would you buy a $3,000 Alo handbag? ct View all", "ocr_text_len": 5832}
