elfast: Censor First, Govern Never Cities Finally Admitting Climate Science Was Never Settled Cities Finally Admitting Climate Science Was Never Settled PLEASE SUPPORT OUR WORK \u2018There is a particular kind of embarrassment reserved for those who chain themselves to railings, glue themselves to motorways, and harangue their neighbors into submission \u2014 - only to discover, some years later, that the adults in the room were right all along, Newsletter Email New Middle East Trade Belfast: Censor First, Govern Search Corridor Emerges after Strait of Hormuz Is Closed Governments across the Middle East and beyond are accelerating efforts to develop alternative routes for energy exports and international trade. The Erasure of Whiteness Gathers Speed \u2018As we saw from the complicity of the British police in the murder of Henry Novak by an immigrant-invader, the decades of propaganda that white people are racists has been successful Israel and Lebanon Talk Amid Escalating War as the Country Faces Collapse Israel is attacking Lebanon continuously, while unarmed civilians suffer mounting deaths and injuries. America and Israel are insisting that Hezbollah be disarmed, Will Trump Kidnap Israel's President Herzog for Violating Trump's Israeli Sedition Edict? Israel's President Isaac Herzog has violated Trump's Sedition Edict that protects Israel and Jews in general from criticism. The Bomb Nobody Wants to id Berlin's AfD has called for a parliamentary inquiry into Nord Stream. The establishment parties will resist. They shouldn't. The Neocon Who Blinked For decades, Robert Kagan has been among the loudest, most relentless architects of the ideology that brought us here \u2014 the belief that American military supremacy, deployed without hesitation and without limit, could reshape the world in Washington's image. Iran\u2019s Advantage Lies Underwater While Israel and the US completely dominate the airspace over Iran - where they carry out hundreds of bombing raids daily in a so far fruitless attempt to stop Iran from firing missiles and drones - Iran has a stranglehold on the Strait of Hormuz. Iran's AD a Wounded Lion - Still Manages to Shoot Down Enemy Planes Israel and the US have carried out thousands of airstrikes against Iran and claim complete air supremacy. At the same time, the number of US fighter jets shot down has risen to the largest the US has lost in any war in decades. Irish Farmers Revolt Against Soaring Fuel Prices - Military Called In In Ireland, farmers, truckers, taxi drivers and others have responded to the rapidly rising fuel prices by blocking roads, fuel depots and the country's only oil refinery, Police were supported by the Irish Armed Forces to break the blockades. WEST MEDIA SEO and advertising aesareewestmedia.com Eitoral staff Never As Belfast is burning, the British government's first instinct is to reach not for answers, but for a muzzle. Henry Nowak - Handcuffed to Death Britain failed Henry Nowak twice: once with a knife, and once with a pair of handcuffs The Shadow Financiers of the Left Finally Exposed At long last, there are signs of real movement in the fight against the dark-money networks propping up far-left extremism. Britain Starts Buying Russian Oil again While Keir Starmer and his Labour ministers continue to talk of \u201cunwavering solidarity\" with Ukraine and the need to \u201cmake Putin pay,\u201d the British government has just surreptitiously signed a permit once again authorizing imports of Russian oil products. CIA's psyop: Operation PBSuccess and PBHistory When the US carries out regime change or color revolutions, as they are called today, psychological operations are absolutely crucial The Hidden History Behind Psyops: Creating Havoc Even Today How the globalists rule us in secret It Seems That No World Ruler Can Accept Reality or Even Is Aware of It \u2018Trump and Netanyahu are not the only politicians who have trapped themselves in a war to their electoral disadvantage. Two Centuries of British Enmity Toward Russia For 200 years, Great Britain has been among. Russia's most irreconcilable and persistent adversaries. Professional sabotage against Italian eline Aprecision sabotage attack on critical energy Infrastructure in northern Italy has crippled one of Europe's most important oil pipelines.", "ocr_text_len": 4495}
