. Full Fact uses cookies to give you the best experience on our website. Find out more about cookies. JeTeNy tl a a | Training Latest Government Tracker Explore our courses in media literacy, fact checking and data analysis. From false health claims to misleading statements on immigration, politics and conflict\u2014our expert team delivers impartial, evidence-based fact checks. Full Fact is monitoring the government's delivery on its promises _ at Policy & Impact Donate Find out how Full Fact is working with those in power to make our politics more honest and truthful As independent, impartial fact checkers, we rely on your donation to ensure our public figures and media back up claims with evidence, and correct the record when they make a mistake. Full Fact Al Full Fact Al is set of tools developed by Full Fact and used by fact checkers \u2018round the world to monitor public debate, find misinformation, and take ction, Evidence you can rely on Fact checking claims made by politicians, public figures and viral online content can give you the full picture backed by the evidence. \u2018Subscribe to weely emi newsletters from Full Fact for updates on pots immigration heath and more. Our fact checks ore free to ead but otto predce 29 ou wil olzo ge occasional emai \u2018bout undressing and other ways you can help You can unsubscribe at anytime For mre information about how we use your data see our Privacy Poy. Recent fact checks \u2018The Sunbed Association's FAQs page claims it is not true that there is no such thing as a fake tan. - anaes This is not correct, according to the NHS and a wide range of health authorities and experts. The global scientific consensus is that tanning raises the risk of cancer. This is true, but it's also already the case that the UK spends more on health and disability benefits than it does on defence. Benefits vs defence \u2018Social media posts have claimed: \u201cDorset Police announced that 44% of alleged \u2018sex offences in Dorset are carried out by \u2018asylum seekers living in asylum hotels\u201d. This is false. Dorset Police _ told us the figure was \u201cincorrect\u201d and not from them, and we could find no data backing up the stat. Asylum seeker claims Can you help us do more? Every donation will help us stop the spread of bad information. 25 BRM c20 other amount Ourimpartiality Feedback and corrections. 900 Full Foctis a registered charity (no. 1158683) ond \u00ab non-profit company (no. 06975984) limited by guarantee and registered in England and Woles. \u00a9 Copyright 2010-2026 Full Fact. Thanks to Hosting UK for donating our web hosting. Privacy, terms and conditions. Who we are Funding and independence Media enquiries FULL FACT Image courtesy of andrewrennie.", "ocr_text_len": 2903}
