{"_key": "highereddive", "source_key": "highereddive", "filename": "HigherEd_Dive.png", "image_file": "HigherEd_Dive.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.2053, "s008_neutral_headlines": 6.9644, "s010_scare_quotes": 5.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 2.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 1.0, "s085_standard_sections": 5.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 18.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00898, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.5371, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.2241, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00063, "small_face_count": 1.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0544, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.3685, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.15, "header_band_height_frac": 0.011, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 2.1582, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0124, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 59.0, "footer_link_count": 127.0, "cta_button_count": 2.0, "newsletter_box_count": 5.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 1.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 9.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 5.167, "headline_size_variance": 0.1724, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 0.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0457, "number_token_frac": 0.028, "city_or_county_in_name": 1.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.7187, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.2259, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.0, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.7721, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.1027, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.5133, "lx_local_civic_per100": 6.9815}, "ocr_text": "Deep Insights Straight to Your Inbox ( HIGHER ED DIVE Get the Free Newsletter G Hicker eo ove Deep Dive Opinion Library Events Press Releases : Finance Closures & Mergers Federal Policy State Policy Legal Leadership Students Faculty & Staff Enrollment Technology TOP STORIES changes Leadership Ledger 4, Clemson, Northwestern and other w 1. Texas Tech instruction rules spurred widespread course 2. Hampshire College may close earlier than planned 3. Hilton officially launches Undergraduate, furthering its push into college markets 4a \" presidents \u2018Don't budget off your hopes\u2019: UNT president on institutional planning 5. Tuition discount rate reaches 57% for private nonprofits, NACUBO says ina shifting world College leaders must \u201cconfront the brutal facts\u201d of their finances if they want to build resilience, warns University of North Texas President Harrison Keller. Read more > THE LATEST CHIGAS UNIVERSITY Al changes everything as Western Michigan University launches buyout program to ease budget \u2018The public institution is offering early retirements to tenured faculty as long as enough sign up to save at least $5 million. @ Finance West Point speech policies paused for civilian faculty by federal judge US. District Judge Cathy Seibel called one of the military college's rules a\u201cbroad and standardless intrusion\u201d on civilian faculty's constitutional rights. # Federal Policy California Senate passes bill that would create $12B in state research funding If enacted, the measure would establish a foundation focused on funding research areas where the federal government has cut. @ State Pokey Florida budget deal would cut extra funding to top public universities Lawmakers also agreed to transfer the University of South Florida Sarasota-Manatee campus to New College of Florida, a conservative favorite, @ Finance DOJ lawsuit accuses UCLA of ignoring antisemitism on campus \u2018The agency sued the University of California, arguing its Los Angeles campus was \u201cdeliberately indifferent\u201d to harassment of Jewish and Israeli students. @ Federal Policy How can states encourage students to fill out the FAFSA? States are adopting policies that mandate students to fill out the form, but experts say these efforts should come with funding and personnel. @ State Potcy Week in review: Should higher education be overhauled? sunsetting 21 programs to University of California faculty calling for standardized testing. regional public university SUNY Fredonia cutting 14 degrees, 7 minors \u2018The public institution is still trying to close a multimillion-dollar deficit after years of enrollment declines. @ Finance Warren requests GAO investigation into Education Department layoffs Sen. Elizabeth Warren asked the government watchdog to probe if employee reductions in the Federal Student Aid office have lessened college oversight. @ Federal Policy \u2018TRACKER Here's a list of the biggest donations to colleges in 2026 so far We're keeping tabs on gifts and commitments of $100 million or more made to higher education institutions. @ Finance Higher education must be rebuilt to restore public trust. Here\u2019s how. Pressure mounts for Education Department to release research funds \u2018The US. Department of Education says it will meet its statutory obligations for funding, but lawmakers say nearly $300 million is still unspent. @ Federal Policy Education Department proposal would erode student protections, critics warn \u2018They praised some regulatory proposals that would require programs to pass an earnings test but said others would weaken the gainful employment rule. @ Federal Policy UT System makes it easier to shutter programs, fire faculty Under rules passed by the system's board, university presidents can axe programs without faculty input and cut professors with limited appeal avenues. @ State Poicy Baldwin Wallace University winds down 16 degree programs, 19 minors \u2018The Ohio private nonprofit\u2019 president said he wants to invest the savings in areas with high student and workforce demand, @ Finance States sue over Education Department\u2019s professional student definition \u2018The lawsuit contends that the agency imposed requirements not found in statute that limit federal loan access for graduate nursing and other fields. @ Federal Policy Entry-level productivity expectations have increased due to AI, report says Nearly a third of HR professionals told D2L. they're hiring fewer early career workers and using artificial intelligence to fil in the gaps. @ Students Stuart Bell named sole finalist for University of Florida president A search panel praised his decade-long tenure at the University of Alabama, but some influential conservatives have criticized his past diversity efforts. @ Leadership University of Michigan poised to buy campus of downsized Lutheran college Nearly two years after Concordia University Ann Arbor moved to fold most of its programs, it's looking to sell real estate for $60 million, @ Finance Education Department releases final rule for Workforce Pell \u2018The regulations detail the process for how short-term programs can get approval from the federal government to be eligible for Pell Grants @ Federal Policy DOL rescinds Biden-era overtime rule, formalizing return to 2019 salary threshold \u2018The salary threshold is only part of the exemption test, one attorney reminded HR leads. Get the free newsletter Subscribe to Higher Ed Dive for top news, trends & analysis MOST POPULAR Hampshire College may A FERS close cartier than planned Clemson, Northwestern and other universities welcome new presidents Tuition discount rate reaches 57% for private nonprofits, NACUBO says Hilton officially launches Undergraduate, furthering its push into college markets LIBRARY RESOURCES 1 AYB00K [E]_ How institutions Can Turn Affordability Into an Opportunity \u20ac e How campus facilities are meeting modern challenges View all COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS Enflux Launches Accreditation Intelligence\u2122 for Physician Assistant Programs \u2018The American University of Paris Board of Trustees Announces Leadership Transition DeVry University and StraighterLine Expand Partnership to Make Higher Education More Accessibl... Edvisor.ai Closes $1.3M Pre-Seed Led by Draper Associates View all | Post a press release WHAT WE'RE READING cin NC megachurch launching college 2 INA PUBLIC PRESS Gwe cxzer University of Iowa eliminates 80 graduate jobs @ THE HanvaRO CRIMSON FAS To Lay Off High-Level Administrators in Staff Restructuring (2 View all EVENTS: View all | Promote an event INDUSTRY INTEL Lessons from a Campus Dining Leader: Cost, Students, and Smarter Procurement", "ocr_text_len": 6591}
