{"_key": "k12dive", "source_key": "k12dive", "filename": "K-12_Dive.png", "image_file": "K-12_Dive.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 1.3258, "s008_neutral_headlines": 4.1555, "s010_scare_quotes": 6.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 1.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 1.0, "s085_standard_sections": 6.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 25.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00486, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.4878, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.4897, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00013, "small_face_count": 1.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0561, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.3342, "content_column_count": "2", "side_margin_frac": 0.145, "header_band_height_frac": 0.011, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 2.5854, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0207, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 56.0, "footer_link_count": 136.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 2.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 12.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 4.368, "headline_size_variance": 0.1918, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 0.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0466, "number_token_frac": 0.0266, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.2841, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.322, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.0, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0947, "lx_question_style_per100": 3.5038, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.1894, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.3788, "lx_local_civic_per100": 5.1136}, "ocr_text": "The Better Way To Buy Office Furniture. Deep Dive Opinion Library Events Press Releases nove : == Policy & Legal Leadership Curriculum Special Education School Models Technology Professional Development Pre-K & Early Childhood TOP STORIES 1. Supreme Court turns away another parental notification case 2. How should school leaders react to controversial student journalism? 3. Philadelphia Phillies to give students inside look at ballpark operations TRACKER 4. As student enrollment declines, a look at public school closures A snapshot of private school trends in 4 charts 5. Screen time limits call for nuance, disability advocates say Enrollment is stable at independent schools as public and private schools face a shrinking student population and increased competition to fill seats. Read more > THE LATEST \u2018COLUMN 1 STAFFED UP Education is no longer a \u2018professional degree.\u2019 What will the ripple effects be? Education advocates are worried about the negative impact a new federal student loan cap will have on staffing for many roles in schools @ Policy & Legal School meal participation at risk from SNAP cuts, FRAC reports Participation in SNAP has fallen by some 3.3 million people in the last year as a new federal law tightened eligibility, data shows. @ Policy & Legal Week In Review: Federal policies and classroom tech face pushback We're rounding up last week's news, from special education data collections to Pittsburgh\u2019s school closures. @ Policy & Legal Pittsburgh Public Schools OKs plan to close 12 schools \u2018The districts Future Ready Plan includes opening two new schools and enhancing access to academics, arts, athletics and more @ Policy & Legal OF | Feeraee The Better Way To Buy Office Furniture. Ed Dept wants to end some IDEA data collections. How did stakeholders respond? Special education and disability groups pushed back against the plan to drop certain data collections tracking racial disparities. Special Education How can states encourage students to fill out the FAFSA? States are embracing policies that mandate or strongly encourage students to fill out the form. Experts say these moves need funding and personnel. @ Policy & Legal AFT president urges bans on screens, student-facing AI for youngest learners Randi Weingarten, president of the nation\u2019s second largest teachers union, said such limits are needed as students are \u201cdrowning in tech. @ Policy & Legal Por aurz Test yourself on the past week's K-12 news From unspent federal funds to an American Federation of Teachers proposal, what did you learn from our recent stories? @ Policy & Legal GOP advances legislation barring \u2018discriminatory equity or gender ideology\u2019 \u2018The bills would codify parts of Trump executive orders that restrict classroom discussions and materials related to LGBTQ+ identities and @ Policy & Legal How the Canvas data breach further frayed families\u2019 trust in ed tech Cybersecurity incidents like the one that hit Instructure threaten the faith placed in schools to protect children and their data, says a leading expert. @ Policy & Legal Teachers lack formal AI guidance for learning and instruction, Gallup finds \u2018Teachers in higher-needs schools were less likely than those in wealthier schools to have received guidelines, echoing previous research, @ Curriculum Don't call it a \u2018miracle\u2019: Mississippi academic gains were fueled by decades of groundwork \u2018The state's marked improvement required more of a marathon than a sprint and cant be chalked up to a single approach, researchers say. @ Policy & Legal Project-based learning is for physical education, too From \u201cbrain boost\u201d videos to creating games from scratch, a \u2018Wisconsin P.E. teacher shares how projects engage his elementary students, @ Curriculum Pressure mounts for Ed Dept to release research funds Nearly $300 million is unspent, according to letters to the Education Department. The agency says it will meet its statutory obligations for funding. # Policy & Legal STUDY HALL What you need to know about charter schools Charter school growth may be slowing but because ofits flexibility and autonomy, it remains a popular school model @ Policy & Legal Week In Review: The latest large district to weigh school closures # Policy & Legal Ed Dept spending priority raises concerns with nod to Judeo-Christianity \u2018The inclusion of \u201cthe founders\u2019 religious beliefs\u201d in discretionary grant priorities comes amid a focus on \u201cpromoting patriotic education. @ Policy & Legal Surgeon general advisory urges caution on youth screen use \u2018The advisory was accompanied by a toolkit calling for schools to \u201climit screen use by assigning work in books or on paper whenever possible. @ Policy & Legal Louisiana 2nd state approved for ESEA funding waiver While the state wants to direct cost savings to priority areas, some have concerns about the waivers\u2019 impacts on vulnerable student populations. @ Leadership 12.6M kids lack access to summer programming Cost, transportation and availability are barriers to these programs despite strong interest from families, an Afterschool Alliance report finds. @ School Models National Assessment Governing Board to restore previously cut NAEP exams In addition to restoring state-level 12th grade reading and math tests in 2032, it will also make more data available for states in certain subjects and grades. @ Curriculum OF Riso The Better Way To Buy Office Furniture. Get the free newsletter Subscribe to K-12 Dive for top news, trends & analysis MOST POPULAR Screen time limits call for nuance, disability advocates say School meal participation at risk from SNAP cuts, FRAC reports leaders react to controversial student journalism? A snapshot of private school trends in 4 charts 9 FNL) How should school ee LIBRARY RESOURCES E]_ The Hidden Cost of Fragmented Payment Systems using a1 To Build College & Career Writing Readiness in K- 2 EI strategic Approach to Modernizing Public Infrastructure COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS Shmoop renews Utah statewide ACT prep contract and expands to AP, ASVAB prep InfoCase and Refreshed Tech Partner to Launch Guaranteed Buyback Program for K-12 Devices ClassDojo Expands Tutoring as Schools Face Ongoing Learning Gaps Foxborough Public Schools Sees 14- Point Increase in School Safety Perceptions, Outpacing Natio. View all | Post a press release WHAT WE'RE READING & coor: Four years later, Colorado's free school meals program is finally delivering money for cafeteria workers (4 Another Houston-area school district is consolidating special education programs for the upcoming school year ic} a Gov. Landry asks lawmakers to pull $168M from school districts for teacher pay EVENTS. 18 Empower Your Teaching: JUN Harness the Power of Assessment Data View all | Promote an event INDUSTRY INTEL How K-12 School Systems Across the Country are Transitioning to Paper-free Student Lifecycle Solutions Protecting Our Students: School Safety \u2018Technology and Alyssa\u2019s Law Updates", "ocr_text_len": 6935}
{"_key": "justfacts", "source_key": "justfacts", "filename": "Just_Facts.png", "image_file": "Just_Facts.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.6548, "s008_neutral_headlines": 1.5866, "s010_scare_quotes": 2.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 2.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 6.0, "s085_standard_sections": 8.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 22.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00347, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.4633, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.6702, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00026, "small_face_count": 1.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0821, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.1215, "content_column_count": "2", "side_margin_frac": 0.365, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0127, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "orange", "accent_color_count": 2.4951, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0211, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 86.0, "footer_link_count": 250.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 1.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 4.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 4.889, "headline_size_variance": 0.2653, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 0.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0174, "number_token_frac": 0.0121, "city_or_county_in_name": 1.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 1.1524, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0838, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.0, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0524, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.1572, "lx_question_style_per100": 4.3478, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.4191, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.9429, "lx_local_civic_per100": 2.2525}, "ocr_text": "JUSTFACTS. SEIZE THE DATA Latest Howe \u2018sour us imaves canes JUST FACTS DALY oE0s PACT APP LUST ACTS ACADEMY Learn the facts. Decide for yourself. Abortion Free Speech Income, Wealth & Poverty Sex Trafficking Constitution Global Warming Monetary Policy Social Security Crime Government Spending National Debt Social Spending Death Penalty Gun Control Pollution Taxes Education Health Care Population Unions Energy Immigration. Racial Issues United Nations Latest Core Research & Studies Crime Ifyou want to acquire a wide and deep understanding of the prevalence and impacts of violent crimes, white-collar crimes, sex crimes, property crimes, drug crimes, and the U.S. justice system, this research provides all that and more. Such serious topics demand serious facts, and Just Facts delivers them with candor, clarity, and accuracy. Healthcare Healthcare is a deeply personal matter, but it has increasingly become the public's business by way of numerous laws and regulations. Furthermore, these laws and regulations have \u2018transformed healthcare into a complex and divisive issue. Thus, if you want to truly understand this vital subject, you will need a firm foundation of facts, which is exactly what this research provides. National Debt Slice through the partisan rhetoric that clouds the heated debate about the national debt by \u2018consulting Just Facts\u2019 research on this issue. Documented with primary sources such as the US. Treasury Department and the Financial Accounting Standards Board, this research provides voters, lawmakers, and policy analysts with data that is critical to understanding this important mater. Education \u2018The Greek philosopher Epictetus said that \u201conly the educated are free,\u201d and Booker T, Washington trusted in \u201cthe power and influence\u201d of facts. Just Facts has united both of these precepts in its research on education. Learn about the tangible outcomes and costs of preschool, K-12 education, higher education, and initiatives like Common Core, school choice, and digital learning, Monetary Policy Everyone uses money, and monetary policy influences the value of that money for borrowers, lenders, savers, and spenders alike, Just Facts has produced research to illuminate {his complicated issue in clear, simple terms. These fats walk you through the evolution of \u2018money from seashells to Bitcoin and answer vexing questions about the Federal Reserve, inflation, exchange rates, and other topics Income, Wealth & Poverty Just Facts has completed a massive research project on income, wealth, and poverty to empower you with crucial facts abou life-changing economic issues. These facts speak to vital questions like: How are poor, middle income, and wealthy Americans faring? What is the gender wage gap? How does government spending and corruption financially impact you? How do US. living standards stack up agains the rest ofthe world? Voter Registration by Non-Citizens \u2018Based on the latest data and an enhanced version ofa stresstested methodology from a scholarly journal, about 10% to 27% of non-citizen adults in the U.S. are now illegally registered to vote, These rats are potentially high enough oovertum the will ofthe \u2018American people in major elections. Sex Trafficking This research may shock, sadden, or infurate you, but most importantly, it wll equip you \u2018ith information that you can use to inform yourself and others about the crime of sex tnalficking. Knowledge is power, and whether you are a private citizen or law enforcement profesional, this knowledge may help you save someone from crue] and unrelenting abuse Immigration Immigration isa defining element ofthe United States, but political agendas, media bias, and personal passions have sown a minefield of misinformation around this issue, That's \u2018where Just Facts steps in. This expansive research will help you become genuinely informed about a subject that has high stakes for America and people throughout the world. Energy The topic of energy is incredibly wide-ranging and inticat, but Just Facts has condensed reams of data on ol, solr, natural ga, biofuels coal, wind, and ober energy sources o help you develop practical knowledge about them. This research will empower you to dcover the pros and cons of different forms of energy and to understand the effect of energy policies on everyday people Survey of Voter Knowledge If there is truth in James Madison's waming that an uninformed cletorate would be a grave threat tothe nation, a scientific survey commissioned by Just Facts shows thatthe US. may be in deep trouble. This unique assessment measured voters\u2019 knowledge of issues that tangibly affect their ives, and it found tat many voters may be casting ballots based on \u2018warped notions of reality Gun Control Does increased government control of firearms lead to a more civilized, less violent society; \u2018oF does it leave law-abiding citizens at the mercy of violent criminals? Is the Second Amendment applicable to citizens or only tothe National Guard? Do we need stricter gun control laws or more enforcement of existing laws? Examine this large collection of facts that speak to these important questions. Masks Despite the fog of contradictory claims and changing government guidelines about masks, dozens of scientific journals have published remarkably consistent data about this issue. However, government officials and big tech executives have repeatedly corrupted and \u2018suppressed such data. The impacts of this extend far beyond the issue of masks and have caused widespread harm and countless deaths. Living Standards in the U.S. Versus Other Countries \u2018A groundbreaking study by Just Facts has discovered that after accounting forall income, charity, and non-cash welfare benefits like subsidized housing and Food Stamps\u2014the poorest 20% of Americans consume more goods and services than the national averages for all people in most affluent countries. Government Spending Given the scale and diversity of federal, state, and local government functions, it can be hard to grasp the big picture of how they spend taxpayer\u2019s money. This gives politicians and activists ample opportunity to distort or distract fom reality, Just Facts\u2019 core research on government spending sa strong antidote to the basless claims, half-truths, and outright falschoods that plague debates abou such matter. Death Penalty Societies have long used the death penalty as a punishment for heinous crimes, but in the \u2018modem era, many people would prefer to abandon it. Debate over such a life-or-death issue \u2018can be clouded by emotion, thus leaving people conflicted and confused. This research \u2018examines the death penalty from a factual perspective to help you develop a foundation of truth from which to form your views. United Nations In the wake of World War II, the United Nations was created to save future generations from the \u201cscourge of war.\u201d Over 70 years later, many people wonder whether itis a bloated \u2018bureaucracy or an effective mechanism for world peace and development. This research cuts through the rhetoric to provide you with the facts about the organization's goals, structure, \u2018rack record, and much more, Freedom of Speech Through much of recorded history, governments have used their power to suppress criticism of themscves. In stark contrast, one of the defining principles of the US. is tha citizens have a right wo criticize the government and to speak about virally everything, Discover \u2018why this came to be and how it plays out in rel lif. Population Human population has tripled since 1950, adding 5 billion people tothe planet. Some say this is very serious and must be corrected immediately to prevent a disaster. Others say al is well and thre is nothing to fear. What do the facts say? Read onto find out how we got 10 this poin, what the effets have been, and what the future might hold I Racial Issues (n this emotionally charged subject where so many people have based ther opinions on fiction from reality. The result is hundreds of facts that shed broad light on matters that could ea notions and prejudices, Just Facts has conducted thorough and extensive research to separate \u2019 bbe uniting instead of dividing people. Essential Facts About Covid-19 Given the spread of misinformation about Covid-19, Just Facts is providing a trove of rigorously documented facts about this disease and its impact fact that have been absent or misreported in much of the media's coverage of this isve. This research also includes a study to determine the deadiness of Covid-19 based on the most comprehensive available measure \u2018These include some vital Unions Regardless of whether or not you belong to a union, they can have tangible and pronounced effects on you. Labor unions in private companies and government affect not only workers and managers but also product prices, tax levels, the general economy, and more. Learn how and why in Just Facts\u2019 scrupulously documented trove of union facts. Taxes \u2018The US. tax system is so complicated that federal tax regulations now strech for nearly 14,000 pages. But even if you studied every word of these, you still wouldn't lear how taxes truly impact individuals, families, and businesses. For that, you'll need Just Facts? cutting-edge research on tax policy. For every major aspect of this issue, you'll find clear, reliable, and rigorously documented facts here. Pollution How much pollution exists in our ar, water, and land\u2014and just how hazardous is it? Answers to these questions often vary across a wide range of extremes; some say there i no cause for concem, while others say we ae in or on the verge ofan environmental | catastrophe. That is why Just Facts has conducted research to help you sort through the hyperbole that permeates this issue Global Warming The issu of climate change has become a contentious minefield of claims and counterclaims, but Just Facts has diligently researched and sorted through this muddle to bring you the concrete facts of the matter. This research provides an abundance of credible information tha transcends the half-truths that dominate ths highly contested topic. Social Security Learn how Social Security operates, the state of it fiscal health, the scope of its benefits, the S history of its tax increases, and much more through Just Facts\u2019 latest research on this topic. As always, this eye-opening research is accompanied by the comprehensive documentation tha separates Just Facts from typical news coverage. Abortion Abortion\u2014the mere mention of this word stirs passions and controversy, but what are the concrete facts of this issue? What do the scientific disciplines tell us? Where do prominent politicians and organizations stand on this matter? More importantly, what are their records? Just Facts has amassed a wealth of meticulously documented facts to help you answer these questions, Social Spending During the past century, vernment social programs\u2014which provide healthcare, income security, education, nuttin, housing, and cultural servces\u2014have grown from a small portion of all goverment spending to the largest share of it. Explore striking fact that document the measures, trends, and history of these programs. Constitution of the United States \u2018The U.S. Constitution is the longest-standing written constitution of all nations in the world, and many other countries have copied its provisions into their constitutions. Learn how and, \u2018why this ground-breaking document was developed and read it along with the Bill of Rights \u2018and all other amendments since the birth of the United States. Just Facts | 3600 FM 1488 Rd. | Suite 120 #248 | Conroe, TX 77384 | Contact Us| Careers Copyright \u00a9 2026 Just Facts. Al rights reserved. Just Facts is a nonprofit 501(c)3 organization. Information provided by Just Facts isnot legal, tax, or investment advice. justfacts.com | justfactsdaly.com CS) JUST FACTS Videos DONATE racre! How do | know these facts are reliable and comprehensive? CITED WORLDWIDE STAY AHEAD OF THE SPIN Enter your era to receive new research enter PRIVACY POUCY", "ocr_text_len": 12039}
