0 + an. 2, 2026 unsuccessfully running for a state senate seat. @ evrnare chan \u00abaun 2, 2026, 3:48 pm \u2018Weekly Highlights, Top Stories and Local Happenings \u2018Stay informed about Southern Colorado news and community events with KRCC's Weekly Digest, delivered to your inbox on Friday mornings. (CPR thanks our sponsors. Nee Noshe Reservoir north of Lamar is drying out Colorado Parks and Wildlife has declared a public fish salvage in the lake north of Lamar. @ evancie chan \u00absun 2, 2028 MmurTaRY to Colorado Springs The facility, one of four to be constructed in the U.S., will be built at Schriever Space Force Base. @\u00ae oan Boyce + 3un.2, 2026 ants At Colorado Springs Fine Arts Center, \u2018yard art\u2019 becomes a window into identity, access and power Yard art might bring to mind garden gnomes or painted rocks, but anew exhibit at the Fine Arts Center at Colorado College asks visitors to look deeper. Vance tells Air Force Academy graduates to prepare for entirely new era of warfare More than 900 cadets graduated Thursday, now commissioned as officers in the Air and Space Forces. austice Federal prosecutors still weighing death penalty for Boulder firebomber Mohamed Soliman's family is appealing a deportation order and his lawyers say they need to stay in the U.S. to testify at any future trial @ eatison sherry \u00bb may. 29, 2026 ENVIRONMENT US. Supreme Court settles long-running water dispute over dwindling Rio Grande The settlement calls for reducing groundwater pumping along the New Mexico. 4% By The Associated Press - May. 28, 2026 The view of Pikes Peak from the new Tava House in auntie at Stix and Soul in Colorado Springs \u2018The new soul food restaurant at the Citadel Mall is on the western side of the mall. ENVIRONMENT \u2018Water in seasonal creek at Great Sand Dunes National Park down to roughly 5 percent of normal Medano Creek typically reaches peak flow around Memorial Day through early June. ausrice DNA research identifies nine more bodies in Pueblo mortuary case At least two dozen decomposing bodies were found at Davis Mortuary last summer. @ vv 00n yee + may 21,2026 Park: Running the lift and fixing the nonprofit\u2019s status Panadero Ski Corporation ran the lift for paying customers at Cuchara for the first time in decades and also had to contend with reinstating its previously revoked 501(c)3 status. 1% By shanna Lewis May. 22, 2026 New $250 million Space Force operations facility coming dwindling river and retiring water rights from irrigated farmland in southern Woodland Park is better than your view. Plus, feel like an It was a busy winter for volunteers at Cuchara Mountain KRCC's New Home KRCC and Colorado Public Radio recently transformed a building in downtown Colorado Springs into a state- of-the-art space. Learn more about the \u2018Southern Colorado Public Media Center. Sign Up For Our Newsletters Our newsletters bring you a closer look at the Southern Colorado stories that affect you and the music that inspires you. \u00a9 Sign Up For KRCC's Weekly Newsletter \u00a9 Sign Up For ANewsletter From The Climate Team Listen to a Colorado Postcard wach fa \u201ctit Colorado Postcards are in HAEME snapshots of our colorful state in sound. They give brief insights into our people and places, our flora and fauna, and our past and present, rom every corner of Colorado. Listen now. Excerpts from StoryCorps \u2018StoryCorps visited Colorado Springs for the month of June 2023 to record stories from members of the community KRCC is airing excerpts of some of the interviews on the radio. Listen to the stories and see photos of the storytellers. COLORADO COLLEGE E Colorado Public Radio \u2018News That Matters, Delivered To Your Inbox Colorado Public Radio. Al Rights Reserve. Privacy Policy. Sign Up For Our Newsletters Our newsletters bring you a closer look at the Southern Colorado stories that affect you and the music that inspires you. + KRCC's Weekly Newsletter \u2018+ ANewsletter From The Climate Team Listen", "ocr_text_len": 4103}
