ship and hope to provide you with valuable coverage from one of our other x publications, Read more from our team, TOP STORIES Dems ask SEC, DOL to not issue anti-ESG rules: Exclusive 2. Pactiv Evergreen settles for $6.25M over 2023 North Carolina mill closure \u2018OPINION 3. What businesses should know about consent rules when calling consumers Legal Dive to stop publishing On Feb. 22,2025, Legal Dive will stop publishing. We hope our daily 5, In broad sweep, EEOC moves to abandon its pending gender coverage of the legal space was helpful to you. Read more > identity bias lawsuits 4, Trump order tightens White House grip on Fed, SEC THE LATEST Ties DEEP Dive DEI attacks are likely to refine and improve programs, experts say \u2018The intense pressure to end diversity initiatives has led companies to scrutinize their policies. Many of the attacks will end up strengthening DEI programs, @ Hicing/Talen Judge halts CFPB firings Inthe same order, the bureau was told not to delete any agency data or transfer its reserve funding to the Fed or anywhere else. The CFPB then reportedly placed most employees on administrative leave. @ Laweuits and Litigation Comcast-NBCUniversal faces FCC probe over \u2018invidious\u2019 DEI policies The agency's new chairman says he\u2019s concerned the cable TY, network and theme park operator continues to promote diversity, equity and inclusion. @ Compliance Federal judge sides with Biden Labor Dept. on ESG fiduciary rule Texas Northern District Court judge said the rule is stil valid under Loper Bright and does not violate the Employment Retirement Income Security Act of 1974, @ Lawsuits and Litigation The SEC has requested to delay climate rule arguments. What's next? Sustainable investing experts are not surprised by the delay and say it is expected to have minimal immediate impact, @ Laweuits and Ligation Wells Fargo faces labor board complaint over union vote \u2018The National Labor Relations Board alleged the lender threatened and retaliated against workers in favor of unionization ata California branch, @ HicingyTatent Executive's failed severance pay lawsuit sought to \u2018change\u2019 ERISA\u2019s rules, 6th Circuit says \u201cTop hat plans\u201d \u2014 like the one at issue in the case \u2014 are not subject to ERISA fiduciary requirements, per the judgment. @ Lawsuits and Ligation Ex-FDIC official McKernan tapped to lead CFPB \u2018The development came on a day when the bureau terminated roughly 70 probationary employees, including enforcement division attorneys, according to Bloomberg Law. @ Hring/Taten Accenture rolls back DEI goals to comply with Trump\u2019s EOs CEO Julie Sweet said the company would end its employee diversity representation goals and put \u201ca greater focus on inclusion and a sense of belonging for al.\u201d @ Hcing/Totent Trump pauses DOJ enforcement of law banning bribes to foreign officials \u2018The administration says the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act is overenforced and harms U.S. companies\u2019 competitiveness against international rivals @ Compliance CFPB\u2019s enforcement, supervision chiefs step down \u2018The moves come after the bureau's new leaders issued stop-work orders - and threatened personnel action in cases of, insubordination.\u201d @ Hiring Totent Conservative groups file EEOC charge over American Bar Association's diversity clerkship \u2018The allegations come amid a swift restructuring of the agency under President Donald Trump. @ Hicing/Talent Acting SEC Chair asks court not to schedule climate rule arguments \u201cThe Commission's briefs previously submitted in the cases consolidated in the Fighth Circuit do not reflect my views,\u201d Acting Chair Mark Uyeda said. @ Laweuits and Litigation Employer allegedly created \u2018exculpatory paper trail\u2019 to justify firing pregnant HR employee \u2018The lack of documented discipline against the employee before she disclosed her pregnancy raised a trial question over the true reason she was fired, the court said. @ Hiring Totent Black workers and workers with disabilities are seeking flexible jobs in record numbers More workers want fully remote jobs or \u201cfully flexible hours,\u201d allowing them to choose when their workdays begin and end, according toa Flexa report. @ HringTotent \u2018Piston Shielding your organization from AI- related liability \u2018There are some basic building blocks to ensure your insurance strategy is adequate. Emerging Issues CFPB\u2019s future hangs in the balance after a wild weekend Headquarters-based staff will work remotely this week after a new acting chief halted agency supervision and enforcement and told the Fed he wouldn't take any unappropriated funding next quarter, Emerging Issues Wave of GC and CLO retirements continues, BarkerGilmore says @ Hiring/Tatent Judge temporarily blocks Trump\u2019s early resignation offer to feds \u2018The US. District Court for the District of Massachusetts will hear additional arguments in a lawsuit brought by federal labor unions on Monday, Feb. 10. @ Hcing/Talent Publishing giants sue Idaho over state law enabling book bans @ Lawsuits and Ligation Former energy drink VP pleads guilty to insider trading The ex-finance executive made $1.6 million trading on non-public data starting three days after he left Celsius Holdings, federal prosecutors alleged. @ Loweuits and Litigation DeepSeek surge hits companies, posing security risks \u2018The Trump administration is scrutinizing the Al app, Italy and Taiwan have banned it, and companies have blocked it. \u2018Pinion DOJ\u2019s rental price-fixing suit is following a misguided path Regulators would like to think that RealPage\u2019s price suggestions are rate mandates, but they only speak to a hypothetical price status at a given point in time. Get the free newsletter Subscribe to Legal Dive for top news, trends & analysis LIBRARY RESOURCES [El] How to manage the complex issues of online age verification E]_ How to Reduce Redaction Risks With Automation El Generative At Adoption: A Guide for Legal Teams and Lawyers to Get Started View all WHAT WE'RE READING @ Lawcou Succeeding as the First General Counsel for a Startup % Ba \u2018Trump's Independent Agency Order Strikes at Model Congress Made \u00a9 conronare counse Outside Counsel Urging Employers to Keep Trans Protections in Place (4 View all EVENTS: View all", "ocr_text_len": 6411}
