e top 7% of households in income, particularly because they were far more expensive than conventional vehicles inthe same classes. Those folks had al the conventional vehicles they wanted Discover more political > Newspaper Subscriptions > Books & Literature > California\u2019s privileges for LGBT utility contractors shred the Constitution \u2018American Thinker, by Don Brown Original Artie Poated by Hazyanas 6721/2026 6:24:39 AM Past Reply California's Public Utilities Commission is pressuring the state's regulated utilities \u2014 PG&E, Southern California Edison, SoCalGas, and others \u2014 to steer roughly $633 million in annual procurement toward businesses cetfied as \u201cLGBT-owned.\u201d Under General Order 156, as expanded by Assembly Bill 1678 in 2014 and given numerical targets in a 2022 CPUC decision, large utilities must pursue aspirational goals of 1.5 percent of their spending with firms atleast S1 percent owned and controlled by lesbian, gay, bisexual, oF transgender individuals. To qualify, owners must submit documentation through the Supplier Clearinghouse proving their sexual orientation or gender identity \u2014 letters from LGBT organizations, personal references attesting to orientation, \u201cTrump: \u2018Years in Jail!) US. Pa Police Arrest Multiple People over Reflecting Pool Vandalism dan Original Article 217026618332 AM Post Reply Trump posted on Truth Social: The United States Park Police have arrested multiple individuals for vandalizing our Nations magnificent Reflecting Pool. Who would do such a thing? These are very serious crimes having to do with the destruction of National Monuments. Years in jail! Work will begin immediately on its repair. President DJT Trump said Friday his administration had \u201ccleaned, renovated, and beautified over 45 Monuments and Memorials, 8 Statues, and 22 Fountains in Washington, DC,\u201d but added that there had been \u201creal problems with Vandalism\u201d at the Reflecting Pool Iran Claims It Is Closing Strait of Hormuz Over Israeli Strikes on Lebanon Breitbart News, by Ezabeth Weel Original ticle Posted by Eb ight \u2014 621/2026 6:12:06 AM Past Rely Ina statement, the IRGC Navy \u201cwarned ships not to approach the waterway,\u201d adding that the ships\u2019 \u201csafety \u2018would be at risk if they did so,\u201d NBC News reported. \u201cIran's top joint military command\u201d explained that the closing ofthe Strait of Hormuz was in response to \u201cbreaches of commitments by\u201d the United States and Israel, according tothe outlt-In response to the statement from the IRGC, Capt. Tim Hawkins, who serves as a spokesperson for the U.S. Central Command, explained that Iran did \u201cnot control\u201d the strait,\"Iran does not control the Strait of Hormuz,\u201d Hawkins said, \u201cTraffic continues to flow, DHS: \u2018Record High\u2019 Deportations Under Trumy Breitbart News, by Llzabeth Weibel Original ticle Posted by EDRight \u2014 621/2026 6:08:50 AM \"Post Reply \u201cDEPORTATION FLIGHTS AT A RECORD HIGH,\u201d DHS wrote in a post on X, replying toa postin which the Washington Examiner shared that nearly 900,000 illegal aliens have been deported since the star ofthe Trump administration in January 2025. DHS added thatthe American people gave the Trump administration a \u201cmandate to arrest and remove criminal illegal aliens,\u201d adding that under President Donald Trump and DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin the agency would \u201ccontinue to deliver.\u201d What RFK Jr, Missed \u2018American Thinker, by Joan Swiesky Orginal Article Poated by EbRight-\u2014 621/2026 6:01:51 AM Pot Reply AU 72, Robet F. Kennedy, Jr. isan impressively educated environmental lawyer, author, aggressive activist on vaccines, citc ofthe pharmaceutical and food industries, anda lifetime political activist, many of whose credentials \u2014 particularly his creative thinking \u2014 appealed to President Trump, who nominated im to be Secretary of Health and Human Services. Of 