ulet\u2019s $59M trade secret verdict against EOFlow Grail executives were upbeat on study results for the Galleri multi- cancer early detection test, while ASCO said more evidence is needed befor THE LATEST s incorporated into screening guidelines. Read more> California attorney general sues over 23andMe data breach \u2018The attorney general said the civil penalties could add up to \u201cmultiple millions\u201d if the suit is successful. @ Dignostis J&J recalls Impella heart pumps after patient dies Johnson & Johnson asked customers to quarantine and return affected products. A spokesperson said J&J conducted quality system audits as part of its integration of Abiomed that resulted in some field actions. @ FDA Siemens Healthineers, AiM team up; Procept completes study enrollment Siemens Healthineers\u2019 MRI scanners would guide robotic neurosurgeries performed with AiMs platform. Elsewhere, Procept finished enrollment in a study of its aquablation -atment in prostate Clinical Tals Oura to add blood pressure feature following FDA policy change The new wellness tool would alert users to signs of increasing blood pressure, Oura is studying a separate feature to flag hypertension that, \u2018would go through the Food and Drug Administration, @ Digital Heath Cornerstone earns Europe's CE mark for surgical robot CE mark certification comes after Hong Kong-based Cornerstone Robotics raised $200 million in November to accelerate its global expansion, Medical Devices Abbott receives CE mark for dual glucose- ketone sensor Abbott's first dual-analyte sensor comes as competitors are working to develop their own versions of the technology. @ Diabetes Alin medtech is booming. Track new devices here. \u2018The Food and Drug Administration has authorized more medical devices that incorporate artificial intelligence. Keep track of the latest developments in this database. onl Insulet recalls 7M patch pumps due to leak risk @ Recalls J&J\u2019s DePuy Synthes inks deal to buy orthopedic surgery tech \u2018The acquisition is the latest in a series of agreements between DePuy \u2018Synthes and organizations associated with entrepreneur St\u00e9phane Lavall\u00e9e. @ Maa Dexcom warns of scrapped glucose sensors being resold Dexcom has identified two lots of G7 sensors that have been stolen, sold and used by customers. # Recalls Olympus expands in cancer tech with $270M buy of BioProtect BioProtect\u2019s balloon spacer device separates the prostate from other structures during cancer radiation, o Maa J&J corrects Impella controller over issue linked to 2 injuries, 1 death \u2018The controller can stop for about 35 seconds, during which time the patient is unsupported by the heart pump. @ FDA Beta Bionics to launch its first insulin patch pump to compete with Insulet \u2018The device called Mint, which would work with the company\u2019s adaptive insulin dosing algorithm, is expected to debut in the first half of 2027. @ Diabetes Oura files for IPO amid healthcare push \"The smart ring maker's filing follows a recent $900 million fundraise and comes amid plans to develop more health features for the device. # Digital Heath Medtronic to create European software hub in Ireland \u2018The investment in cardiac digital health will add 85 jobs initially, with more growth expected over the next three years. @ Cardiac Intuitive readies 100 updates and improvements for da Vinci 5 Some updates to Intuitive\u2019s surgical robot aim to improve communication between remote and on-site physicians to expand education opportunities. Medical Devices Sentante lands Europe's CE mark for endovascular robot \u2018The Lithuania-based robotic surgery company is advancing a remote stroke system that was accepted into the FDA's total product life cycle advisory program earlier this year. 1 Medical Devices Medtronic to buy SPR Therapeutics for about $650M Medtronic would gain a treatment for chronic pain management in its third major acquisition this year. eo Maa Stryker\u2019s chief accounting officer to retire William Berry Jr. will retire in September, with Corporate Controller Emily Baculik stepping into the role. @ Earnings Guardant wins FDA approval for updated liquid biopsy \u2018The company could secure a higher price for the new test than for its older, narrower product, Wal Street analysts said. @ FDA Medtronic data back renal denervation in the long term Analyses presented at EuroPCR assessed Medtronic\u2019s Symplicity blood pressure procedure in patient groups with severe hypertension and who had prior cardiovascular events. # Cardiac Endologix buys clot removal system from Surmodics Endologix will market the system to vascular interventionists who use its other devices to treat peripheral artery disease and abdominal aortic aneurysms. o Maa Top medtech executive moves in 2026 Integra LifeSciences has reappointed Stuart Essig as CEO, and Edwards Lifesciences and BD named new CFOs. Read MedTech Dive's roundup for all the details. eMaa a 1. Trump further tweaks steel, aluminum, copper tariffs 2. Resmed completes $340M Noctrix takeover 3. Natera\u2019s Solomon Moshkevich on how MRD testing pinpoints cancer recurrence 4, Intuitive elevates Taylor Patton to chief commercial and marketing officer Get the free newsletter Subscribe to MedTech Dive for top news, rends & analysis MOST POPULAR Abbott receives CE mark for dual glucose-ketone sensor Resmed completes $340M Noctrix takeover J&J recalls Impella heart pumps after patient dies California attorney general sues over 23andMe data breach LIBRARY RESOURCES e New medical devices reshaping the medtech industry ]_ insight: The Revenue Leaks in Medtech Commercial Strategies UNE e Al and digital health trends in medtech COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS Axis Spine Technologies appoints renowned neurosurgeon Dr. Jean- Christophe Leveque to Medical ... 1 in 3 Women Don't Know Menopause and Bone Loss Are Connected, New Osteoboost Data Reveals Positrigo Expands U.S. Presence with New NeuroLF at