On Iran: Trump Under Fire For Not Yet Published Mol 3 Uiraine Open Threed Posted by b at 17:48 utc | Comments (222) car 202641 June 16, 2026 War On ran: Trump Hat 20264 Lebanon - U.S. Offers To Ignite Sectarian War War On ran: Trump H During a press conference at the G7 meeting in France U.S. President Donald Trump : criticized Israel's way of waging war against Hizbullah. Urraine Open Tread War On ran: Trump Hat Video via FOXne1 Partial transcript {tell you what ~ Israelis fighting Hizbullah too long and too many people are being killed. And you don't have to knock down an apartment house every time you are looking for somebody. Because there are alot of people in those apartment houses and not all are Hizbullah, That I ean tell you. Trump does not say it explicitly but he is accusing Israel of committing war crimes. Fine so far. iMay-2008 But then he suggests to solve the Hizbullah problem by using Abu Mohammad al-Julani Aon 2008 aka Ahmed al-Sharaa, the al-Queda ruler of Syria, to (re-)ignite a sectarian Sunni-Shia February 2008 Peover 2008 And I suggested to eral to let Syria take care of Hizbullah ~ \"cause tobe honest with pecan you T think they would do a better job of doing it. (.] Syria, you know, he's pulled that povambac Country together amazingly quickly. He's very capable. And he's been very good for me. He's protected ~ everything I've asked for he's done. And if Israel cant do the job without killing everyone he wll do the job, Syria will do the job. Just an hour ago another Israeli attack in southern Lebanon killed another four random people. The U.S.-Iran Memorandum of Understanding agreed upon two days ago May 2007 Ber 200 Femme, 2007 forces from Lebanon December 2006 Israel's prime minister Bibi Netanyahoo is obviously trying to sabotage Trump's Iran Sovemba: 2005 deal. He has already lost the war against Iran which he himself had instigated. Now his August 2006 generals are telling him they can not win. \u2018Trump will have to squeeze Netanyahoo hard ~ by withholding intelligence, money or weapons - to end his conflict in Lebanon. The publie offer by Trump to Netanyahoo to use the Al-Qaeda kingpin of Syria to \u2018finish the job\u2019 in Lebanon may be a his last chance to escape from the problem. December 2005 But there are complications. Cont. reading: Lebanon = US. 1 To Ignite Sectarian War Posted by b at 17:41 utc | Comments (262) June 15, 2026 War On Iran: The MoU - A Small Pause In A Decades Long Conflict The United States and the Islamic Republic of Iran have agreed upon a Memorandum of Understanding which is supposed to end the current hostilities between the country. A MoU is non binding. No text has been published and public remarks on either side hint that there are different interpretation of what the various clauses of the MoU are supposed to mean. + RSS Feed > Aiom Feed The agreement, ifit survives that long, is supposed be signed in Switzerland on Friday, Until about the last minute Tran was not willing to sign on to it. There was, and political opposition in Iran against an agreement with the U.S. Iran, itis argued, is in an advantageous position. It could and should demand more than itis supposed to get under the MoU. Without knowing the details ofthe social-economic situation in Iran it is hard. to judge if that is true. Last Friday, Mehr News Agency published a 14 point draft of the MoU. This Iranian draft version included: 1. Permanent and immediate end to war on all fronts, including Lebanon. 2. US commitment to non-interference in Iran\u2019s internal affairs and respect forthe sovereignty of the Islamie Republic of Iran, 3. Complete lifting ofthe naval blockade within go days. 4.US commitment to withdraw its foree from around Iran, 5. Reopening of the Strat of Hormuz within 30 days, under Iranian arrangements. 6. Suspension of sanctions on oil and petrochemical product sales and derivatives, \u2018and full Iranian access to its financial resources Points 2., 3.,6., are straight out of the 1981 Algier Accords which had ended the Iranian hostage crisis. Under that agreement the U.S. had committed to not intervene politically or militarily in Iranian internal affairs and to remove the freeze on Iranian assets and sanctions on Iran. The U.S started to break those commitments as soon as the Accord had been signed While Iran, on Sunday afternoon local time, was still arguing about signing the MoU, l, pt to sabotage the agreement, launched an attack on Beirut in Lebanon. Iran immediately pulled back from the MoU. It announced retaliation strikes against Israel proper. President Trump, who was very eager to get the MoU signed, had to make addition concessions to get the agreement back on track: Cont, reading: War On Iran: The MoU \u2014 A Smal Posted by b at 16:15 utc | Comments (299) Long Conflict June 14, 2026 Iran Open Thread 2026-126", "ocr_text_len": 14789}
