vide social media features and to analyse our traffic. We also \u2018share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners who may combine it with other information that you've provided to them or that they've collected from your use of their services. Necessary Preferences Statistics Marketing \u00a9 io } @ @ EE ee ee Login Q What the NUJ does list for Al Quds Radio; Mohammed Fayez Yousef Abu Matar, freelance photographer; Ahmed Shehab, producer of Voice of Prisoners Radio; Hossa Latest news NATIONAL UNION oes (2 | oe JOURNALISTS NATIONAL UNION es () JOURNALISTS NUJ condemns intolerable delay in Martin O'Hagan murder review The NUJhas described as \"intolerable\" the action of the Office of the Police Ombudsman for Northern Ireland (OPON?) in blocking the release of its own report into the failed police investigation of the 2001 murder of journalist Martin O'Hagan. 01June 2026 News Statement from the DC Thomson NUJ chapel representatives Editorial staff at DC Thomson are coming together to seek formal recognition for the NUJ, ensuring colleagues have an independent and collective voice in discussions about pay, conditions and the future of our work. 01 June 2026 News NUJ slams Ofcom decision to approve STV cuts to local news The NUJ has condemned Ofcom's decision to allow STV to cut its dedicated news coverage for the North of Scotland as \u201cthe weakest of decisions in the face of the strongest of opposition\u201d. 01June 2026 News Join the NUJ \u2018We're stronger together. Upcoming events and training Events cal 10 June 2026 11 June 2026 17 June 2026 Reps' Training Stage 1, Health, Safety and Equality Workshop 10 June 2026 Welfare Workshop Stage 1,17 June 2026 Putting together a pay claim, Stage 2, 11 June 2026 Become an NUS equality rep with dealing with a bullying manager, creating an active chapel and negotiating a robust house agreement are among the skills... Trade union training Online 24 June 2026 New Members Induction Workshop, 24 June 26 This one-hour workshop is for all members. The aim of this workshop is for you to learn more about the NUJ, how chapels and branches are established a... Trade union training Online Become an NUJhealth and safety rep with the union's three-stage training. Trade union training Online 24 June 2026 NUJ Reps\u2019 Induction Workshop, 24 June 2026 Trade union training Online the union's two-stage training. Trade union training Online 1 July 2026 Organising & Recruitment, 1 July 2026 Trade union training Online eneeLane\u00ae wignever FAIR DEAL FO FREELANCES \u2018The NUJ campaign to fight for a better deal for freelances. #FairDeal4Freelances includes a charter of freelance rights that sets out the benefits the self-employed Fair Deal 4 Freelances should enjoy. Support the campaign red engine NUJ in your workplace NUJ chapels play a vital role in helping you at work. Wherever there are three or more NUJ members in a workplace, a chapel can be formed. The NUJhas more than 1,000 chapels and some of them are recognised by the companies below. 1B] BC] SPRINGER NATURE RTE Latest publications More publications Do you know who's talking? The Journalist June- July 2026 Our cover feature explores the range of reasons why fewer young people are becoming journalists including how social media's generation gap might bec... 02 June 2026 The Irish Journalist - May 2026 \u2018Welcome to the May 2026 edition of The Irish Journalist. 01 May 2026 The Journalist Apri May 2026 Our cover feature explores the rise of the fake experts after a journalist's suspicions about one person he was emailing led him to discover Al creati... 27 April 2026 Senior Reporter - April 2026 News from the NUJ's 60+ Council. 17 April 2026", "ocr_text_len": 3859}
