s Type to search Fair, prosperous and sustainable societies We support informed, inclusive decision-making about natural resources and the energy transition. (> Learn about NRGI ) We use cookies on this site to enhance your user experience By clicking the Accept button, you agree to us doing so. More info In focus Suneeta Kaimal and Patrick Heller reflect on how resource governance has evolved over two decades and why the coming years demand more from institutions, accountability and political leadership than ever before. ACCOUNTABILITY, FOSSIL FUEL TRANSITION, TRANSITION MINERALS Foundations and Future-Proofing a New Era of Resource Governance NRGI at 20 This year marks NRGI's twentieth anniversary. Explore reflections and initiatives on transforming resource governance for a new era. Visit our anniversary page ) The future of national oil companies As part of NRGI's 20th anniversary, explore our latest work on how national oil companies can navigate risks, seize opportunities and shape what comes next. REPORT) 24 MAR 2026 BLOG Post) 24 man 2026 BLOG POST) 19 aR 2026 National Oil Company Transformation: Pathways for Transformation: What From Transparency to Transformation: Strategic Choices for an Uncertain Today's Energy Uncertainty Means for NRGI\u2019s NOC Work Past, Present and Energy Future National Oil Companies Future mh ae Our focus areas Anticorruption & accountability Fossil fuel transition Just energy transition Addressing extractive-sector corruption is crucial Fossil fuels are not the future, but many As the global energy transition accelerates, for citizens in resource-rich countries and for the countries lack concrete pathways beyond the decisionmakers must ensure that itis just, attainment of global climate goals. production of oil, gas and coal. inclusive and equitable\u2014with people's needs at its center. State-owned enterprises Taxation & revenue management. Transition minerals State-owned companies are critical but Effective revenue management