{"_key": "nolabels", "source_key": "nolabels", "filename": "No_Labels.png", "image_file": "No_Labels.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 1.1468, "s008_neutral_headlines": -0.879, "s010_scare_quotes": 1.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 1.0, "s085_standard_sections": 3.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 18.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.004, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.8684, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.4799, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00292, "small_face_count": 7.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0396, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.1989, "content_column_count": "1", "side_margin_frac": 0.0, "header_band_height_frac": 0.1041, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 2.3657, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0286, "page_scroll_length": "long", "nav_item_count": 22.0, "footer_link_count": 47.0, "cta_button_count": 3.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 18.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 8.636, "headline_size_variance": 0.2277, "page_text_density": "medium", "timestamp_count": 1.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0115, "number_token_frac": 0.0069, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 1.1468, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0459, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.2294, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 5.2752, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.4587, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.0, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.2294}, "ocr_text": "Extremes on both sides are getting dangerous and making itimpossible for \u2018America to solve its most important problems. No Labels strengthens the \u2018commonsense center in Congress and across the country because if we do not do this work, no one will. Let's Get Started. GD GD When the talking stops, the fighting starts. Itis a tragic lesson of history that too many Americans, and too many of our leaders, forget. Frustrated Americans are increasingly raging at the other side or receding from politics altogether. No Labels needs millions of citizens to join us in offering another way. We bring together builders and fixers across America and in Congress, where we support House and Senate members with the courage to think independently and find commonsense solutions. Our Initiatives MAKE CONGRESS conversations No Labels continues to bring Join us in our conversation today members of Congress together about what a constructive third force while also mobilizing No Labels in our politics might look like. members to support the campaigns of our congressional allies. ec\u00bb Learn More An oral history from anear-future American crisis America is headed toward a debt crisis, and there is zero evidence that Washington has the will to avoid it. Read No Labels' new booklet, Nightmare on Main Street, to see how such a crisis could arrive, what it would mean for you, and why the planning needs to begin now to address it. ent The No Labels Movement The No How It Started In 2010, a group of Republicans, Democrats and Independents saw the growing levels of partisan dysfunction in Washington and decided to try what had never been done before: assembling a national Movement to represent commonsense Americans. \u2014 Congress We identify and unite leaders in both parties who are willing to buck party leadership and govern with common sense. We inspired the creation of the Problem Solver Caucus and host regular \u201cbicameral\u201d meetings between House and Senate leaders, which have fostered major legislative victories such as the Infrastructure Bill in 2021 and CHIPS and Science Act in 2022. \u2014 Citizens With the help of grassroots supporters nationwide, we are creating a home for the politically homeless. No Labels cultivates, educates, and empowers citizens tired of the angriest and most reckless politicians dominating the debate and worried that America lacks commonsense political leadership when we need it most. \u2014 Elections We mobilize our members to support the campaigns of allied House and Senate members in both parties. This creates an independent support base for courageous elected officials, enabling them to fend off primary challenges from partisan activists and extremists who punish leaders for seeking bipartisan solutions.", "ocr_text_len": 2742}
