cracy through real debate\u2014replacing polarization with dialogue, outrage with curiosity, and noise with reason About Us Ways To Engage DISCOVER MORE Open to Debate is the nation\u2019s leading nonpartisan, nonprofit media platform dedicated to bringing together people of multiple viewpoints for civil discourse. Our weekly debates cover a variety of pressing topics\u2014from politics to culture, and everything in between\u2014 and are available through NPR, YouTube, Substack, and podcast platforms. Q 350+ DEBATES Since 2006, we have engaged millions of global audience members through a variety of unique formats that evolve with our discourse. Q we 25+ AWARDS World-renowned organizations, including the cies, Webby \u2018Awards, and Telly Awards, have recognized the quality of our programming ((\u00bb)) 900+ DEBATERS influential voices from across the political and cultural spectrum have taken our debate ge to address today's most critical topics. 350+ STATIONS Open to Debate is a one-hour weekly program broadcast on NPR stations across the country. Ns also air individual des as specials. Explore our latest debates\u2014thought-provoking conversations that illuminate today's most pressing issues and strengthen the culture of civic dialogue r New Ways To Engagk \u2122 Upcoming & Recent Debates % RECENT DEBATE Generational Divides with Nick Gi May 29, 2026 llespie Generational Divides with Nick Gillespie: Are the Parents Alright? Reshma Saujani WATCH ON SUBSTACK yore Debaters Lenore Skenazy Kristin Gallant Sven @- May 22, 2026 Government as Shareholder: Proactive Competitive Strategy or Last Resort? Debaters Richard Falkenrath Laura Taylor-Kale \u2018Yasheng Huang Bob Pozen o eo O- April 30, 2026 Should We Separate the Art from the Artist? 1 0100000! 1 01100 0011 1 0. o April 16, 2026 Will the Al Bubble Burst? \u2018Magnus Grimeland Ryan Cummings May 7, 2026 Should Museums Repatriate Cultural Artifacts? Debaters Mario Trabucco della Torretta Chika Okeke-Agulu Dominic