mp; the new FDA commish @ Biotech FDA chief's exit clouds already murky drug approvals During Dr. Martin Makary\u2019s tenure as commissioner, the FDA faced pushback over high-profile drug rejections for Replimune and UniQure, @ Biotech Why the FDA\u2019s push for real-time clinical trials could favor Big Pharma \u2018The agency's new initiative promises faster drug approval times, but smaller trial sponsors could struggle to keep up. # Biotech India\u2019s pharma industry is going global. But can it catch up to China? Arecord Sun Pharma acquisition signals global ambitions. But infrastructure, capital and policy gaps could stand in the way of India becoming an R&D powerhouse. @ Manufacturing How tough is it getting for vaccine makers in the U.S.? {As federal policy chills domestic demand, some companies are increasingly leaning on sales from international markets. @ Pharma Cancer, immunology startups lead latest wave of stealth exits A handful of recently debuted biotechs reveal where drug R&D is headed next. @ Biotech Lilly, Gilead lead pharma\u2019s M&A boom. Deal volume in 2026 sf cancer and autoimmune disease drugs. outpacing last year, \\d is being driven by @ Biotech Biotech layoffs are easing, but is the worst over? BioNTech is one of the most recent companies to announce cuts, but the pace of job losses is slowing, @ Biotech Novo hikes guidance on Wegovy pill\u2019s fast sales start Sales and profit should shrink less than originally anticipated thanks to strong momentum for its new obesity pill, the drugmaker said in its \u2018most recent earnings report, Commerciaization Anew company rises from the ashes of Purdue Pharma Knoa Pharma will still sell the opioid medications that triggered a national crisis, but with guardrails. @ Patient What's at stake in Amgen\u2019s showdown with the FDA? \u2018The agency accused Amgen of manipulating data for its fast-growing drug Tavneos and wants it pulled from the market, but the large pharma is digging its heels in. 4 Phoema Protein degraders gain speed as Arvinas scores landmark approval Although excitement over the biotech\u2019 \u201cProtac\u201d protein degrader is being tempered by narrower-than-expected clinical benefit, R&D in the field is heating up. @ Biotech Obesity drugmakers chase weight loss. Biohaven is betting on muscles. With many pharma companies focused on developing drugs that shed pounds, Biohaven is digging its heels into a clinical program based on an experimental myostatin inhibitor that builds muscle. 1 Phoema Pfizer deals extend patent life for a top- selling rare disease drug Get the free newsletter Subscribe to PharmaVoice for important stories, insights & perspectives MOST POPULAR As amyloid falls out of favor, here\u2019s where Alzheimer\u2019s R&D is headed next Vertex\u2019s Journavx made history, but left a void in the pain space AstraZeneca aims for a new blockbuster run in cardio disease Longevity science picks up steam in pharma LIBRARY RESOURCES Policy, Pricing and the Changing Economics of Orphan Drugs PLavB0oK [E] Navigating the Era of the Single Pivotal Clinical Trial \u2018The State of Process Intensification View all COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS reprai Launches reTRAIN, Bringing AL-Native Training to Pharma's Many Needs \u2018Veeva Announces Falcon, an Agentic Platform and Standard Agents to Deliver Agentic Labor in Dr... BioPhorum relaunches expanded Host Cell Protein Data Platform to support safer biopharmaceut View all | Post a press release EVENTS 1% om {8 cardiovascular Forum 1% rou JS oncology Forum as conn g8 Analyticon View all | Promote an event", "ocr_text_len": 5675}
