{"_key": "politicaltribune", "source_key": "politicaltribune", "filename": "Political_Tribune.png", "image_file": "Political_Tribune.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 1.5272, "s008_neutral_headlines": 0.417, "s010_scare_quotes": 3.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.1328, "s078_absolutist_framing": 2.0, "s085_standard_sections": 6.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 15.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.01252, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.6431, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.1987, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00313, "small_face_count": 4.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0711, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.3722, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.086, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0087, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "red", "accent_color_count": 2.085, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0305, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 35.0, "footer_link_count": 79.0, "cta_button_count": 6.0, "newsletter_box_count": 1.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 1.0, "category_badge_count": 4.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 2.636, "headline_size_variance": 0.1704, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 5.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0214, "number_token_frac": 0.0617, "city_or_county_in_name": 1.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.3984, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.664, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.5312, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.2656, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.3904, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.0, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.9296}, "ocr_text": "\u2018Subscribe \u00aeD Login Magazine YOUR SUPPORT KEEPS US PUBLISHING. FOLLOW THIS LINK TO SUBSCRIBE TO OUR PRINT MAGAZINE. My City, Their Riot 08June Tom Williams The far right seized on the murder of Henry Nowak to bring riot and disorder to the streets of Southampton. The violence exposed not only the shameless cynicism of its leaders, but also the neglect and frustration on which they thrive. Art as Resistance 08june Katie Tobin \u2018Anew timely exhibition remembers the anti-fascist Artists\u2019 International \u2018Association, exploring the role of culture in counteracting oppression. British Empire Never Left Ireland 08june Ethan Rooney In County Waterford, sheep farmers face eviction as the Duke of Devonshire's estate imposes rent hikes of up to 900% \u2014a stark reminder that British imperialism still \u2018shapes rural Ireland. Cricket for the Many 04June Richard Heller / Peter Oborne \u2018The sport long associated with empire and elite privilege has a surprising, often neglected history of radicalism \u2014 which its fans must recuperate today. 20 May Labour's Social Base Is Collapsing 18May The Gazafication of Lebanon 14May Living in a Mineral World 12May Lessons From Defeat: The General Strike at 100 12May Starmer's Resignation Is Not Enough May Orban's Legacy 07 May Mark Rowley's Right-Wing Crusade 12May The Left Must Unite Against Labour and Reform May After Schadenfreude 09 May How Devolution Destroyed Scottish Labour 20 May Family Economics 15 May \u2018The Autocracy Network Free Zone Island 22May David. Powell From Freeports to Al Growth Zones, Britain is quietly being transformed into a network of deregulated corporate \u2018enclaves where democracy is replaced by private governance. 19May Tariq Mehmood's Resistance (and) Literature 13May MPs to Met Chief: Retract Gaza Protest Smears What is the Radical Right? o2iune \u2014stathis Kouvelakis Reactionary forces have deepened neoliberalism\u2019s authorian trends and eroded democracy across the globe. Understanding the nature of their project is necessary to defeat it. 17 May Letter From Santa Marta 14May National Questions Who Was Maureen Duffy? o2June Jennifer Jasmine White \u2018The prolific British author and activist, who died last week aged 92, blazed anew path between fiction and the front line of radical politics. The Hasan Piker Ban Exposes the Power of the Israel Lobby Ollune \u2014 Karl \u2018The decision to ban Hasan Piker and Cenk Uygur from the UK marks further \u2018escalation in the clampdown on critics of israel. The Age of Cannabusiness OtJune Kojo Koram Inmany parts of the world, the disastrous \u2018War on Drugs\u2019 is winding down. But legalisation brings its own problems, with the rise of the drug commodity driving corporate concentration and deepening inequality. Cuba Must Not Stand Alone OlJune Doug Wilson \u2018Cuba has long stood with peoples fighting for dignity and self-determination across the globe. As \u2018Washington threatens the island with military intervention, it's time to return that solidarity in kind. Subscribe 1Year| 4 Issues \u00a319.95 1Year | 4 Issues \u00a329.95 Digital Subscription Print + Digital Subscription \u2018Subscribe to Tribune today and help us build a real, socialist alternative to Britain's media moguls. Start a New Subscription Renew Your Subscription Ireland\u2019s Quiet Complicity 29May Hugo Harvey Despite ireland's claims of neutrality, US warplanes supplying the Gaza genocide continue to pass through Shannon Airport while the government looks the other way. Labour\u2019s Gaza Reckoning 18May \u2014Daniley- Williamson \u2018The movement for Palestine has become one of the largest mass mobilisations in British history. Labour's local election drubbing shows itis now beginning to reshape electoral politics. Music Beyond Borders 28May Ben Thompson \u2018The V&A East's inaugural exhibition is a work of radical archival history, ranging across continents \u2018and epochs to excavate the traditions that gave rise to Black British music. American Dystopia 27May \u2014 Dawood All Tycoon, the debut feature by Charlotte Zhang, understands that yesterday's science fiction is today\u2019s reality. 07 May Sheffield Music Invented The Future 05 May \u2018Al Workers Against the War Machine 29 April Trail of Destruction 27 April 10Foot's Indoor Publishing 23May Tom Wiliams Adamning new report has. found that every Premier League club is tied to \u2018companies implicated in Israel's war crimes \u2014 exposing the beautiful game's complicity in genocide. 08 May The Collapse of Starmerism 05 December \u2018Working-Class Writer Is Something to Be 27 April Nowhere Else to Go 25 April \u2018Andrea Egan: \u2018Scrap the Anti-Migrant Crackdown\u2019 Subscribe to Tribune today and help us build a real, socialist alternative to Britain's media moguls. \u2018Subscribe Magazine \u2018About Us Contact us Privacy Policy \u00a92026", "ocr_text_len": 4718}
