emains stigmatised as an individual failing. Recognising its structural underpinnings is key to liberatory framings of sobriety, writes William Rayfet Hunter READ MORE > BOOKS - HISTORY -LGBTQ+ Deviants and trailblazers - review Rebecca Jane Morgan\u2019s account of the fight for legal recognition for trans people in the UK offers a valuable resource to contemporary activists, writes kit Heyam ALTERNATIVE ECONOMIES - COLONIALISM AND IMPERIALISM - LATIN AMERICA SOCIALISM Cuba stands firm Cuba continues to show the world an alternative mode of development even in the face of US regime change, argues Helen Yaffe Manage Consent x eves alr Consul Eres aera wl Sew a's fesees ats sect 1s browsing behaviour or uniques on this site Not consenting or withdrawing consent, may adversely atfct cra features and functions Deny View preferences AUTHORITARIANISM AND THE FAR RIGHT - DEMOCRACY - LABOUR PARTY Elections 2026: The political Shifts reshaping Wales Robin Mann reports on how support for both Plaid Cymru and Reform is transforming the Welsh political landscape READ MORE > READ MORE > NEW ISSUE OUT NOW STRIKING BACK STRIKING BACK FROM OUR ARCHIVE Red Pepperreturns with a new-look, extended annual print edition, featuring: The 100 year legacy of the 1926 General Strike Anti-racism and migrant justice: new approaches needed Free press under threat in Latin America Mid-century wars for oil in Nigeria and Iran Photo essays: West Bank lives and Gen-Z protest With Sara Ahmed, Gargi Bhattacharyya, Zrinka Bralo, Behrooz Ghamari- Tabrizi, Juliet Jacques, David Howell, Matt Lee, Callum Cant and many more! BUY | STOCKISTS | SUBSCRIBE Just Irish Emigration may be at the core of Irish national memory but this has not translated to into a welcoming embrace for its immigrant population, writes Ola Majekodunmi READ MORE > Preview the FULL 30-year archive (aa) RED PEPPER LIVE! IN FOCUS PALESTINE Dispatches from Gaza: ceasefire cycles As talks of a ceasefire rise and fade from the headlines, S