ustworthy capital partner from a predatory one, says US Professional Funding and US Medical Funding's Christopher Cornella @ Financials Red Robin sells 30 company-owned units for $23.5M Western Idaho and will continue to operate them under the Red Robin brand. @ Franchising Dog Haus signs 50-unit deal, adds new execs \u2018The hot dog chain hopes recruiting high-performing operators from other restaurants will help it grow from over 50 stores to 1,500. 6 Franchising Woworks hires former Subway exec as chief growth officer James Walker joins the six-branded company as it continues to expand nationwide through single-concept and co-branded locations. 4 Franchising Portillo\u2019s opens first airport unit \u2018The nontraditional location signals ongoing investment in Texas, where Portillo's had a disappointing 2025. # Operations How Chipotle\u2019s rewards relaunch extends reach of its marketing flywheel Curt Garner, chief strategy and technology officer at the chain, explains how a \u201cSummer of Extras\u201d effort builds on and gamifies its rewards program, 6 Marketing Dairy Queen adds $150K development incentive for food-focused stores \u2018The cash incentive and further rewards for multi-unit development could help the brand grow its Grill & Chill concept. @ Financials Wingstop launches loyalty program Club Wingstop's exclusive perks and experiences could help improve guest frequency and same-store sales growth Consumer Tends Tijuana Flats relaunches franchising Under Latitude Food Group's ownership, the 100-unit fast casual chain will partner with operators to open new units and refranchise select stores. 6 Franchising Qdoba completes $435M whole business securitization \u2018The transaction will alow the chain to refinance debt, providing liquidity to help it reach 2,000 units and support investments in remodels and digital makelines. @ Financials Chili\u2019s remakes iconic Baby Back Ribs jingle \u2014 again \u2014 with Lizzo \u2018The cultural play comes several years after the chain tapped Boye II Men to remix the tune in an effort to double down on '90s nostalgia. eee oive Restaurant tech execs warn against AI overdependence There are limits to ATs use cases, reliability and applicability, industry leaders said at the 2026 National Restaurant Association Show. Operations Church\u2019s Texas Chicken appoints Popeyes vet as chief commercial officer Kevin Nemeth will oversee various aspects of the chain's commercial strategy and help connect brand, digital, loyalty, menu and execution. @ Executive News Sweetgreen hires Chipotle exec as chief strategy officer Cindy Olsen will help oversee the beleaguered chain\u2019 turnaround strategy after it posted its worst sales decline since going public. Executive News Papa Johns\u2019 CMO on driving cultural relevance with a \u2018Toy Story\u2019 tie-up agency partners and how the chain is working with Google Cloud on AL @ Technology REACH Grow with smarter targeting, \u201cSD DOORDASH Ads Get the free newsletter Subscribe to Restaurant Dive for top news, rends & analysis MOST POPULAR Cafe Rio hires &pizza CEO after losing its way McDonald's bets chicken, restaurant improvements will grow sales KFC expands $10 bucket deal across weekdays Major Taco Bell franchisee sells 44 restaurants LIBRARY RESOURCES 1 Agentic Commerce: How to Power Al-Driven Payment Experiences How Al is shaping the restaurant industry Checkout is Now a Loyalty View all COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS ZeroToOne.Al Deploys its Large Behavioral Model at Advertising Scale Through GroundTruth, Laun... Harri Launches Engage360\u2122 to Help Restaurant Operators Combat Frontline Turnover Deliverect Partners with DataCandy to Connect Digital Ordering, Loyalty and Gift Cards Across... Parrish Chapman Appointed Executive Vice President of Sales at Hi Auto View all | Post a press release WHAT WE'RE READING @ cLoomaers Starbucks to Take AI Usage Into Account in Tech Workers\u2019 Bonuses (% \u00a349 NEWS Last call? States look to