uth Dakota State University\u2019s Dakota Lakes Research Farm hosts its annual Field Day on June 26 featuring updates on long-term agronomy projects including oat and wheat trials. Attendees can participate in tours, educational sessions, meals sponsored by local organizations, giveaways\u2014and learn more about sustainable farming practices. Nine South Dakota students appointed to U.S. service academies for 2026 SDSU schedules groundbreaking Harland and Neuweiler compete for new women's soccer on- in men's pole vault at U20 campus facility July 28 Championships More News NON-PROFIT NFIB launches new ads urging Sen. Thune to repeal beneficial ownership mandate in South Dakota \u2018The National Federation of Independent Business has launched new ads in South Dakota urging Senator John Thune to push for permanent repeal of beneficial ownership information mandates affecting small businesses. The group argues these requirements are burdensome and calls on Congress for legislative action. BUSINESS SDSU Extension announces virtual Wisdom Writing Workshop for July 18 South Dakota State University Extension willoffe its virtual Herlooms: Wisdom Writing \u2018Workshop on July 18. The free session includes guided reflection activities focused on aging. June 18,2 South Dakota students receive honors at 2026 National Day Contest in Maryland Seventy-three South Dakota students competed at this year\u2019s National History Day Contest held June 14-18 near Washington D.C, earning several awards including top placements for. istory lune 18,2026 McLaughlin man sentenced to two years in federal prison for assault with a weapon \"A McLaughlin man has been sentenced to two years in federal prison after pleading guilty to assault with a dangerous weapon stemming from an alteration ata graduation party last yea. june 17,2026 NON-PROFIT USD voice students advance to national semifinals in record numbers Four University of South Dakota voice students have advanced further than ever before in national singing auditions after qualifying through rigorous regional rounds. They will represent USD at July's National Association of Teachers of Singing conference in San Antonio. USD students assist athletes at South Dakota Special Olympics Summer Games University of South Dakota students supported 85 athletes at this year's South Dakota Special \u2018Olympics Summer Games by conducting hearing screenings as part of Healthy Athletes. june 17,2026 as sex offender [Atte Eagle man has been sentenced to five months in federal prison after falingto update his sex offender registration while staying ata casino out-of state. The sentence follows prior June 17, 2026 Sioux Falls man sentenced for failing to register as sex offender \u2018ASioux Falls man has been sentenced to nearly two years in federal prison for filing to register as sex offender after previous corwictions. The case highlights ongoing efforts under Project Safe. june 17,2026 scHoots Little Eagle man sentenced to federal prison for failing to register @env SPORTS DIRECTORY \u2018Tren ng \u2018SDSU Dakota Lakes Research Farm Feld Day to showcase long-term agronomy research June 26 Nine South Dakota students appointed to US. service \u2018academies for 2026 \u2018SDSU schedules groundbreaking for new women's soccer on-campus facility July 28 Harland and Neuweller compete in men's pole vault at 1U20 Championships INFIB launches new ads urging Sen. Thune torepeal beneficial ownership mandate in South Dakota \u2018SDSU Extension announces vetual Wisdom Writing, Workshop for July 18 South Dakota students receive honors at 2026 National History Day Contest in Maryland McLaughlin man sentenced to two yearsin federal prison fr assault with aweapon USD voice students advance to national semifinals in record numbers USD students assist athletes at South Dakota Special \u2018Olympics Summer Games Local news, in your inbox. \u2018The stories that matter to Rushmore State News AINews -\u00bb Rushmore State News