es Section 301 probe of Vietnam \u2018The White House's investigation, frequently used as a precurser to tariffs, will evaluate the country's intellectual property acts, policies and practices @ Procurement UPS invests $50M in automotive, industrial logistics push @ Logistics eee oive CFOs face tricky tariff refund questions as process gains steam Faster-than-expected results are easing early operational fears while shifting attention to decisions on accounting, tax and financial reporting issues. @ Risk and Resiience USPS, DHL eCommerce ink $10B-plus long-term contract The deal adds to other arrangements the agency has secured with Amazon and UPS ast looks to improve its financial outlook. @ Logistics UP, NS revised merger application moves ahead \u2018The Surface Transportation Board is now considering the updated materials, and asked both parties to submit supplemental information by July 27, @ Freight E.Lf expects $58.5M in tariff refunds to fuel price cuts In ts last fiscal year, the beauty brand grappled with a roughly 55% tariff rate, which drove the need for price adjustments. 4 Procurement SharkNinja leverages production flexibility to mitigate tariffs \u2018The household appliance maker taps multiple factories for its top \u2018SKUs, giving it room to maneuver on costs, CEO Mark Barrocas said. 1 Procurement Walmart: Store-fulfilled deliveries getting faster More than 36% of deliveries from stores arrived in three hours or less in QL, with quicker speeds fueling customer engagement, EVP and CFO John David Rainey said. @ Logistics Walmart ties expected tariff refunds to price strategy amid cost pressures CFO John David Rainey said potential recoveries would be directed toward lowering prices as fuel costs pressure consumers. @ Procurement New rail data requirement a \u2018win\u2019 for shippers, expert says Class I railroads will soon need to report two additional metrics, which a former BNSF director said could boost service transparency. @ Freight CBP raises accepted tariff refunds to $85B As of May 22, about $20.6 billion in certified refunds with interest have been completed through Customs and Border Protection's dedicated portal. Operations Management Novelis aluminum plant to resume operations following fire damage \u2018The company has started commissioning its New York plant and expects to ramp up hot mill production in the coming weeks @ Fisk and Resiience \u2014\u2014 Full tariff refunds for de minimis imports? US says no A lawsuit aims to revive the exemption and land refunds on all tariffs for shipments that would have qualified, but the Justice Department po offered a rebuttal i \u201cARGFT @ Logistics Target touts improved inventory turns in Qu \u2018The retailer aims to leverage artificial intelligence tools alongside its two new facilities to reduce volatility and in-stock issues. { Operations Management Regulation 1. US eyes new tariffs for China, EU, Mexico and more after 2. USTR floats 25% tariff on Brazil imports 3. Advance Auto Parts nears finish line on distribution center consolidation strategy \u2018Trump further tweaks steel, aluminum, copper tariffs \u2018Target launches $367M food distribution center in Colorado Get the free newsletter Subscribe to Supply Chain Dive for top ews, trends & analysis MOST POPULAR \u2018Trump further tweaks steel, aluminum, copper tariffs Advance Auto Parts nears finish line on distribution center consolidation strategy Target launches $367M food distribution center in Colorado Port of Charleston to increase automotive cargo capacity LIBRARY RESOURCES 2) How Retail Supply Chain Leaders Are Navigating Disruptions \u00a9) How Intelligent Shipping is Transforming Eeommerce Delivery Puavaoox E]_ what shippers should Look For in a Logistics Partner COMPANY ANNOUNCEMENTS Lloyd's Register Selects Raindrop to Power a New Era of Procurement Royal Canadian Steel and Affiliates to Pay $19 Million to Settle Customs Fraud Allegations Capital4Trade and Tech Cargo Complete Wave