ncluded comedians, \u2018actors, musicians, HMA fighters, authors, artists, and beyond. WATCH NOW Pte by Try Cana JOE ROGAN A standup comedian for over 30 years, Rogan\u2019 seventh hout long comedy special \u00abJoe Rogan: Burn the Boots premiered live on Netflix on August 3, 2024, Rogan\u2019 previous comedy specials include Joe Rogan Strange Times (2018) and Joe Rogan: Triggered (2016 for Netflix, Joe Rogan: Rocky Mountain High (20%) for Comedy Central, Joe Rogan: Live from the Tabernacle (2012 released via his website, Taking Monkey in Space (2008) on CO & DVD, and Joe Rogan Live (2007) \u2018on DVD, Additionally, Rogan released the Cs Shiny Hoppy Jihad (2007) and In \u2018Gonna Be Dead Someday (2000). Rogan is host of The oe Rogan Experience, consistently ranked one of the most popular podcasts and currently distributed by Spotty. The Joe Ragan Experience launched on December 2, 2009 helping to create the space of lng form conversation video podcasting With over 2000 episodes, an average of 2 - 3 hours in length each, the show has become a destination fr open dialogue with 9 wide range of quests and perspectives including standup comedians, athletes, authors, artists, prolific thinkers, and scientists. \u2018Since 2002, Rogan has provided color commentary forthe UFC (Utimate Fighting Championship). Rogan\u2019 passion for HHA began with martial arts practice atthe \u2018age of 15 Within two years, the Boston naive earned a black belt and soon became the Massachusets full contact Tae Kwon Do champion four consecutive years. By the age of 19, Rogan won the US Open Tae Kwon Do Championship and \u20182s lightweight champion went onto beat both the middle and heavyweight tile- holders to obtain the Grand Championship. Fl credits incude Here Comes The Boom 202} and Zookeeper (201. Rogan hosted Joe Rogan Questions Everything (203) fr the Syy channel, Rogan hosted the competition realty series Feor Factor on NBC in 201/12 and previously for sic seasons onthe network rom 2001-2006. Prior to Fear Fctr Rogen played Joe Garall the resident electrician onthe hit NBC comedy series NewsRadio, Rogan regularly performs stand-up locally in Austin at his club Comedy Nothership as wel as touring across the country and internationally. Powered by Squarespace", "ocr_text_len": 2413}
