e Measures,\u201d and Hamilton Fish, Editor of The Washington Spectator. Paranoia on Parade, Part 2: The \u201cDirectors Cut\" with Jack Bryan Paranoia on Parade, Part 3: Bonus Interview with Hamitton Fish Letters to the Editor \u2018The Spectator welcomes letters from our readers reflecting diverse points of view. We'll assume they are for publication unless stipulated otherwise. Send letters via email to editors@washingtonspectator.org, and for information on where to send written correspondence to the editor, click here. The Roberts Court Has Turned the Voting Rights Act on Its Head Leslie Winner's current piece in The Washington Spectator (The Roberts Court has Turned the Voting Rights Act on Its Head) Is a concise, logical, clear and incredibly persuasive explanation of why the Callais opinion is so wrong. The simple statement that results matter more than intent is. something that has been missed in so many other commentaries. | hope it gets wider attention because it really explains what is going on. | also feel a little better thinking that the progress from all that work post-Gingles has not been eliminated, even if we are going in a very wrong direction at the moment. Anita Earls", "ocr_text_len": 5138}
{"_key": "thewatsoncenter", "source_key": "thewatsoncenter", "filename": "The_Watson_Center.png", "image_file": "The_Watson_Center.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.0, "s008_neutral_headlines": 2.6562, "s010_scare_quotes": 0.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 2.0, "s085_standard_sections": 2.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 33.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.01388, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.7404, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.0, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00894, "small_face_count": 6.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0525, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.2943, "content_column_count": "1", "side_margin_frac": 0.0, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0864, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 1.5088, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0183, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 25.0, "footer_link_count": 101.0, "cta_button_count": 2.0, "newsletter_box_count": 1.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 1.0, "category_badge_count": 5.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 6.143, "headline_size_variance": 0.2121, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 0.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0769, "number_token_frac": 0.0099, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.3922, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.1961, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.0, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 1.9608, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.0, "lx_local_civic_per100": 2.7451}, "ocr_text": "ALUMNI s Jos mycNU AACHRISTOPHER NEWPORT UNIVERSITY Request Into visit appLy ((@WVE Admission ~ Academics + Student Life ~ Athletics THE WASON CENTER Informing Democracy, Inspiring Leaders THE WASON CENTER POLLING WASON LEADERSHIP_\u2014_-SUPPORT OUR MISSION The Wason Center is where students, scholars, and civic leaders come together to turn knowledge into action. From hands-on polling to real-world political engagement, our programs offer unmatched opportunities to build the skills, insights, and connections that fuel public service and informed citizenship For more than a decade, the Wason Center has delivered unbiased, nonpartisan insights that inform citizens and lawmakers on the issues shaping Virginia's future. Our student-faculty teams conduct surveys, research, and political analysis, amplifying voices across the Commonwealth. As we enter our second decade, we're expanding beyond research to inspire values-driven, evidence- based leaders who know how to solve real problems. \u201cThe Wason Center has been an incredible experience that has allowed | me to learn about the practical application of leadership and the importance of civic engagement in young generations. MOLLY PUCKETT '27 What Makes Us Different Nonpartisan and Impactful Our student-led polling is trusted statewide and shapes the conversation on key policy issues. Real-World Engagement Students work with leaders across the Commonwealth, from city councils to the halls of Richmond. Leadership in Action Through mentorship, networking, and public events, we connect students with trailblazers in government, law, journalism, and public service. Why Our Work Matters We turn knowledge into action. Our students learn to think critically, ask hard questions, and understand the issues that shape our world. We turn service into change. By connecting with leaders who drive real solutions, our students learn to transform communities and strengthen democracy. 100+ 1,000+ 50+ students involved annually in policymakers, students, and nationally recognized polls used research and civic programming citizens engaged through public by media outlets like The forums and events Washington Post and NPR Programs and Opportunities Student Research Y Career Development & Mentorship Y Civic Events and Forums Y tinguished Virginians Speaker Series Y Captains in the Ca Y Wason Scholars Y About Our Name Judy and Harry Wason have dedicated their lives to empowering citizens and strengthening communities. Their vision for the Wason Center is to ensure every citizen has a voice in public policy and every student has the opportunity to lead m\u2122 \u2018aptai Annual event inspires election participation, encouraging students to register to vote and giving them the opportunity to meet local and state candidates. MORE ABOUT THE EVENT Get Involved Whether you're a student eager to make a difference, a leader interested in mentoring, or a citizen looking to stay informed, there's a place for you at the Wason Center. STUDENTS ALUMNI AND PARTNERS VIRGINIA LEADERS Join our team, attend events, and apply Support our work through mentorship, Help shape the next generation of civic for the Wason Scholars program, sponsorship, or engagement leaders by participating in our forums and sharing your experience. Join us as we build a stronger democracy, one informed leader at a time. JOIN OUR MAILING LIST > SUPPORT THE WASON CENTER > READ OUR LATEST POLLS >", "ocr_text_len": 3420}
