{"_key": "transgendertrend", "source_key": "transgendertrend", "filename": "Transgender_Trend.png", "image_file": "Transgender_Trend.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.7172, "s008_neutral_headlines": -0.0559, "s010_scare_quotes": 14.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 1.0, "s085_standard_sections": 4.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 21.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.01759, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.8698, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.1888, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00375, "small_face_count": 6.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.066, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.2738, "content_column_count": "1", "side_margin_frac": 0.172, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0987, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "green", "accent_color_count": 3.5669, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0281, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 49.0, "footer_link_count": 120.0, "cta_button_count": 3.0, "newsletter_box_count": 1.0, "social_icon_count": 1.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 8.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 3.667, "headline_size_variance": 0.1351, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 2.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0175, "number_token_frac": 0.0123, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.5123, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.2049, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.3074, "lx_question_style_per100": 5.0205, "lx_culture_war_per100": 1.127, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.1025, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.6148}, "ocr_text": "Home AboutUs ** 10th Anniversary Crowdfunder ** Transgender\u00a7 \u2018Support Transgender Trend! The Science Resources Autism & Gender Identity Treatments and Side-Effects Articles Blog My Body is Mel Contact Us SHOP Cass Review Terms and conditions Children\u2019s trans-themed books Ao PLEASE SUPPORT OUR WORK! This organisation was established on an entirely voluntary basis. Its Welcome to Transgender Trend. continued development relies on the kind donations of those who support Close and accept \u2018ofnd ou moe, rcusing how to contol cokes, se here: Cooke Pty DP cox0 \u2018 Printed publications and PDF downloads \u201cTeenagers have the right to explore their identities its their job - but adults should not be joining in ~ schools should not be telling girls they're boys and boys they're girls.\u201d \u2018Stephanie Davies-Arai talks to David Bull about what schools should understand from the \u2018Supreme Court judgment that the words \u2018woman\u2019 and \u2018sex\u2019 in the Equality Act 2010 relate to biology. \u00a9 YouTube BUY NOW spy\u00bb KE A body book thot celebrates YOU! ita Pood * \u00a34990 ta Autism and , Gender Challenging the Gender Mythos | with ate Stephanie Davies-Arai a \u201cWe have failed this generation of kids\u201d. \u2018Stephanie Davies-Arai talks to Benjamin Boyce about the new unreality we are living in, what we are doing to kids, the real function of puberty blockers and how The Tavistock Judicial Review has changed the world. Available in print and download sere cece tow The Tavistock's Experimentation with Puberty Blockers A collection of 5 articles Transition by Dr. Michael Biggs, Department of Sociology, University of Oxford. FREE pdf download now available from transgendertrend.com/shop \u2018CAPTURED! The Full Story Behind The \u2018Memorandum of Understanding \u2018on Conversion \u2018Transgender Trend is the leading organisation in the call for evidence-based healthcare for children and young people suffering gender dysphoria and for factual, science-based See articles relating to specific topics: teaching in schools. Our expertise was acknowledged recently when we were granted permission by the High Court to intervene in the Keira Bell v Tavistock & Portman NHS Trust. judicial review. Established in 2015, Transgender Trend has led the way in advocating for the rights of children to reject gender stereotypes and be who they really are without discrimination, labelling or medical intervention to \u2018fix\u2019 them. We believe all children have the right to go through puberty and reach adulthood with their a We believe that children with gender dysphoria deserve evidence-based treatment and have a right to the same duty of care as any other child. Our message is: No child is born in the wrong body. \u2018Transgender Trend advocates for the most vulnerable children who are caught up in the recent trend in society to replace the objective reality of sex with the subjective idea of \u2018gender identity\u2019 as the criteria for being a man or being a woman. \u2018Gender identity\u2019 ideology teaches children who don't conform to masculine or feminine stereotypes that their personalities are \u2018wrong\u2019 for their sex, and their bodies are then \u2018wrong\u2019 for their gender identity, The number of children and young people who now believe they are really the opposite sex is reflected in the unprecedented recent trend in referrals to the Tavistock Gender Identity Development Service. Boys and girls should be able to wear what they like and have whatever interests they choose without adult interpretation through the lens of a non-scientific, ideological belief that human beings are born with an innate sense of being male or female, which is inevitably based on sex stereotypes. In school, acceptance of a boy who likes to play with dolls as a gir is no acceptance at al Acceptance of a lesbian adolescent girl as a straight boy is no acceptance at all. This approach only serves to reinforce restrictive and harmful stereotypes. \u2018Affirmation\u2019 is not kind, it affirms to a child that they are the wrong sex and encourages a child's belief that their body needs medically changing. Medical intervention can only ever effect cosmetic change; the child's sex remains the same. We advocate for the rights of lesbian and gay young people to grow up as lesbian or gay. We advocate for the rights of autistic children and those with mental health problems or background trauma to receive proper therapeutic care, not a \u2018diagnosis\u2019 that they are really the opposite sex. All children and young people deserve treatment based on clinical evidence, not ideology. In schools all children deserve to be taught science-based facts, not ideology disguised as \u2018fact\u2019. All children have the right to privacy from the opposite sex in toilets and changing- rooms. Policy in schools must always put safeguarding first and schools should not use resources that confuse children about sex. Children should not be coerced into expressing a belief in \u2018gender identity\u2019 through the threat that not to do so is \u2018unkind\u2019 or \u2018transphobic\u2019. On this site you will find information and research, resources for parents and teachers and legal information. Please have a look around the site and sign up to our blog for updates on current news stories and developments. We have worked tirelessly for years to facilitate debate about an issue which we feel should be openly and publicly discussed. Please join us. We receive no funding from any organisations, charities or government, we depend entirely on individual donations from our supporters. Our continued development relies on your kind donations. Please consider setting up a monthly donation, or you can make a one-off donation by credit card, Paypal or through your bank. Thank you for whatever donation you are able to make. the funding page Subscribe To Blog Via Email Recent Posts PRIVACY POLICY Transgender Trend takes your privacy seriously; your email address is stored securely. We do not share this list with anyone else. You may unsubscribe at anytime by CHET responding tothe link at the end of blog posts. May 28, 2026 ((susscrise ) May 11, 2026 Join 2,296 other subscribers.", "ocr_text_len": 6062}
