{"_key": "wjctnprjacksonville", "source_key": "wjctnprjacksonville", "filename": "WJCT_-_NPR_-_Jacksonville.png", "image_file": "WJCT_-_NPR_-_Jacksonville.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.2258, "s008_neutral_headlines": 2.216, "s010_scare_quotes": 2.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 1.0, "s085_standard_sections": 6.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 14.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00364, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.7831, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.4619, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00133, "small_face_count": 12.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0647, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.2861, "content_column_count": "2", "side_margin_frac": 0.084, "header_band_height_frac": 0.012, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 1.9092, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0062, "page_scroll_length": "very_long", "nav_item_count": 33.0, "footer_link_count": 267.0, "cta_button_count": 2.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 2.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 1.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 11.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 3.75, "headline_size_variance": 0.3157, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 27.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0294, "number_token_frac": 0.0596, "city_or_county_in_name": 1.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.542, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.4878, "lx_timestamp_per100": 2.439, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0903, "lx_health_scare_per100": 1.084, "lx_question_style_per100": 2.8004, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.1807, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.542, "lx_local_civic_per100": 2.168}, "ocr_text": "WJCT & News SHOWS & PODCASTS - NEWS ~ ABOUT Fresh Air Q__\u2014 @ Donate Now >) \u00a9 [PaAlstcam Today's Radio Schedule Earlier Today \u00ab 8:00 pm. First Coast Connect S00 pm. (> onarnow ) BBS NewsHour 10:00 p.m. Fresh Air Later Today View Weekly Schedule firsteagast connect Dive into the heart of Northeast Florida with First Coast Connect . This captivating weekday call-in program brings you face-to-face with the region's movers and shakers, from community leaders and local artists to standout event planners. Engage in vibrant discussions and delve into the week's hottest topics with our exciting Friday Roundtable, featuring a dynamic mix of local media personalities and civic luminaries. Tune in, connect and become part of the community conversation. Weekdays live at 9 a.m.; Rebroadcast at 8 p.m. Call us: 1 (904) 549-2937 (Note: This line is only active during the program, 9-10 am) Email firstcoastconnect@wjct.org Twitter: Tag @FCConair on Twitter Facebook: Comment on facebook.com/FCConair First Coast Connect A House Call from Dr. Joe Thour ago From a spike in alcohol use during pregnancy to what we're learning from hantavirus and Ebola outbreaks, we discuss the latest medical headlines. > LISTEN - St00 = First Coast Connect First Coast Connect First Coast Connect First Coast Week in Review May 29, 2026 > LISTEN - Stoo ing medical research une 2,2026 LISTEN - Stoo Breaking down the budget une 1, 2026 > LISTEN \u00ab st00 What\u2019s HEALTH GOT TO DO WITH! What's Health Got to Do with It? is an engaging weekly talk show hosted by Dr. Joe Sirven, a renowned physician and medical journalist. The show navigates the intricacies of the healthcare system, offering insight into treatment access, insurance coverage, and maintaining good health. Each episode, centered around a specific topic, dives into compelling healthcare stories and explores solutions for healthcare challenges. The program encourages active listener participation, fostering a community that is locally-focused and solution-driven on healthcare issues. Saturdays at 4 p.m. and Sundays at 9 p.m. (e What's Health Got to Do with It? Protection medicine; tick bites; covert consciousness May 30, 2026 From psychedelic depression treatments to an uptick in tick bites, our health experts unpack the month's biggest medical headlines. What's Health Got to Do with It? What's Health Got to Do with It? What's Health Got to Do with It? Care beyond the The heart and brain Motherhood battlefield connection unscripted May 23, 2026 May 16, 2026 May 8, 2026 > LISTEN - 55:00 > USTEN - S100 > LISTEN - 55:00 (AML ny = THE FLORIDA ROUNDUP P MLZLZ Hear what Florida is talking about each week with newsmakers and journalists discussing issues defining the Sunshine State, hosted by Tom Hudson. This show is co-produced by WLRN in Miami and WUSF in Tampa, Ways To Connect Call us: (05) 995-1800 rag @FloridaRoundup Hurricane season begins, DeSantis\u2019 property tax plan, living shorelines and more May 29, 2026 This week on The Florida Roundup, we looked at the official federal forecast for the Atlantic hurricane season that begins June 1 with meteorologist John Morales (00:00). Then we spoke about emergency response and preparedness with former FEMA administrator Craig Fugate (13:40). We also spoke with the mayors of Daytona Beach Shores and Cedar Key to talk about how their coastal communities are preparing for this year\u2019s storm season (2126). Plus, Your Florida reporter Meghan Bowman joined us to discuss Gov. Ron DeSantis\u2019 property tax plan and the new state budget (28:52). And later, we learned about how more municipalities and private homeowners in the Tampa Bay region are embracing a natural alternative to cement seawalls (37:12) and other environmental news (45:54) Senior homes lack state oversight, redistricting in Florida and Texas, and more April17,2026 Political boundaries, campus free speech and weekly news briefing April 24, 2026 High gas prices and affordability, property tax ballot push, and environmental news Apri, 2026 Latest Local Newscast from 'WICT News 89.9 Latest National Newscast from NPR News LOCALIiQ Discover Jacksonville like never before with Jacksonville Today, a nonprofit local digital journalism service from WICT Public Media, With a daily five-minute read, stay updated on the city's top news, events, and engaging opinion pieces. Beyond news, it's your doorway to actively participate in the community. Get ready to experience Jacksonville, one email atatime. St. Johns County sheriff seeks budget increase to raise deputies\u2019 pay City Council delays bill t to put mil school tax renewal on November ( ballot Property tax overhaul headed to ballot; see how your legislators voted Supra Revolving Sushi Bar prepares to replace Hooters in Tinseltown Jax Beach bars and restaurants can expand ia capacity on Jaguars Sees game days npr NPR News is your go-to destination for reliable national news, delivering comprehensive reporting, thoughtful analysis, and engaging storytelling. With a commitment to accuracy and balanced coverage, NPR News keeps you informed about the latest national happenings, offering insights and perspectives that go beyond surface-level news National News Greetings from Porto, whose lanes are lined with colorful textiles Esme Nicholson, 2 hours ago Linen scarves, cotton aprons and dishtowels adorn the entrances to souvenir shops, many of which are run by Bangladeshis whose home country shares Portugal's rich tradition of textile manufacturing. National News Takeaways from lowa's primaries. And, DOJ nixes Trump's \u2018ant weaponization\u2019 fund Brittney Melton, 4 hours ago Polls have now closed in six states that held primary elections yesterday. Here are the key takeaways. And, the Justice Department has scrapped plans for Trump's \u201canti-weaponization\u201d fund, > USTEN \u00ab 15 National News President Trump seeks control of science funding Katia Riddle, S hours ago The White House Office of Management, and Budget is moving to take more control of billions of dollars in federal grants. Critics say the proposed change would jeopardize the integrity of US. National News Ukrainian drones st Petersburg oil terminal ahead of Putin visit The Associated Press, 6 hours ago Ukrainian drones struck an oil terminal in St.Petersburg and set it ablaze, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said, as the city hosted an annual economic forum promoted by President Putin. National News We finally know enough about how the brain breaks to focus on fixing it, experts say on Hamilton, 7 hours ago The Allen Institute in Seattle says scientists have now learned enough about how the brain works to start fixing it when it breaks, National News \"They went through my vocal cords': Barry Manilow recovers after lung cancer surgery Phil Harrell, 7 hours ago Nearly 83, Barry Manilow is recovering from cancer, preparing for a series of concerts, and releasing his first album of new songs in nearly 15 years, What a Time.", "ocr_text_len": 6947}
