{"_key": "wolfstreet", "source_key": "wolfstreet", "filename": "Wolf_Street.png", "image_file": "Wolf_Street.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.1712, "s008_neutral_headlines": 0.2536, "s010_scare_quotes": 3.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 2.0, "s085_standard_sections": 2.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 1.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.0, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.3026, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.0, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.0, "small_face_count": 0.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0745, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.3592, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.11, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0308, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "blue", "accent_color_count": 0.6885, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.003, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 92.0, "footer_link_count": 107.0, "cta_button_count": 1.0, "newsletter_box_count": 3.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 3.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 8.778, "headline_size_variance": 0.1688, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 24.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0206, "number_token_frac": 0.1083, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 1.2842, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0171, "lx_timestamp_per100": 2.0548, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 1.7123, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0, "lx_market_money_per100": 4.7089, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.2568}, "ocr_text": "Discover more Mortgage Lenders Mortgages Financial Newsletter Subscription WOLF STREET The Stories behind Business, Fi |= mortgage Auto Loan Comparison Economic Forecasts \u00a9 Market Research Reports Hom Wolf Richt Donat Housing Bubt Contact IMPLODED STOCKS Brick & Mortar Drunken Sailors And More Data Showing a Weirdly Decent Labor Market \u2018by Wolf Richter \u00abJun 2, 2026 + 32 Comments But this dynamic makes it harder for young people to find a job. As Prices Spike, Manufacturing Expands at Fastest Rate in 4 Years, Orders Surge, Supplier Deliveries Slow bby Wolf Richter \u00abJun 1, 2028 +15 Comments \u2018Amid improved automation and efficiencies, production rises, but employment doesn't, or only a litte. US Government Sold $742 billion of Treasury Securities last Week. T-bill Yields now Below Surging Inflation. Bond Market Bets on Rate Hikes \u2018Commenting ECON RUMBLINGS Food Inflation in America by Product: It Boils down to a Sharp Acceleration on Top of Already Very High Prices by Wolt Richter \u00ab May 18, 2028 Ground beet, steak, chicken, fruit & veggies, coffee, dairy, eggs, other foods, and total The Most Splendid Housing Bubbles in \u2018America: Price Drops & Gains in 33 Big Expensive Cities, April 2026 bby Wolt Richter\u00bb May 16, 2026 Europe jome prices fell year-over-year in 25 ofthe 33 bi federal Reser Dy Wo tar May 31,2028 1 Comment taper ces Apr bunch at mules, \u2018The Fed is behind the curve, the bond market is saying, and i's going to hike led by Oakland & Austin, down by 26% from 2022 \u2018Housing Bubble 2 belatedly starting later this year, whether it wants to oF not. Two Set new highs. Inflation & Devaluation Japan obs \u2018The Magnitude of the Numbers Is just Mindboggling: 12 U.S. Here Come the HELOCs: Mortgages, Mae Companies, $30 Trillion Housing-Debt-to-Income-Ratio, Serious \u2018Mads & Companies by Wolf Richter * May 28, 2028 + 121 Comments Delinquencies, and Foreclosures in Q1 Ol Gas, Power But if they pop: There are only so many trillions that can vanish from 2026 tors May 14,2006 Retail portfolios before it triggers a recession, by Wot Richter + May \u201cTrucks & Cars Mortgage balances barely ticked up, but HELOCS me As soared, PCE Inflation Surges Further Away from Fed's Target, now Nearly Double the Fed\u2019s Target, and 5+ Years above Target by Wolf Richter + May 28, 2028 +'160 Comments Trend reversal started a year ago. Services inflation stuck at high rate for a year. Now prices of food, energy, computers & software (inflationary Al boom), and gold jewelry (gold price spike) all surged. Micron, the WTF Al Mania Chart of the Year by Wolt Richter May 27, 2026 + 105 Comments The stock has a history of collapsing by 50% to 98% after every spike, regularly falling below its Dotcom Bubble high. But this time is different? \u2018Oh Dear, Condo Prices already Dropped by 15% to 33% in 24 Bigger Markets, Some Back to Where They'd Been 20 Years Ago bby Wolf Richtor\u00ab May 25, 2028 \u00ab 90 Comments Plus, in another 44 bigger cities, condo prices dropped by 7% to 14% so far, as the mindboggling Condo Bubble comes unglued. 10-Year TIPS v. 10-Year Treasury Securities: Bond Market Has Long Been Delusional about Actual CPI Inflation \u2018by Wolf Richter \u00ab May 26, 2026 74 Comments There's no indication the bond market is better now in figuring future inflation; its expectation of 2.4% annual CPI over 10 years seems woefully low. Prices of Single-Family Homes already Down 10% to 26% in these 15 Bigger Cities: Every Market is Different by Wolf Richter \u00ab May 22, 2026 \u00bb \u00a79 Comments \u2018San Francisco & Portland came off the list. Fort Worth & Aurora (CO) come on the lst. Credit Card Delinquencies, Balances, Debt-to-Income, Credit Limits, and Collections in Q1 2026: Americans and their Revolving Credit by Wolf Richter \u00ab May 20, 2026 42 Comments The free-money hangover is getting worked off. Bond Bloodbath Worsens on Inflation, Lax Fed, and Flood of New Debt. Mortgage Rates hit 6.75% by Wolf Richter + May 20, 2028 +217 Comments, Usly trifecta that spooks the bond market. To soothe bond yields and mortgage rates, the Fed needs to hike, not \u201clook through\" inflation. \u2018Auto Loan Balances, Debt-to-Income Ratio, and Delinquencies of \u2018Subprime & Prime Auto Loans in Q1 2026. How Bad Is it? bby Wolf Richter + May 19, 2028 67 Comments Several subprime-specialized dealer-lender chains collapsed, and shares of \u2018America's Auto Mart imploded. Subprime lending is not for the squeamish. But it\u2019s only a small part of auto finance. Food Inflation in America by Product: It Boils down to a Sharp Acceleration on Top of Already Very High Prices by Wolf Richter\u00bb May 18,2026 104 Comments Ground beet, steak, chicken, fruit & veggies, coffee, dairy, eggs, other foods, and total. The Most Splendid Housing Bubbles in America: Price Drops & Gains in 33 Big Expensive Cities, April 2026 bby Wolf Richter May 16, 2026 + 67 Comments Home prices fell year-over-year in 25 of the 33 big expensive cities in April, a bunch set multi-year lows, led by Oakland & Austin, down by 26% from 2022. Two set new highs. US Government Sold $691 Billion of Treasury Securities this Week, 10-Year Yield Spikes to 4.6%, 30-Year Yield to 5.12% as 2nd Wave of Inflation Takes Off by Wolt Richter \u00ab May 15, 2026 + 82 Comments The Fed is \u201cbehind the curve,\u201d and the bond market is getting very nervous. Here Come the HELOCs: Mortgages, Housing-Debt-to-Income- Ratio, Serious Delinquencies, and Foreclosures in Q1 2026 by Wolf Richtor+ May 14, 2028 - 76 Comments Mortgage balances barely ticked up, but HELOCs soared. Producer Price Inflation Explodes as the Services PPI Blows Out on Top of the Energy Price Spike by Wolf Richter + May 13, 2026 \u00ab121 Comments, This is a massive amount of inflation that companies are passing on to each \u2018other through much of the economy. Household Debts, Debt-to-Income Ratio, Serious Delinquencies, Foreclosures, Collections & Bankruptcies in Q1 2026 bby Wolf Richter \u00ab May 12, 2026 +55 Comments \u2018Americans and their Debts: Student loans that suddenly have to be repaid \u2018again fueled overall delinquency rates. CPI Inflation Blows Past Fed Rates as Core Services, Gasoline, Electricity, and Food Spike. Fed's \u201cReal\u201d Rates Are now Negative by Wolf Richter \u00ab May 12, 2026 +118 Comments The Bureau of Labor Statistics finally corrected part of the CPI distortions in September, October, and November. \u2018Supply of Existing Single-Family Homes Rises to Highest in 10 Years, Condo Supply Highest since 2012, Sales in Deepfreeze bby Wolf Richter \u00ab May 11, 2026 \u00ab 75 Comments April was another bad dud for spring selling season as supply continued to pile up. Producer Price Inflation Explodes as the Services PPI Blows Out on Top of the Energy Price Spike by Wol Richter\u00bb May 13, 2026 Tis isa massive amount of inflation that companies are passing on to each ather through much of the economy. SUBSCRIBE TO WOLF STREET Enter your email address to receive notifications of \u2018new posts by email Email Address SS fed: wolstreet.com/feed Copyright \u00a92011 -2026 Wot treet Corp. All ights Reserved, See our Privacy Pliy & Opt-Out Preferences.", "ocr_text_len": 7036}
{"_key": "witherspooninstitute", "source_key": "witherspooninstitute", "filename": "Witherspoon_Institute.png", "image_file": "Witherspoon_Institute.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.2838, "s008_neutral_headlines": 0.834, "s010_scare_quotes": 7.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 0.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0, "s078_absolutist_framing": 1.0, "s085_standard_sections": 6.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 24.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.02758, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.8388, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.0, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.00183, "small_face_count": 1.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0788, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.3469, "content_column_count": "1", "side_margin_frac": 0.04, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0064, "logo_centered": 0.0, "accent_hue": "orange", "accent_color_count": 2.9907, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0834, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 29.0, "footer_link_count": 201.0, "cta_button_count": 2.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 0.0, "search_box_present": 0.0, "weather_widget_present": 0.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 7.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 3.667, "headline_size_variance": 0.2858, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 21.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0856, "number_token_frac": 0.039, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.8515, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.0, "lx_timestamp_per100": 1.9868, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.0, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 3.8789, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.0946, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.0, "lx_local_civic_per100": 1.1353}, "ocr_text": "\u2018THE HUMAN PERSON '\u00ae EDUCATION & CULTURE SEXUALITY & FAMILY ABOUT \u00a5 FEATURED ESSAY CONTEST Public Discourse POLITICS & LAW The Bookshelf: The 2026 Public Discourse Summer Reading List By The Editors We use cookies on our website to give you the most relevant experience by remembering your preferences and repeat visits. By clicking \u201cAccept All\", you consent to the use of ALL the cookies. However, you may visit \"Cookie Settings\" to provide a controlled ae a Bl EDUCATION & CULTURE consent, THE HUMAN PERSON. Al, Magnifica Humanitas, and the Law of the Golem \u2018The Imago Dei as History: A Review of Tomer Persico\u2019s In Wt POLITICS & LAW EVENTS EDUCATION & CULTURE Written Constitutions, Judicial Review, and the BROWSE v SUBSCRIBE SUBMIT SUPPORT BUSINESS & ECONOMICS = Q CCookieSettings | Accept All Ml EDUCATION & CULTURE, POLITICS & LAW The Forgotten Foundations of Constitutional Law By Seth C. Oranburg God's Image Limits of Constitutional Dy Nicholas Aronay By Thomas Holman Hope June 11,2026 June 8, 2026 June 10,2026 By Nicholas Aror June 9, 2026 VIEW MORE ARTICLES Keep up with the conversation! Subscribe to Public Discourse today. SUBSCRIE Interviews October 16,2025 | EDUCATION & CULTURE Here's Why Church and State Must Remain Separate: A Q&A with Hunter Baker By Micah Watson and Hunter Baker | continue to believe that our best path forward is to respect one another and to avoid the constant temptation to engage in emotional and political manipulation from the left and right. VIEW MORE INTERVIEWS Book Reviews June 2, 2026 | EDUCATION & CULTURE amilton, Jefferson, and the Fight for Power in America By David Lewis Schaefe Taken as a whole, Rosen's book offers a learned and sober account of the relevance of Hamilton's and Jefferson's principles to America\u2019s past, present, and possible future, \u2018VIEW MORE BOOK REVIEWS. Long Reads March 31, 2026 EDUCATION & CULTURE \u2018What Does Academic Freedom Look Like at a Catholic University? By Santiago Schnel When a university advertises Catholic identity, itis making a promise to students and families: that faith and reason will be engaged seriously, that moral questions will be treated as real, that the human. person's complexity will not be assumed away. \u2018VIEW MORE LONG READS ESSAY SERIES Western Parenting aa September 30, 2025 | THE HUMAN PERSON A Free and Flourishing Society Recognizes Our Dependence: A Q&A with Leah Libresco Sargeant \u2018The whole world is God's creation, an expression of his love. The truth about ourselves as dependent creatures who he loves, whom he sent his Son to redeem, is out there for us. We can blind ourselves to it, we can ignore it, but i's very loud. And the more we help each other see it, the happier we will ultimately be. May 19, 2026 | W EDUCATION & CULTURE Games Gone Wild: How Metrics and Gamification Distort Reality and Capture Values By Joshua Pauling Games might just be one way to shake us free from the shackles of metrics and reclaim the human goods that deserve much more than a number. March 26, 2026 Edgardo Mortara Should Not Have Been Taken from His Parents EDUCATION & CULTURE By Nathaniel Peters \u2018An in-depth review of Matthew Tapie's The Mortara Case and Thomas Aquinas's Defense of Jewish Parental Authority How the West Really Lost Dating adt and Elizabeth Lyon Hall By Mary Ebel We are very different people from those who came before us, because of our deficits in social learning, OWA craig a doubt the origin, au then tic ity muineness + quality lent of the authenti- writer (of @ book, May 13,2026 | i THE HUMAN PERSON Authenticity, RIP: Lionel Trilling Revisited By Michael C. Behrent \u2018Authenticity was a cultural force that risked destroying culture itself. n the early twenty-first century, the time has perhaps come to rediscover it February 26, 2026 WR SEXUALITY & FAMILY, THE HUMAN PERSON A Look Inside the Endometriosis Epidemic Can We Restore Hope in Women's Healthcare? November 23, 2025 m SEXUALITY & FAMILY The Parental Arms Race Needs to End By Patrick T. Br In a world where \u201csuccess\u201d is increasingly understood as zero-sum, we might have some empathy for today's parents who are worried they are letting their kids down if they are not setting them up to succeed, even if that comes at a collective cost. \u2018VIEW ALL IN THIS SERIES Newsletters November 9, 2025 Babies, Made to Order: The New York Times Sounds the Reproductive Technology Alarm By Glenn T. Stanton If Siddiqui's new moral imperative for artifical, disembodied procreation to ensure perfectly healthy babies becomes the norm, have we not lost something truly beautiful and human, the link between physical sexual communion and procreation? November 6, 2025 Intensive Parenting Is (Probably) Incompatible with Having Many Kids. By Ivana Greco Is it possible to be considered a good parent today if your top priority is not perfecting your children, but rather simply being their \u201csafe place\u2019? | don't know the answer, but it seems to me that being a warm and loving parent that children feel safe with is both a worthy and challenging goal. | have often reflected that many of my worst parenting mistakes happened when I tried to convince my kids to be other than the people they are. November 30, 2024 From the Editor\u2019s Desk: Public Discourse\u2019s Monthly Roundup, November 2024 Infiltrating the culture with countercultural thinking about the value of life\u2014and its connection to true, authentic gratitude\u2014is not a religious or political matter, and no ideological camp has the upper hand in the argument. We need civil dialogue across political lines, and that\u2019s what we seek to do, VIEW MORE PAST NEWSLETTERS November 2, 2024 From the Editor's Desk: Public Discourse\u2019s Monthly Roundup, October 2024 By RJ. Snel substance as well. And our pages were full of substance this month, as every month, October 5, 2024 From the Editor\u2019s Desk: Public Discourse\u2019s Monthly Roundup, September 2024 By Matthew X, Wilson A crucial aspect of Public Discourse's mission is to be a beacon of light and a forum for serious, rigorous, and truth-seeking discourse even when temptations toward despair, radicalization, and provocative polemics abound. At PD, we charitably examine and challenge ideas and arguments\u2014we don't attack or demonize people, and we don't serve any worldview, party, or ideology besides the cause of truth. \u00ab THE WITHERSPOON INSTITUTE Public Discourse CD vox Monthly newsletters now on S Ovyaqan Public Discourse \u00a9 2026 | All Rights Reserved", "ocr_text_len": 6450}
