{"_key": "worldaffairsblog", "source_key": "worldaffairsblog", "filename": "World_Affairs_Blog.png", "image_file": "World_Affairs_Blog.png", "ok": true, "feature_schema": "nollm_raw12_v3_lx9_v8", "nollm_features": {"s004_sensational_verbs": 0.3584, "s008_neutral_headlines": 0.4566, "s010_scare_quotes": 18.0, "s023_no_owner_identified": 0.0, "s072_loaded_category_tags": 1.0, "s076_conspiracy_tropes": 0.0512, "s078_absolutist_framing": 3.0, "s085_standard_sections": 4.0, "s097_suspicious_url": 0.0, "story_block_count": 1.0, "hero_image_area_frac": 0.00116, "thumbnail_size_uniformity": 0.7998, "s060_templated_imagery": 0.0, "largest_face_area_frac": 0.0, "small_face_count": 0.0, "s066_cluttered_blog_look": 0.0505, "inter_story_whitespace_frac": 0.5283, "content_column_count": "3plus", "side_margin_frac": 0.312, "header_band_height_frac": 0.0468, "logo_centered": 1.0, "accent_hue": "none", "accent_color_count": 0.0, "background_brightness": "white", "s067_alarmist_colors": 0.0018, "page_scroll_length": "medium", "nav_item_count": 6.0, "footer_link_count": 24.0, "cta_button_count": 0.0, "newsletter_box_count": 0.0, "social_icon_count": 1.0, "search_box_present": 1.0, "weather_widget_present": 1.0, "account_button_present": 0.0, "category_badge_count": 0.0, "mean_headline_word_count": 7.222, "headline_size_variance": 0.3134, "page_text_density": "dense", "timestamp_count": 7.0, "allcaps_token_frac": 0.0155, "number_token_frac": 0.0185, "city_or_county_in_name": 0.0, "lx_ideology_identity_per100": 0.768, "lx_attribution_per100": 0.2355, "lx_timestamp_per100": 0.3584, "lx_loaded_outgroup_per100": 0.1024, "lx_health_scare_per100": 0.0, "lx_question_style_per100": 4.4035, "lx_culture_war_per100": 0.1024, "lx_market_money_per100": 0.0512, "lx_local_civic_per100": 0.7168}, "ocr_text": "WORLD AFFAIRS search MOST VIEWED POSTS _ UIGHUR CARD TO BREAK UP CHINA \u2014 REPUBLISHED \u2018There was an amazing article written in 1997 that sheds light into the American/Western attacks \u2018on China using Uyghurs as geopolitical pawns. The article is in PDF format, which is hard to read So, Lam summarizing the article and copy/pasting the entire article. The orginal article appeared \u2018on LaRouche Pub's EIR magazine, Here is the link \u2018Once you understand history, the present makes sense, American/British imperialism and thelr ruthless manipulations playbook never change. summary RECENT POSTS Uighur Card to break Up China Republished + 1997 article: \u201cUyghur Card to Break Up China\u201d by Joseph rewda + The West funded radical Uyghurs who wanted to blow up \u201cNew Silk Roa\u00e9 rainsie \u2018American Empire is Collapsing in Xinjian nang Real Time + \u201cUyghur Liber Jon Front\u201d => offices in US/UK + \u201cTurkestan\u201d & \"Uyghur genocide\u201d were talking points in 1994 + \"Chinese Chechnya\u201d \u2014 term used by US state Dept! + Terrorist bombings were already happening in China in 1990s, thanks to Uyghur separatists, who claimed responsibility Some excerpts from the article 1. Since 1992, Xinjiang has acquired global strategic significance, as the route of the Eurasian Continental Bridge (which later came to be known as One Belt One Road or Belt and Road Initiative) 2. Sir Wiliam Peters, a former British deputy high commissioner in Bombay and career Intelligence specialist, who Is today chairman of the Tibet Society and board member of the Royal Society of Aslan Affairs, the primary British intelligence outfit targeting China 3. In 1994, Lord Avebury sent an open letter to the British Foreign Office demanding that it \u2018save the peoples of Eastern Turkestan,\" who were \u201cfaced with national extinction\u201d 4. In an interview with Voice of America on Feb.14, the retired career State Department offical, now with Kissinger at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, predicted that Xinjang could become a \u201cChinese Chechnya. 5. \"The Chinese are building railroads, but the people are opposing the railroad, and will destroy the railroad. This Is just like the American movies on the history of California, What the Indians di, in fighting the railroads, is what we will do\u201d \u2014 leader of the U.S. branch of the Uighur Liberation Front, Gulamettin Pahta. 6. In October 1994, Vighur liberationist leader Erkin Alptekin addressed a conference in New York City of the \u201cAllied Committe of the Peoples of Eastern Turkestan, Inner Mongolia Tibet. (Okay, now the entire atc: \u2018Uighur card\u2019 used to break up China by Joseph Brewda Since February, the Xinjiang Autonomous Region of north west China has been the target of series of disturbances and bombings, caried out-by their own claims-by \u201cUighur\u201d separatist \u2018groups attempting to split the region from China. What is at stake in Xinjiang isa project of strategic importance: the Second Euro-Asian Continental Bridge, the \u201cnew Si Road\u201d China-to- West Asia-and-Europe rail lie which opened in 1992. Ths project, atthe core of all current projects to develop the Eurasian landmass, was only finally completed, a century after the first Europe-to-Asia line was built in Russia, when the connection between the Chinese ral system and that of Kazakhstan in Central Asia was finished Xinjiang is being targeted by foreign-steered and foreign-headquartered separatist movements Claiming to represent the Turkic-language-speaking Uighur \u201cpeople\u201d of Xinjiang. Although in 1949, Xinjiang\u2019s population was approximately 95% Uighur, today, about half of the 16 milion population are of Chinese origin. Xinjiang also has China's largest deposits of oll and natural gas, uranium, gold, and other raw materials, ince 1992, Xinjiang has acquired global strategic significance, asthe route ofthe Continental Bridge. The Chinese government is now building two more branches of the \u201cLand-Bridge\u201d:a second connection to Kazakhstan, and the first rail line to the city of Kashi, the Chinese terminus ofthe Pakistan-China Karakoram Highway. The separatists make no bones about the fact, that these strategic ralllines are ther target. The leader of the U.S. branch of the Uighur Liberation Front, Gulamettin Pahta, told EIR on March 11 that the \"Continental Bridge\u201d isa Chinese \u201cimperialist\u201d plot that must be blocked. \u201cThey are bullding railroads, but the people are opposing the railroad, and will destroy the railroad. This is, just like the American movies on the history of California, What the Indians did, infighting the railroads, is what we wil do. The same thing is happening. Every train coming into eastern Turkestan is bringing in Chinese. This must be stopped,\u201d Pahta said Just how \u201csuccessful\u201d the separatists ae infighting the ralroads, is questionable. Western press \u2018outlets, in an effort to inflame the situation, have repeatedly given all kinds of figures for \u2018casualties in disturbances in Xinjiang, and a bomb explosion in Bejing, numbers which Chinese accounts have not confirmed. However, spokesmen for the Uighur Liberation Party and the Eastern Turkestan Liberation Organization have claimed credit for the violence. Moreover, efforts by the British to inflame relations between China and the Central Asian Republics, by staging some of their East Turkistan\u2019 separatist actions out of states bordering on CChina, have also been dealt a setback President Nursultan Nazarbayev of Kazakhstan, fresh from discussions in Beijing about ral and \u2018energy cooperation with China, held a Feb. 22 press conference, in which he denounced the idea (of secessionism. \u201cSo-called minorities le in Inner Mongolia, Xinjiang, Tibet, the south, and in \u2018other regions of China. Their aspiration for self-determination is understandable. However, we \u2018amin no way welcome the idea of separatism. There are 6,000 peoples and ethnic groups in the world all of them were to decide to declare sovereignty one day, then numerous helpless, dwarfish countees would emerge on the planet, along with the existing powerful countries that are striving for development and prosperity, and this would mean chaos, permanent wars, and endless conflicts Gulamettin Pahtais a member of an international network of Uighur liberationist groups deployed by the British and Dutch monarchies\u2019 Unrepresented Nations and Peoples Organization (UNPO), the British Royal Society of Asian Affairs, and Lord Avebury\u2019s House of Lords human rights rmercenaries.The UNPO has trained the Uighur liberationists in \u201cdiplomatic skills\" atthe Australian National University, according to Its lterature, through grants provided by the Dutch Foreign Ministry After World War Il, the Uighur separatists were led by Isa Yusuf Alptekin, who led a revolt in Xinjang in 1945. Today, the leadership of the network has passed to his son, Erkin Alptekin, who is also chairman of the UNPO. \u201cThe British command structure In addition to the Anglo-Dutch UNPO, which has targeted much of Siberia, as well as large sections of Central Asia and western China for break-up into ethnically divided mini states, IR has identified a complex of largely London-head quartered intelligence fronts, all pushing the destabilization of China \u2018One of the most important ritish case officers forthe Uighur independence movement is Sir William Peters, a former British deputy high commissioner in Bombay and career intelligence specialist, who is today chairman of the Tibet Society and board member of the Royal Society of \u2018Asian Affairs, the primary British intelligence outfit targeting China. In 1991, he wrote an \u2018optimistic forecast of Uighur and Tibetan rebellion, after a tour of Xinjiang, in the society's Journal, Asan Affairs: \u201cTo the south and east [of Xnjiangylies Tibet Stories ofthe Tibetan resistance filter through ta Kashgar [Kashi] and its neighbors. To the northeast, Uighurs see the moves toward multpolarity in Outer Mongolia and hear about unrest among Mongols in Inner Mongolia. On the western side there is no telling what direction semi-independent republics in Kazakhstan, Tajikstan, Kyrayzia, and Uzbekistan might move vis-a-vis China If there is any truth inthe story of miltary help from Kyrgyz across the border for their fellow tribesmen in Xinjiang. this thought will be al the stronger. A few Uighurs have heard of the Joint Committee for the Manchu, Mongol, East \u2018Turkmen, and Tibetan Peoples and are particularly anxious to obtain by whatever means possible the Committee's publication One Voice. They have some links with Isa Alptekin. leader ofthe Turkestan Liberation Movement. tis noteworthy that Alptekin's son Erkin Alptekin took an active art in the International Convention on Tibet in London from 6 to 8 July [1990 \u201cThe conjunction of revived minority discontent on both national and religious grounds, of improved access across the frontier to fellow tribesmen, of major politcal change in neighboring Countries, and ofthe sustained world reaction against genocide, colonialism, and apartheid, \u2018creates a situation in Central Asia in which radial change is just possible. The present campaign to arouse world opinion on the subject of genocide, colonialism, and apartheld in China could be the lever which pres out from a Politburo due for change radical concessions in areas such as Xinjiang and Tibet \u201cThe House of Lords and Foreign Office speak Lord Avebury, chairman of the British Parliamentary Human Rights Group, is another controller of| the separatists. In 1994, Lord Avebury sent an open letter tothe British Foreign Office demanding that it \"save the peoples of Eastern Turkestan,\u201d who were faced with national extinction.\u201d In 1995, Lord A vebury told EIR that he was pessimistic that Britain could be successful in defending the Uighurs and Tibetans from Chinese efforts to exterminate them, simply through human rights campaigns, implying that he favored more aggressive London involvement in the destabilization of Xinjiang. Lord Ennals a former British Foreign Secretary, was, until his recent death, another top patron of the Uighur and Tibetan independence movements. He was also a leader of the UNPO, Martin Ennals, Lord Enna!\u2019 s brother, controls Amnesty International, the British Foreign Office front which oversees international propaganda campaigns against China, over alleged suppression of the Uighurs and Tibetans. \u2018American \u2018cousins\u2019 weigh in \u2018Among the so-called \u201cAmericans\u201d who have joined the Anglo-Dutch drumbeat to destabilize the New Silk Road\u201d through secessionist violence in Xinjiang is one of Henry Kissinger\u2019 leading State Department proteges, Dr. Helmut Sonnenfeldt In an interview with Voice of America on Feb. 14 \u2018the retired career State Department official, ow wit Kissinger at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, predicted that Xinjiang could become a \u201cChinese Chechnya. Sonnenfeldtgloated, \u201cthink the Chinese have tried to observe very closely what happened in Chechnya in part because they may be conscious ofthe possiblity that something of that sort might arise in their own domain\u201d Sonnenfeldt cautioned that, should such an uprising gain steam, \u201cit needs to be dealt with harshly and rapidly.\u201d or else China will be forced to grant the region autonomy-precisely the British strategic plan Elsie Walker is another leading propagandist devoted to \u201crousing world opinion\u201d on Xinjiang. A cousin of former US. President Sir George Herbert Walker Bush, she heads the US.-based Asians for Democracy, which also mobilizes on behalf ofthe Tibetan cause. In October 1994, Uighue Nberationist leader Erkin Alptekin addressed a conference in New York Cty of the \u201cAllied Committee of the Peoples of Eastern Turkestan, Inner Mongolia, Tibet,\u201d organized by Walker's outfit In its official announcement ofthe conference, the Dalai Lama's so-called Tibetan government in-exile declared: \u201cThis conference is being organized to let the international public know that in the uncertainty, instability, and even turmoil in China, that may result from the death of strongman Deng Xiaoping, the struggle to regain the freedom ofthese three peoples (Tibetans, Uighurs, and Mongols] from communist China domination will be pursued relentlessly, \u2018According to both Chinese and foreign news accounts, on the day of Deng Xiaoping's funeral three bombings took place in Xinjiang. The proposed map of a China broken into pieces, which the separatists distributed atthe conference, leaves no doubt what their London masters are attempting = Chris Kanthan, Make a one-time donation Choose an amount $5.00 10.00 $20.00 Your contribution is appreciated Here's the link. Thanks! @ Facebook =X X \u00a9 Reds \u2014 Unkedin \u2018OLDER", "ocr_text_len": 12632}
